00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:51.070
other people feeling back on their heels.

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:53.610
When someone comes to you as a patient,

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:55.560
what are some of the
first things that you want

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:56.670
to know about them?

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:58.960
I mean, obviously you want
to know their blood pressure.

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:01.500
You want to know something
about their mental health

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:02.660
and family history.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:04.160
But in terms of hormone health,

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:06.500
what are the sorts of probe
questions that you ask

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:07.617
and what are you looking for?

00:11:07.617 --> 00:11:10.970
And I ask this because I'd
like people to be able to ask

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:13.060
some of these very same
questions for themselves.

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:17.670
- Yeah, so when you do a physical exam

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:20.500
and a history, you have
a lot of different parts.

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:22.100
You have your history of present illness

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:23.130
if they have a complaint,

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:25.600
maybe the patient
doesn't have a complaint.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:27.780
In that case, things
like their social history

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:30.770
and their family history
are extremely important,

00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:31.860
because that gives you

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:33.830
an insight into their genetics

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:36.400
and an insight into their hormone health.

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:39.220
So patients will tell
me, oh, I'm doin' okay,

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:42.240
but it helps to ask them,
well, how are you now?

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:43.073
Let's say the patient is 50.

00:11:43.073 --> 00:11:45.970
How are you now versus when you were 20,

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:47.920
and what has changed?

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:49.410
So I've gotten the question the lot,

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:52.580
how do you get your doctor
to order a better lab workup

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:55.710
or to even include your basic hormones?

00:11:55.710 --> 00:11:58.550
And there's no magic answer to that,

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:01.160
but what really helps is you tell them,

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:03.100
my energy is not as good as it used to be.

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:05.010
My focus is not as good as it used to be.

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:08.170
My athletic performance is
not as good as it used to be.

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:10.200
So you don't have to have a pathology

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:12.020
in order for a lab to be indicated.

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:14.540
You just have that pertinent symptom.

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:15.760
- I think that's going
to be really helpful,

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:17.500
because for many people,

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:18.930
the idea of getting a blood test to look

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:20.980
at their hormones just seems like such

00:12:20.980 --> 00:12:22.660
an enormous hurdle to get over,

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:24.923
and many doctors won't prescribe them.

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:28.860
And would you say that it's,

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:30.480
using the approach you just described,

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:34.460
that it's equally
effective for men and women

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:36.940
or do you find that, for
one reason or another,

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:39.740
that men and women have
different challenges

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:40.850
and advantages in trying

00:12:40.850 --> 00:12:43.223
to access their deeper hormone data?

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:45.780
- Yeah. It's slightly different.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:48.650
With women, there's a
lot more objective data.

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:51.940
So if they're having
menstrual irregularities or

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:55.610
if they're not havin' a period,

00:12:55.610 --> 00:12:57.550
if they're having too heavy of periods,

00:12:57.550 --> 00:12:59.223
then those are things that they talk about

00:12:59.223 --> 00:13:01.920
very frequently with their doctor.

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:03.480
Men are more hesitant.

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:06.900
So men really want to know
what their testosterone is,

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:08.420
but at the same time,

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:09.970
they really don't want
to tell their doctor

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:13.100
how their libido is or
how their energy is,

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:16.570
because it's almost like
they feel less masculine

00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:19.260
or they feel less like
a guy when they say that

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:21.730
even if they're just talking
to their doctor about it.

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:23.840
- Yeah, I think that that
raises a really important point,

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:26.600
which is that the whole
discussion around hormone health

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:28.930
is a bit of a barbed wire topic,

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:32.190
because in many ways when
we hear the word hormone,

00:13:32.190 --> 00:13:34.860
we think testosterone and estrogen,

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:37.920
we think notions of
masculinity and femininity.

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:40.140
And of course testosterone
and estrogen are present

00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:42.300
in all sexes, right?

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:44.100
All chromosomal backgrounds.

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:46.560
And just varying degrees in ratios.

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:49.840
But it also raises all these
issues about sexual health that

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:50.673
it's kind of interesting,

00:13:50.673 --> 00:13:52.490
'cause I'm surrounded by medical doctors

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:53.990
in my lab at Stanford.

00:13:53.990 --> 00:13:56.830
And the more physicians
that I surround myself with,

00:13:56.830 --> 00:14:00.330
the more open is the
discussion around sexual health

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:01.620
and reproductive health.

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:02.860
But in the general population,

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:06.310
I think some of these topics
are a little bit taboo

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:07.740
or against kind of barbed wire.

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:08.960
And so I think that people are seeking

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:10.650
a lot of this information on YouTube

00:14:10.650 --> 00:14:11.930
and through communities that may

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:15.290
or may not be very educated
about the actual biology.

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:16.883
So along those lines,

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:20.660
we could probably assume
that hormones are changing

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:22.560
across the lifespan, right?

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:25.483
Certainly from childhood
and puberty and onward.

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:28.050
If you would,

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:29.870
I'd love to just kind
of take a snapshot of

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:33.680
what you think everybody
should be thinking about

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:37.280
or doing to optimize their hormone health,

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:41.630
male or female, in,
let's say in their 20s.

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:44.490
And then maybe we could migrate
that to their 30s and 40s.

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:45.910
But before that,

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:47.730
could you just tell us what
everyone should be doing

00:14:47.730 --> 00:14:51.290
for their hormone health
from puberty onward?

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:55.260
- Yeah, the law of
diminishing returns applies.

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:57.950
So doing a little amount

00:14:57.950 --> 00:15:00.150
of what I call lifestyle interventions

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:04.240
over a long period of time is
going to be far more helpful

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:07.600
or efficacious than doing a
lot and then doing nothing

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:09.870
or doing a lot and then doing nothing.

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:12.790
So I talk about the big six pillars.

00:15:12.790 --> 00:15:16.630
The two strongest ones are
likely diet and exercise.

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:17.630
For hormone health,

00:15:17.630 --> 00:15:21.900
specifically resistance training
is particularly helpful.

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:26.900
For diet, caloric restriction
can be particularly helpful,

00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:30.280
especially with the epidemic
of metabolic syndrome

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:33.270
that is continuing to
on go in this country

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:36.000
and in developed countries in general.

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.010
So those are the two most powerful.

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:41.750
So number one and number
two are diet and exercise.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:44.290
For the last four, I have a
little bit of alliteration.

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:47.170
So there's stress and stress optimization.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:48.580
That has to do with cortisol,

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:50.330
that has to do with your mental health,

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:52.130
that has to do with societal health,

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:54.560
and collective health
of your family as well.

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:58.290
When you're a member of a family
or even a very close friend

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:03.390
trying to achieve optimal health
together is very important.

00:16:03.390 --> 00:16:05.100
It's the same thing
with nicotine cessation.

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:06.910
It's the same thing with
hormone optimization.

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:10.750
If you do it as a household
unit, it's far more helpful.

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:14.090
So after stress, you
have sleep optimization.

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:16.180
Sleep is extremely important,

00:16:16.180 --> 00:16:18.960
especially for mitochondrial
health as well.

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:20.350
And then you have sunlight,

00:16:20.350 --> 00:16:22.640
which encompasses
anything that's outdoors.

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:25.430
So you move more, you have cold exposure,

00:16:25.430 --> 00:16:27.770
you have heat exposure, that's sunlight.

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:29.700
And then last one is spirit.

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:33.520
So that's kind of the
body, mind, and soul.

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:36.820
If you have all the other five in,

00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:38.220
they're dialed in completely,

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:40.010
but you don't have your spiritual health,

00:16:40.010 --> 00:16:41.200
whatever you believe,

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:43.860
then that's going to
profoundly impact your body

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:44.693
and your mind as well.

00:16:44.693 --> 00:16:46.710
- Yeah, and we're definitely
going to touch into this notion

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:47.543
of spiritual health,

00:16:47.543 --> 00:16:50.740
because I think for some people
that might draw connotations

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:54.470
of certain things that may
or may not be accurate,

00:16:54.470 --> 00:16:57.090
but I know a number of
academic laboratories

00:16:57.090 --> 00:16:59.450
that are focused on this and a number of,

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:01.210
not just functional medicine clinics,

00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:04.570
but research clinics and
hospitals throughout the country

00:17:04.570 --> 00:17:06.930
that are achieving some
really interesting data,

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:09.470
not just in people that are quite sick,

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:11.140
but in healthy people who are trying

00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:12.270
to further optimize health.

00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:14.180
So we will definitely touch back to that.

00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:17.590
If you would be so kind
as to maybe give us

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:19.810
a little bit more detail about
some of these other areas.

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:22.850
So when people hear diet,
I immediately think, okay,

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:24.640
now we get into

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:28.990
the combat around vegan,
plant-based, carnivore, et cetera.

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:33.040
But I think that my general view of this

00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:35.150
is that most people
should probably be eating

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:37.070
as few highly processed foods,

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:38.610
highly palatable foods as possible,

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:39.750
which doesn't mean eating foods

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:40.820
that don't taste good, of course.

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:44.130
But what other sorts of
things do do you recommend

00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:45.243
in the realm of diet?

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:49.400
And then I also want to know
about caloric restriction,

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:51.890
because my understanding
is that a caloric surplus

00:17:51.890 --> 00:17:55.200
can actually support certain
hormones like testosterone.

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:57.420
So how does one combine
caloric restriction

00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:59.440
and still optimize hormones?

00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:02.730
But what would you say
is a really terrific way

00:18:02.730 --> 00:18:04.810
to think about an approached diet?

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:07.040
- Yeah. Diet should be an
individualized approach.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:09.230
So if you have a car,

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:11.220
each car is made different and requires

00:18:11.220 --> 00:18:12.380
a different sort of fuel,

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:15.920
whether it's a race car,
whether it's a diesel truck,

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:17.240
they have different fuels

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:19.890
for different performance outcomes.

00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:21.150
So if you're trying to tow something

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:22.900
or you're trying to go fast.

00:18:22.900 --> 00:18:24.580
So it's the same way with athletes.

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:26.620
It's pretty well studied.

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:29.100
The more intra-workout carbs

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:30.910
ultra long distance athletes take,

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:31.910
in general, they do better.

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:35.221
I think they've studied this
in cyclists quite often.

00:18:35.221 --> 00:18:37.060
It also depends on your genetics.

00:18:37.060 --> 00:18:39.300
So you can have a genetic polymorphism

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:42.540
and you metabolize carbs and sugar better,

00:18:42.540 --> 00:18:44.320
even when they're unopposed by fiber.

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:45.850
- How does one determine whether

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:48.553
or not they have such a polymorphism?

00:18:48.553 --> 00:18:50.170
I mean, I'm an omnivore,

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:52.610
so I do eat some high quality meats,

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:53.620
not in huge quantities,

00:18:53.620 --> 00:18:56.010
but I also eat vegetables
and starches, I feel fine.

00:18:56.010 --> 00:18:57.883
I've never done an elimination diet.

00:18:58.852 --> 00:19:00.740
I think I did a very low carb diet once

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:03.440
and all it gave me was a lot
of psoriasis and poor sleep,

00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:04.273
so I backed off.

00:19:04.273 --> 00:19:06.020
I probably didn't do it correctly,

00:19:06.020 --> 00:19:07.910
but I know a lot of
people that do quite well

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:10.560
on a very low carb or zero carb diet.

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:15.180
- Yeah, particularly those
who are at risk of cancer,

00:19:15.180 --> 00:19:16.940
because you have less glucose

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:19.230
that can be easily uptaken into cells.

00:19:19.230 --> 00:19:22.170
And then also people
with autoimmune diseases.

00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:23.380
- They tend to do well on auto-

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:25.570
- On lower carb diets, yeah.

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:28.410
But yeah, as far as the how do you know,

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:30.700
basically you can use your biofeedback,

00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:33.320
how you're feeling, to guess
what you tolerate well,

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:35.390
or you can just get genetic testing,

00:19:35.390 --> 00:19:37.610
which can be fairly
expensive, but most of all,

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:41.100
it requires a physician
or someone who knows how

00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:43.030
to interpret the test accurately.

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:45.070
- And if someone had the means or

00:19:45.070 --> 00:19:47.900
would you say that getting
regular blood testing

00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:48.733
is a good idea?

00:19:48.733 --> 00:19:50.600
And if so, what is regular blood testing?

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:52.780
Is it every three months?
Is it every six months?

00:19:52.780 --> 00:19:54.070
Of course the backdrop

00:19:54.070 --> 00:19:56.930
of life is changing too,
stress levels, et cetera.

00:19:56.930 --> 00:20:01.240
- Yeah, every three to six
months for preventative purposes,

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:02.640
at times you need blood tests

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:05.920
at faster frequencies than that.

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:08.090
And then you should also get a blood test

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:10.570
when you're fasting and
when you're not fasting.

00:20:10.570 --> 00:20:13.290
So if you're looking
for damage to the beach,

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:14.640
you don't just look at low tide,

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:16.480
you look at high tide and
you see what's happening

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:17.680
at high tide as well.

00:20:17.680 --> 00:20:18.827
- I think that's a great way to put it.

00:20:18.827 --> 00:20:23.390
And in terms of general
recommendations around exercise,

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:24.900
I mean, I'm of the mind,

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:26.330
based on the data that I've seen,

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:28.500
that almost everybody should,

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:33.400
or everybody should be getting
150 to 180 minutes minimum

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:35.260
of Zone 2 cardio per week

00:20:35.260 --> 00:20:39.190
that kind of could continue
while having a conversation,

00:20:39.190 --> 00:20:42.210
but if one were to exert any more effort,

00:20:42.210 --> 00:20:43.650
it would have a hard time
getting the words out.

00:20:43.650 --> 00:20:44.950
At least that, right?

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:47.010
For cardiovascular health
and general brain health

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:50.120
and musculoskeletal health
plus resistance exercise.

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:52.830
Is that more or less the
contour of what you recommend?

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:54.900
- Yeah, that's more or less the contour.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:59.583
The more you're doing your
Zone 2 cardiovascular exercise,

00:21:00.420 --> 00:21:03.880
the slightly less
important a long duration

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:05.780
of caloric restriction is.

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:08.260
- Interesting, and that brings
us to caloric restriction.

00:21:08.260 --> 00:21:12.360
So it's very clear that
caloric restriction

00:21:12.360 --> 00:21:14.970
can allow one to lose weight, right?

00:21:14.970 --> 00:21:17.250
This is the classic CICO, C-I-C-O,

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:18.500
calories in calories out.

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:20.660
We are not disputing
calories in calories out.

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:23.320
But somehow that always
has to be stated 50 times

00:21:23.320 --> 00:21:25.940
in any forum because of whatever follows,

00:21:25.940 --> 00:21:27.700
people I think will anchor to,

00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:28.880
and assume that we don't mean that,

00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:31.820
but I know you and I both agree
on calories in calories out

00:21:31.820 --> 00:21:33.960
as a fundamental law of thermodynamics.

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:38.700
But it's clear to me that
based on what I've read

00:21:38.700 --> 00:21:42.100
that when one is in a
slight caloric surplus

00:21:42.100 --> 00:21:44.870
that hormones like
testosterone can be optimized,

00:21:44.870 --> 00:21:47.150
but is that true for
somebody who's showing up

00:21:47.150 --> 00:21:48.880
with excessive body fat?

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:49.713
How does this all work?

00:21:49.713 --> 00:21:52.390
Because body fat is manufacturing enzymes

00:21:52.390 --> 00:21:54.070
that convert testosterone to estrogen.

00:21:54.070 --> 00:21:54.903
So in other words,

00:21:54.903 --> 00:21:57.460
how does someone know if they
should use caloric restriction

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:59.020
or avoid caloric restriction?

00:21:59.020 --> 00:22:01.040
- Yeah, here's how to parse that out.

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:05.110
So before I delve into the
details a bit more, I should say,

00:22:05.110 --> 00:22:07.860
as a board-certified
obesity medicine physician,

00:22:07.860 --> 00:22:10.880
obviously the laws of
thermodynamics apply.

00:22:10.880 --> 00:22:12.930
And then in addition to that,

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:16.390
there is nothing special
about intermittent fasting

00:22:16.390 --> 00:22:18.670
or caloric restriction

00:22:18.670 --> 00:22:20.720
or exercise when it pertains

00:22:20.720 --> 00:22:24.230
to losing body weight in general.

00:22:24.230 --> 00:22:25.280
When you do lose weight,

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:28.020
about 33% of that is lean body mass.

00:22:28.020 --> 00:22:31.120
And about 10% of fat cells,

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:34.330
adipose cells are actually
lean body mass as well,

00:22:34.330 --> 00:22:35.550
because it has proteins and water

00:22:35.550 --> 00:22:37.840
and things like that in it too so

00:22:38.840 --> 00:22:41.400
the reason for exercise

00:22:41.400 --> 00:22:44.460
and the reason for caloric
restriction in general,

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:47.310
including intermittent
fasting, is health reasons.

00:22:47.310 --> 00:22:49.290
That's how you increase your health span.

00:22:49.290 --> 00:22:50.920
It's not necessarily
going to make the weight

00:22:50.920 --> 00:22:53.860
on a scale change, but that
doesn't matter as much.

00:22:53.860 --> 00:22:55.923
It's been fairly well studied
in both mice and humans.

00:22:55.923 --> 00:22:58.020
It's much easier to study in mice.

00:22:58.020 --> 00:23:01.560
So that's a precursor to
our six types of people,

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:02.737
the ones that care about mice studies

00:23:02.737 --> 00:23:05.110
and the ones that care
about human studies.

00:23:05.110 --> 00:23:08.670
But if you correctly restrict mice by 40%,

00:23:08.670 --> 00:23:12.030
than they can

00:23:12.030 --> 00:23:15.090
have improved testosterone parameters,

00:23:15.090 --> 00:23:17.190
but only if they're obese to start.

00:23:17.190 --> 00:23:19.730
And it appears to be that
same way in humans as well.

00:23:19.730 --> 00:23:22.110
So the easy way to think about it is

00:23:22.110 --> 00:23:24.800
if you're obese or you
have metabolic syndrome,

00:23:24.800 --> 00:23:27.940
caloric restriction will
improve your testosterone.

00:23:27.940 --> 00:23:30.520
There has been a study and they
talk about all these studies

00:23:30.520 --> 00:23:33.470
in a systematic review from
the Mayo Clinic Proceedings

00:23:33.470 --> 00:23:35.630
in March of last year.

00:23:35.630 --> 00:23:39.030
And they note that there is a study

00:23:39.030 --> 00:23:42.770
in young, healthy men and
they calorically restrict them

00:23:42.770 --> 00:23:44.660
and their testosterone does decrease.

00:23:44.660 --> 00:23:46.090
So if you're young and healthy

00:23:46.090 --> 00:23:47.710
and you don't have metabolic syndrome,

00:23:47.710 --> 00:23:48.720
then caloric restriction

00:23:48.720 --> 00:23:51.480
will likely decrease your testosterone.

00:23:51.480 --> 00:23:53.460
- That clarifies a lot for me.

00:23:53.460 --> 00:23:55.510
And I believe it will clarify a lot

00:23:55.510 --> 00:23:56.820
for other people as well.

00:23:56.820 --> 00:24:00.040
And I'm delighted that you
pointed out this distinction

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:02.750
about intermittent fasting
not being the only way

00:24:02.750 --> 00:24:04.460
to achieve caloric restriction.

00:24:04.460 --> 00:24:08.380
There are a number of young, healthy,

00:24:08.380 --> 00:24:10.590
or older, healthy people I know

00:24:10.590 --> 00:24:13.020
who like using intermittent fasting,

00:24:13.020 --> 00:24:15.430
even if they're not trying to lose weight,

00:24:15.430 --> 00:24:16.530
for a couple of reasons.

00:24:16.530 --> 00:24:18.950
Some believe that it
might extend lifespan.

00:24:18.950 --> 00:24:21.410
I think that's still a
bit of an open question.

00:24:21.410 --> 00:24:22.820
It's a bit of a hard experiment to do,

00:24:22.820 --> 00:24:23.970
because the control group is,

00:24:23.970 --> 00:24:26.283
no one wants in the
control group as I say.

00:24:26.283 --> 00:24:27.870
- It does in mice.

00:24:27.870 --> 00:24:29.450
- Right. Exactly.
- Captive audience.

00:24:29.450 --> 00:24:32.380
- Exactly, and the other
feature of it that's

00:24:32.380 --> 00:24:34.730
a little bit tricky is that many people

00:24:34.730 --> 00:24:37.270
like intermittent fasting
because of the mental effects,

00:24:37.270 --> 00:24:39.440
the clarity of mind that
they feel during fasting,

00:24:39.440 --> 00:24:43.310
the increased pleasure in
eating when they finally do eat

00:24:44.500 --> 00:24:46.850
and here I'm referring
to intermittent fasting

00:24:46.850 --> 00:24:48.850
of the sort where eating
windows are anywhere

00:24:48.850 --> 00:24:50.340
from 8 to 12 hours a day.

00:24:50.340 --> 00:24:52.830
Not extended fasts of 24 hours or more.

00:24:52.830 --> 00:24:55.540
So the question therefore is,

00:24:55.540 --> 00:24:59.390
for the healthy lean enough person, right?

00:24:59.390 --> 00:25:03.760
Non-obese person, is
intermittent fasting a bad idea

00:25:03.760 --> 00:25:05.440
in terms of hormone health?

00:25:05.440 --> 00:25:07.330
Is oscillating between this period

00:25:07.330 --> 00:25:10.990
of kind of feast and famine
within a 24 hours a problem

00:25:10.990 --> 00:25:14.240
if one is getting sufficient
calories to maintain weight?

00:25:14.240 --> 00:25:16.590
- Yeah, so if they're in
a caloric maintenance,

00:25:16.590 --> 00:25:18.423
then it's not going to be,

00:25:20.400 --> 00:25:21.640
it's not going to be deleterious.

00:25:21.640 --> 00:25:24.090
It's not going to be bad
for their hormone health.

00:25:24.090 --> 00:25:26.100
There's a couple different
hormones that we can talk about.

00:25:26.100 --> 00:25:27.680
We can talk out testosterone.

00:25:27.680 --> 00:25:31.720
We can talk about DHEA, which
usually go hand in hand.

00:25:31.720 --> 00:25:33.430
And then we can also talk
about growth hormone,

00:25:33.430 --> 00:25:36.920
which is not a steroid hormone,
but it's a peptide hormone.

00:25:36.920 --> 00:25:39.870
So it's a chain of proteins,

00:25:39.870 --> 00:25:43.110
amino acids that are put
together instead of a sterile,

00:25:43.110 --> 00:25:46.590
think of sterile hormones
as coming from cholesterol.

00:25:46.590 --> 00:25:48.780
So intermittent fasting,

00:25:48.780 --> 00:25:52.320
you do get a little spike in
growth hormone after you eat,

00:25:52.320 --> 00:25:56.200
but you also get a huge
spike in growth hormone,

00:25:56.200 --> 00:26:00.880
a more significant, less
negligible spike overnight.

00:26:00.880 --> 00:26:05.170
And that is improved if you
are intermittent fasting.

00:26:05.170 --> 00:26:08.170
So it's probably going to
help your growth hormone

00:26:08.170 --> 00:26:11.090
and subsequently IGF-1 levels,

00:26:11.090 --> 00:26:14.300
which will help more
in the older age groups

00:26:14.300 --> 00:26:15.720
than younger age groups.

00:26:15.720 --> 00:26:17.530
- And I like to eat dinner.

00:26:17.530 --> 00:26:19.830
So for me, that means sometime
around six or seven o'clock,

00:26:19.830 --> 00:26:20.730
sometimes eight o'clock.

00:26:20.730 --> 00:26:23.686
I confess last night,
'cause I was working late,

00:26:23.686 --> 00:26:24.760
I ate pretty big,

00:26:24.760 --> 00:26:27.200
it was basically my only meal
of the day, at 10 o'clock.

00:26:27.200 --> 00:26:28.633
That's a rare thing for me.

00:26:30.010 --> 00:26:33.660
Can I still achieve a high
degree of growth hormone output

00:26:33.660 --> 00:26:36.800
if, let's say I avoid food
in the two to three hours

00:26:36.800 --> 00:26:38.150
before going to sleep?

00:26:38.150 --> 00:26:40.980
Or does one have to be very
deep into a fast in order

00:26:40.980 --> 00:26:44.300
to achieve the increase in growth hormone?

00:26:44.300 --> 00:26:46.760
- There's still pretty
good growth hormone output

00:26:46.760 --> 00:26:49.910
even if you eat two or three
hours before you sleep.

00:26:49.910 --> 00:26:52.690
It's just the law of diminishing
returns, the longer you go,

00:26:52.690 --> 00:26:54.800
you get slightly more and slightly more.

00:26:54.800 --> 00:26:58.160
- Right, and I know a
number of people think

00:26:58.160 --> 00:27:00.460
of growth hormone in the context

00:27:00.460 --> 00:27:03.930
of the exogenous growth
hormone and the fact

00:27:03.930 --> 00:27:08.730
that that can, in some cases,
be associated with cancers.

00:27:08.730 --> 00:27:10.240
I've been asked many times before,

00:27:10.240 --> 00:27:13.060
can the increase in growth
hormone from things like saunas

00:27:13.060 --> 00:27:15.590
or intermittent fasting cause
levels of growth hormone

00:27:15.590 --> 00:27:18.600
that are so high that they cause cancers.

00:27:18.600 --> 00:27:21.080
My impulse is to say, no,

00:27:21.080 --> 00:27:23.750
it seems like it's not like to happen,

00:27:23.750 --> 00:27:27.090
but I should probably verify
that statement with you.

00:27:27.090 --> 00:27:28.740
- Yeah, so quite unlikely.

00:27:28.740 --> 00:27:32.162
I think about growth hormone,
and especially IGF-1.

00:27:32.162 --> 00:27:34.090
And there's actually an IGF-1 and IGF-2.

00:27:34.090 --> 00:27:37.800
But I think about it in
terms of endocrine IGF-1,

00:27:37.800 --> 00:27:41.150
mostly IGF-1 that's
synthesized in the liver

00:27:41.150 --> 00:27:43.150
and released in the liver

00:27:43.150 --> 00:27:46.350
versus IGF-1 that's released classically.

00:27:46.350 --> 00:27:49.820
An example of this would be
your IGF-1 levels increase

00:27:49.820 --> 00:27:52.850
after resistance training or exercise.

00:27:52.850 --> 00:27:54.887
And that's more of like
paracrine or autocrine,

00:27:54.887 --> 00:27:57.600
and they have more local action.

00:27:57.600 --> 00:27:59.760
So that IGF-1,

00:27:59.760 --> 00:28:02.610
it's pretty well studied that
if you just give people IGF-1,

00:28:02.610 --> 00:28:05.520
it's not going to, at physiologic levels,

00:28:05.520 --> 00:28:08.410
it's not going to improve
their body composition.

00:28:08.410 --> 00:28:11.750
However, that IGF-1 that's
autocrine and paracrine

00:28:11.750 --> 00:28:14.930
just working in those
local tissues and muscles

00:28:14.930 --> 00:28:17.280
is likely part of the reason why you get

00:28:17.280 --> 00:28:21.720
a improved body composition
response after exercise.

00:28:21.720 --> 00:28:26.480
- I see, and just to clarify
for me and for others,

00:28:26.480 --> 00:28:29.660
what can we say are the
major functions of IGF-1

00:28:29.660 --> 00:28:32.540
and IGF-2 that are distinct
from just growth hormone?

00:28:32.540 --> 00:28:34.880
Are they just kind of the
active hormone growth hormone?

00:28:34.880 --> 00:28:37.680
The kind of the pickaxe end

00:28:38.900 --> 00:28:40.640
of the assembly line?
- Yeah.

00:28:40.640 --> 00:28:42.860
So they have a much
longer duration of action.

00:28:42.860 --> 00:28:45.200
I believe the half-life of IGF-1

00:28:45.200 --> 00:28:47.170
is several days almost a week,

00:28:47.170 --> 00:28:49.860
whereas growth hormone has
an extremely fast half-life

00:28:49.860 --> 00:28:51.690
of only hours.

00:28:51.690 --> 00:28:55.800
So growth hormone acts
significantly on the liver

00:28:55.800 --> 00:28:58.410
to produce IGF-1.

00:28:58.410 --> 00:29:01.960
So it's around

00:29:01.960 --> 00:29:04.440
in the serum in the blood long enough

00:29:04.440 --> 00:29:08.960
to where it's producing an
effect pretty much all the time.

00:29:08.960 --> 00:29:10.090
- Very interesting.
- Yep.

00:29:10.090 --> 00:29:12.770
- Well, and then your
other pillars, stress,

00:29:12.770 --> 00:29:15.280
we've talked a lot about
stress on this podcast before

00:29:15.280 --> 00:29:17.053
and tools for managing stress.

00:29:18.260 --> 00:29:20.040
Sleep obviously is a big one.

00:29:20.040 --> 00:29:22.580
I think, if nothing else,

00:29:22.580 --> 00:29:25.520
I will either put people
to sleep with my podcast.

00:29:25.520 --> 00:29:26.370
Certainly not one,

00:29:26.370 --> 00:29:29.730
but my solo episodes or
hopefully convince people

00:29:29.730 --> 00:29:31.370
that sleep is the foundation of mental

00:29:31.370 --> 00:29:33.050
and physical health and performance.

00:29:33.050 --> 00:29:36.010
Are there any aspects
of hormone optimization

00:29:36.010 --> 00:29:37.460
that can improve sleep?

00:29:37.460 --> 00:29:40.120
I know sleep can improve
hormone optimization,

00:29:40.120 --> 00:29:42.730
but are there any aspects
of hormonal optimization

00:29:42.730 --> 00:29:44.170
that can improve sleep?

00:29:44.170 --> 00:29:47.150
And for people that are suffering
from this common syndrome

00:29:47.150 --> 00:29:49.210
of going to sleep and then
waking up at 03:00 or 04:00

00:29:49.210 --> 00:29:50.043
in the morning,

00:29:50.043 --> 00:29:51.600
we know that can be
associated with depression,

00:29:51.600 --> 00:29:55.370
but are there any hormonal
indications that might lead

00:29:55.370 --> 00:29:57.640
to that kind of situation?

00:29:57.640 --> 00:29:59.900
- Yeah, there's three big ones.

00:29:59.900 --> 00:30:02.670
The first one is not super common,

00:30:02.670 --> 00:30:04.810
but it's a very direct correlation.

00:30:04.810 --> 00:30:08.750
If you have a growth hormone
deficiency, a true deficiency,

00:30:08.750 --> 00:30:10.350
whether you're an adult or a child,

00:30:10.350 --> 00:30:12.930
then your sleep is likely
going to be affected.

00:30:12.930 --> 00:30:16.320
And let's say you're a child
with growth hormone deficiency,

00:30:16.320 --> 00:30:19.030
once that is replaced with therapy,

00:30:19.030 --> 00:30:21.740
your sleep is going to
get significantly better.

00:30:21.740 --> 00:30:25.100
The second one that's
a very common scenario

00:30:25.100 --> 00:30:28.410
is if you're having what's
called vasomotor symptoms

00:30:28.410 --> 00:30:31.300
of menopause or vasomotor
symptoms of andropause

00:30:31.300 --> 00:30:33.770
which are also applicable.

00:30:33.770 --> 00:30:37.400
And that's where your
progestogenic activity,

00:30:37.400 --> 00:30:41.350
so your main progestogens are progesterone

00:30:41.350 --> 00:30:42.762
and then and pregnenolone

00:30:42.762 --> 00:30:45.880
and then 5-alpha,
3-alpha-progesterone, which is-

00:30:45.880 --> 00:30:48.230
- Where are those
manufactured in the body?

00:30:48.230 --> 00:30:51.490
- So they're manufactured in a few places.

00:30:51.490 --> 00:30:54.487
In men, they're manufactured
some in the testes

00:30:54.487 --> 00:30:56.080
in the Leydig cells.

00:30:56.080 --> 00:30:57.480
In women, they're manufactured

00:30:57.480 --> 00:30:59.610
in the ovaries until menopause.

00:30:59.610 --> 00:31:02.740
And then they're also
manufactured in the adrenal gland.

00:31:02.740 --> 00:31:06.700
So if you're pre-adrenopausal

00:31:07.660 --> 00:31:10.610
where your adrenal glands are
still working fairly well,

00:31:10.610 --> 00:31:13.287
usually still have a decent
amount of progesterone around,

00:31:13.287 --> 00:31:15.500
and this can be measured too.

00:31:15.500 --> 00:31:18.650
So after menopause,

00:31:18.650 --> 00:31:22.510
women make progesterone
from their ovaries,

00:31:22.510 --> 00:31:24.620
or sorry, from their adrenal glands.

00:31:24.620 --> 00:31:27.910
If that progesterone crosses
the blood-brain barrier,

00:31:27.910 --> 00:31:30.300
especially if it's 5-alpha
and 3-alpha reduced,

00:31:30.300 --> 00:31:32.190
so it's modified a little bit,

00:31:32.190 --> 00:31:35.030
then it is both a GABA agonist,

00:31:35.030 --> 00:31:37.210
which helps sleep just like GABA does,

00:31:37.210 --> 00:31:38.830
gamma-amino butyric acid,

00:31:38.830 --> 00:31:41.590
the main inhibitory neurotransmitter

00:31:41.590 --> 00:31:42.940
of which lots of things work on,

00:31:42.940 --> 00:31:44.640
alcohol works on GABA as well.

00:31:44.640 --> 00:31:46.990
Gabapentin also works on GABA.

00:31:46.990 --> 00:31:50.110
Migraine medicines, many
of them work on GABA.

00:31:50.110 --> 00:31:53.855
Benzodiazepines, and also non-benzos.

00:31:53.855 --> 00:31:55.840
So an example of a benzo would be Xanax.

00:31:55.840 --> 00:32:00.630
An example of a non benzo would be Ambien.

00:32:00.630 --> 00:32:02.360
So those all work on GABA.

00:32:02.360 --> 00:32:05.460
So GABA is also helped by

00:32:05.460 --> 00:32:07.800
the progestogenic activity as well.

00:32:07.800 --> 00:32:10.410
That's why a lot of women in
menopause feel like their sleep

00:32:10.410 --> 00:32:13.810
is much worse is because
they have lower activity

00:32:13.810 --> 00:32:15.860
of those progestogens.

00:32:15.860 --> 00:32:18.483
- And for men in so-called andropause,

00:32:19.460 --> 00:32:22.640
low testosterone, is that
also one of the causes

00:32:22.640 --> 00:32:24.220
of poor sleep.

00:32:24.220 --> 00:32:26.337
- Low testosterone can lead to poor sleep,

00:32:26.337 --> 00:32:30.020
nut my third scenario is actually,

00:32:30.020 --> 00:32:32.170
if a man begins TRT,

00:32:32.170 --> 00:32:35.150
then they develop poor sleep
because of sleep apnea.

00:32:35.150 --> 00:32:38.390
It drastically raises
the risk that somebody

00:32:38.390 --> 00:32:39.990
is going to have sleep apnea.

00:32:39.990 --> 00:32:40.890
And then a lot of people,

00:32:40.890 --> 00:32:42.070
especially when they first started

00:32:42.070 --> 00:32:43.530
in the first month or two,

00:32:43.530 --> 00:32:45.870
it puts them into this
hypersympathetic state,

00:32:45.870 --> 00:32:49.540
because they have overactive
androgen receptors,

00:32:49.540 --> 00:32:52.430
especially after a long
time of being hypogonadal.

00:32:52.430 --> 00:32:56.950
Then they have a physiologic dose of TRT

00:32:56.950 --> 00:33:00.130
and that causes the sleep issue itself.

00:33:00.130 --> 00:33:02.940
- Interesting, I have a
lot of questions about TRT,

00:33:02.940 --> 00:33:05.360
testosterone replacement therapy.

00:33:05.360 --> 00:33:07.680
I should just mention that when you say

00:33:07.680 --> 00:33:09.763
it increases sympathetic activity,

00:33:10.750 --> 00:33:14.240
you don't mean that taking testosterone

00:33:14.240 --> 00:33:15.800
increases sympathy for others.

00:33:15.800 --> 00:33:17.010
It may in fact do the opposite.

00:33:17.010 --> 00:33:18.930
Although it's very clear
from my discussions

00:33:18.930 --> 00:33:20.170
with my colleagues

00:33:21.010 --> 00:33:23.420
in the endocrinology side and also with

00:33:23.420 --> 00:33:25.400
the great Dr. Robert Sapolsky

00:33:25.400 --> 00:33:26.730
that increasing testosterone

00:33:26.730 --> 00:33:30.150
merely exacerbates existing
features of people.

00:33:30.150 --> 00:33:31.670
So the jerks become bigger jerks,

00:33:31.670 --> 00:33:35.210
kind people become even
more kind in general,

00:33:35.210 --> 00:33:37.750
but I want to get into TRT in depth,

00:33:37.750 --> 00:33:38.920
but it's very interesting to me

00:33:38.920 --> 00:33:42.250
to hear that testosterone
replacement therapy increases

00:33:42.250 --> 00:33:44.240
the risk of sleep apnea.

00:33:44.240 --> 00:33:47.470
And I want to make sure that I ask that

00:33:47.470 --> 00:33:50.580
is that also the case in
people that are using TRT

00:33:50.580 --> 00:33:52.190
who are not hypogonadal?

00:33:52.190 --> 00:33:54.340
Because in the classic situation,

00:33:54.340 --> 00:33:56.030
if somebody isn't making
enough testosterone,

00:33:56.030 --> 00:33:58.380
they're below 300 nanograms
per deciliter on the chart,

00:33:58.380 --> 00:33:59.213
they go in and take TRT.

00:33:59.213 --> 00:34:01.640
But many people nowadays, let's be honest,

00:34:01.640 --> 00:34:05.020
are taking doses of testosterone

00:34:05.020 --> 00:34:07.180
even though they are in
the sort of standard range,

00:34:07.180 --> 00:34:08.970
because the range is so large because

00:34:08.970 --> 00:34:11.250
of other symptomology, is that right?

00:34:11.250 --> 00:34:15.030
- Yeah, I do love the
analogy that Dr. Sapolsky had

00:34:15.030 --> 00:34:17.250
about monks taking testosterone

00:34:17.250 --> 00:34:19.550
and making them more and more generous.

00:34:19.550 --> 00:34:23.380
So that does appear to be what
testosterone usually does,

00:34:23.380 --> 00:34:26.890
is it exacerbates, if you will,
what you're previously like.

00:34:26.890 --> 00:34:29.570
So it's not going to
change you as a person.

00:34:29.570 --> 00:34:34.490
But if you're eugonadal
before you start testosterone-

00:34:34.490 --> 00:34:35.323
- Meaning?

00:34:35.323 --> 00:34:37.050
- Meaning you have normal testosterone,

00:34:37.050 --> 00:34:40.050
and then you start TRT or

00:34:40.050 --> 00:34:41.600
self-administered TRT,

00:34:41.600 --> 00:34:44.130
steroids, however you want to look at it,

00:34:44.130 --> 00:34:46.580
then your risk of sleep
apnea still goes up

00:34:46.580 --> 00:34:48.190
in a dose-dependent fashion.

00:34:48.190 --> 00:34:50.780
So the higher the dose, the more risky.

00:34:50.780 --> 00:34:53.510
With the sympathetic and the
parasympathetic nervous system,

00:34:53.510 --> 00:34:56.180
the sympathetic is the fight
or flight nervous system,

00:34:56.180 --> 00:34:58.920
the parasympathetic is
the rest and digest.

00:34:58.920 --> 00:35:00.720
So if you have too much fight or flight,

00:35:00.720 --> 00:35:02.250
and stress can cause that too,

00:35:02.250 --> 00:35:04.300
then you're not going to
rest as well at night.

00:35:04.300 --> 00:35:08.400
- I want to touch on
testosterone in women because

00:35:09.630 --> 00:35:11.090
there is testosterone in women.

00:35:11.090 --> 00:35:13.510
I'd like to know where that
testosterone comes from,

00:35:13.510 --> 00:35:16.280
which tissues, I'd like to know whether

00:35:16.280 --> 00:35:19.510
or not testosterone replacement
therapy make sense in women.

00:35:19.510 --> 00:35:22.280
I'm hearing more and more
about women using testosterone.

00:35:22.280 --> 00:35:25.500
And I'd like to know
whether or not knowing

00:35:25.500 --> 00:35:26.560
a woman's testos,

00:35:26.560 --> 00:35:30.860
for her to know her
testosterone is of equal,

00:35:30.860 --> 00:35:33.870
less than or more value
than knowing, for instance,

00:35:33.870 --> 00:35:35.290
progesterone and estrogen levels?

00:35:35.290 --> 00:35:37.090
Because I think there are a
lot of misconceptions about

00:35:37.090 --> 00:35:38.770
the roles of testosterone in women.

00:35:38.770 --> 00:35:40.220
- For health optimization,

00:35:40.220 --> 00:35:43.270
testosterone is just as important to know.

00:35:43.270 --> 00:35:46.550
For pathology prevention, for example,

00:35:46.550 --> 00:35:48.860
breast cancer, osteoporosis,

00:35:48.860 --> 00:35:52.380
estrogen, and progesterone
are more important to know.

00:35:52.380 --> 00:35:53.830
So when you're thinking about women,

00:35:53.830 --> 00:35:55.520
women think that they
have such a tiny amount

00:35:55.520 --> 00:35:57.850
of testosterone, because you test it,

00:35:57.850 --> 00:35:59.950
most people test a free testosterone,

00:35:59.950 --> 00:36:02.290
so a testosterone that's unbound,

00:36:02.290 --> 00:36:03.730
which is by far

00:36:03.730 --> 00:36:06.890
the smallest proportion of testosterone.

00:36:06.890 --> 00:36:09.580
Any androgen is bound by lots

00:36:09.580 --> 00:36:12.520
of different steroid-binding proteins.

00:36:12.520 --> 00:36:15.540
But the ones that are most
pertinent are called SHBG,

00:36:15.540 --> 00:36:17.760
or sex hormone-binding globulin.

00:36:17.760 --> 00:36:20.750
And that binds the androgenic steroid,

00:36:20.750 --> 00:36:23.600
for example, DHT or dihydrotestosterone.

00:36:23.600 --> 00:36:25.630
It's associated with prostate enlargement,

00:36:25.630 --> 00:36:27.620
it's associated with
male pattern baldness.

00:36:27.620 --> 00:36:29.790
It binds that the most strongly,

00:36:29.790 --> 00:36:32.660
and then it binds testosterone
next most strongly,

00:36:32.660 --> 00:36:35.580
and then it binds things
like androstenedione

00:36:35.580 --> 00:36:37.983
or DHEA, dehydroepiandrosterone.

00:36:39.750 --> 00:36:41.910
And then it binds the estrogens,

00:36:41.910 --> 00:36:43.310
the weakest, like estradiol.

00:36:44.360 --> 00:36:47.320
So if you look at the total
amount of testosterone,

00:36:47.320 --> 00:36:50.940
women actually have, almost
all women, not all women,

00:36:50.940 --> 00:36:55.520
but almost all of them have
significantly more testosterone

00:36:56.370 --> 00:36:58.310
than estradiol, but it's because it's

00:36:58.310 --> 00:37:00.780
in different measurements.

00:37:00.780 --> 00:37:03.820
So estradiol, a lot of
time is picograms per mil

00:37:03.820 --> 00:37:06.310
as opposed to nanograms per deciliter.

00:37:06.310 --> 00:37:09.770
So women have more
testosterone than estrogen

00:37:09.770 --> 00:37:14.090
and significantly more DHEA than either.

00:37:14.090 --> 00:37:16.860
- Interesting. Do women
make dihydrotestosterone?

00:37:16.860 --> 00:37:18.110
- Yeah.

00:37:18.110 --> 00:37:20.510
- And where does this
testosterone come from?

00:37:20.510 --> 00:37:22.180
Because they don't have testes.

00:37:22.180 --> 00:37:24.550
- Yeah, so most testosterone in women

00:37:24.550 --> 00:37:29.400
that are premenopausal can come
from theca cells, T-H-E-C-A.

00:37:29.400 --> 00:37:31.480
So theca cells are cells in the ovaries

00:37:31.480 --> 00:37:33.390
that can produce testosterone.

00:37:33.390 --> 00:37:37.070
And a lot of people have actually
heard about hyperthecosis,

00:37:37.070 --> 00:37:38.700
not the term itself.

00:37:38.700 --> 00:37:41.520
But a lot of Olympians that are,

00:37:41.520 --> 00:37:44.970
their chromosomes are XY, they're females,

00:37:44.970 --> 00:37:47.250
and they're not taking any-

00:37:47.250 --> 00:37:48.369
- Wait, they're XY,

00:37:48.369 --> 00:37:49.990
but they're females?
- Or sorry, they're XX.

00:37:49.990 --> 00:37:51.430
- Oh, okay.
- Yeah. Thank you.

00:37:51.430 --> 00:37:53.453
So they're XX, they're not XY,

00:37:54.300 --> 00:37:56.210
and they have never transitioned or been

00:37:56.210 --> 00:37:59.600
on any sort of hormone
replacement or testosterone,

00:37:59.600 --> 00:38:03.270
but they naturally produce a
huge amount of testosterone,

00:38:03.270 --> 00:38:05.090
as much as many men.

00:38:05.090 --> 00:38:06.490
And some of these women,

00:38:06.490 --> 00:38:08.150
I believe they were from Botswana,

00:38:08.150 --> 00:38:10.630
were banned from competing in the Olympics

00:38:10.630 --> 00:38:12.450
in certain distances.

00:38:12.450 --> 00:38:15.890
I believe they were banned from
the 400 meter and 800 meter,

00:38:15.890 --> 00:38:17.790
because their natural testosterone

00:38:17.790 --> 00:38:19.310
was deemed to be too high.

00:38:19.310 --> 00:38:22.140
- So they mistakenly thought
that they were using steroids?

00:38:22.140 --> 00:38:24.840
- They actually knew they
were not using steroids.

00:38:24.840 --> 00:38:26.390
They knew it was their theca cells

00:38:26.390 --> 00:38:28.940
were just genetically gifted, I suppose.

00:38:28.940 --> 00:38:31.230
And they still made them change distances.

00:38:31.230 --> 00:38:32.063
- [Andrew] Wow.

00:38:32.063 --> 00:38:33.880
- So one or two of these
athletes changed to,

00:38:33.880 --> 00:38:37.240
I believe it was the 3K or the 5K,

00:38:37.240 --> 00:38:38.870
and they still did quite well,

00:38:38.870 --> 00:38:40.590
but it was not their best event.

00:38:40.590 --> 00:38:41.713
- Interesting, yeah, that's turning out

00:38:41.713 --> 00:38:44.450
to be a very interesting
and controversial area

00:38:44.450 --> 00:38:47.310
of this notion of hormone
therapies and natural variation

00:38:47.310 --> 00:38:49.880
in hormones on different
chromosomal backgrounds.

00:38:49.880 --> 00:38:50.770
Fascinating, we should probably do

00:38:50.770 --> 00:38:52.650
a whole episode about that,

00:38:52.650 --> 00:38:54.400
'cause it's very much of the times.

00:38:55.999 --> 00:38:59.250
So men and women both make DHT.

00:38:59.250 --> 00:39:02.250
I'd like to ask about DHT in men.

00:39:02.250 --> 00:39:04.600
So often we hear about testosterone in men

00:39:04.600 --> 00:39:08.730
and free testosterone being
the unbound form of course.

00:39:08.730 --> 00:39:13.600
But dihydrotestosterone, where
does it come from in men?

00:39:13.600 --> 00:39:17.400
What is the cascade of events
that takes testosterone

00:39:17.400 --> 00:39:19.860
to dihydrotestosterone and what are some

00:39:19.860 --> 00:39:21.770
of the quote/unquote positive

00:39:21.770 --> 00:39:23.870
and negative effects of,

00:39:23.870 --> 00:39:28.170
here I'm only referring to
endogenous dihydrotestosterone.

00:39:28.170 --> 00:39:29.003
And in fact,

00:39:29.003 --> 00:39:31.440
I'll make it very clear whether or not

00:39:31.440 --> 00:39:33.210
I'm talking about taking something

00:39:33.210 --> 00:39:34.630
or one's own natural production.

00:39:34.630 --> 00:39:35.463
Here we're just,

00:39:35.463 --> 00:39:36.296
I think up until now we've

00:39:36.296 --> 00:39:37.950
just been talking about
natural production.

00:39:37.950 --> 00:39:40.440
So tell us about DHT in men,

00:39:40.440 --> 00:39:43.090
such a powerful hormone
during development obviously.

00:39:44.024 --> 00:39:45.273
But what is it doing?

00:39:46.180 --> 00:39:48.700
- DHT is a very androgenic hormone.

00:39:48.700 --> 00:39:51.360
So whether you're talking about DHEA,

00:39:51.360 --> 00:39:54.950
which is a weak androgen,

00:39:54.950 --> 00:39:58.430
or testosterone, which is a
relatively strong androgen,

00:39:58.430 --> 00:40:01.310
or DHT, which is a very strong androgen,

00:40:01.310 --> 00:40:03.990
they bind to the androgen
receptor in both men

00:40:03.990 --> 00:40:05.330
and in women.

00:40:05.330 --> 00:40:09.230
So the effect of all
three of those is mediated

00:40:09.230 --> 00:40:11.160
by the androgen receptor.

00:40:11.160 --> 00:40:13.890
There's a couple different
beta-estradiol receptors

00:40:13.890 --> 00:40:15.810
and alpha-estradiol receptors,

00:40:15.810 --> 00:40:18.300
but there's only one androgen receptor.

00:40:18.300 --> 00:40:21.030
Intriguingly, it is on the X chromosome,

00:40:21.030 --> 00:40:25.193
so men get their androgen
receptor gene from their mother.

00:40:26.090 --> 00:40:29.720
Women get one androgen receptor
gene from their father,

00:40:29.720 --> 00:40:31.000
one from their mother.

00:40:31.000 --> 00:40:33.670
Often the one that is more
sensitive to androgens

00:40:33.670 --> 00:40:36.550
and people with PCOS, that's
the one that's active.

00:40:36.550 --> 00:40:38.950
The other one is methylated and inactive.

00:40:38.950 --> 00:40:40.070
- Can I just pause you one second?

00:40:40.070 --> 00:40:40.903
Sorry to interrupt,

00:40:40.903 --> 00:40:43.800
but I have to ask this
question before I forget.

00:40:43.800 --> 00:40:45.280
And I know a number of people
are probably wondering,

00:40:45.280 --> 00:40:47.110
I've heard that whether

00:40:47.110 --> 00:40:50.420
or not one develops male pattern baldness,

00:40:50.420 --> 00:40:53.700
whether or not a male develops
male pattern baldness,

00:40:53.700 --> 00:40:55.203
just to be very precise,

00:40:56.610 --> 00:40:59.020
you could get some information
about that by looking

00:40:59.020 --> 00:41:00.790
at your mother's father,

00:41:00.790 --> 00:41:03.170
and that would, in keeping
with what you just described,

00:41:03.170 --> 00:41:04.050
that the X chromosome,

00:41:04.050 --> 00:41:06.610
which of course is handed
off through the mother,

00:41:06.610 --> 00:41:09.310
is carrying the genes that encode

00:41:09.310 --> 00:41:11.962
for the number and distribution

00:41:11.962 --> 00:41:14.090
of these androgen receptors
that DHT will bind to,

00:41:14.090 --> 00:41:14.923
'cause of course,

00:41:14.923 --> 00:41:15.940
I think as you'll probably tell us,

00:41:15.940 --> 00:41:17.260
that DHD is a responsible

00:41:17.260 --> 00:41:19.610
for male pattern bald and
beard growth, is that right?

00:41:19.610 --> 00:41:21.970
Should I look at my
grandfather on my mother's side

00:41:21.970 --> 00:41:24.090
to determine what I'm
likely to look like in terms

00:41:24.090 --> 00:41:26.800
of my DHT-ness, is that a word?

00:41:26.800 --> 00:41:27.920
- Yeah, it's the best guess

00:41:27.920 --> 00:41:31.050
that you could make
purely from phenotypes.

00:41:31.050 --> 00:41:33.680
Now you can measure your genotype and

00:41:34.590 --> 00:41:35.950
get a better idea of that.

00:41:35.950 --> 00:41:38.130
Assuming that it's true
male pattern baldness,

00:41:38.130 --> 00:41:40.420
it's related to the gene transcription

00:41:40.420 --> 00:41:42.230
of the androgen receptor.

00:41:42.230 --> 00:41:45.880
So I like to think of
it as how much of this

00:41:45.880 --> 00:41:50.800
androgen receptor gene is
activated by any androgen?

00:41:50.800 --> 00:41:53.010
So if you have an
extremely sensitive gene,

00:41:53.010 --> 00:41:55.970
which usually means you
have very few CAG repeats,

00:41:55.970 --> 00:41:57.900
which is basically just

00:41:57.900 --> 00:42:02.170
a certain, CAG encodes
for a certain amino acid,

00:42:02.170 --> 00:42:04.750
and if you have very few of the repeats,

00:42:04.750 --> 00:42:07.460
then your androgen
receptor gene works better.

00:42:07.460 --> 00:42:10.310
Think of it as a corollary
to Huntington's disease

00:42:10.310 --> 00:42:14.250
where if you have very few of,
called trinucleotide repeats,

00:42:14.250 --> 00:42:17.200
then it's not as severe as a disease,

00:42:17.200 --> 00:42:20.150
but after you get more
and more CAG repeats,

00:42:20.150 --> 00:42:21.760
which by the way are,

00:42:21.760 --> 00:42:24.793
in the population you're getting
more and more CAG repeats,

00:42:25.710 --> 00:42:27.960
so it's a natural selection of process

00:42:27.960 --> 00:42:32.700
that has been ongoing for a
variety of number of reasons.

00:42:32.700 --> 00:42:34.340
But anyway if you have more repeats,

00:42:34.340 --> 00:42:37.070
then that gene activates in the cytoplasm

00:42:37.070 --> 00:42:38.350
and moves to the nucleus

00:42:38.350 --> 00:42:40.890
and causes gene transcription more often

00:42:40.890 --> 00:42:42.640
and hair loss more often.

00:42:42.640 --> 00:42:45.590
- So does that mean that we're
seeing more hair loss now due

00:42:45.590 --> 00:42:49.003
to elevated levels of DHT
than we were 50 years ago?

00:42:50.340 --> 00:42:51.383
- Probably not.

00:42:52.380 --> 00:42:56.690
The hair loss 50 years ago,
well, not 50 years ago,

00:42:56.690 --> 00:42:57.950
but 500 years ago,

00:42:57.950 --> 00:43:00.160
was probably more significant,

00:43:00.160 --> 00:43:02.760
because on average, 500 years ago,

00:43:02.760 --> 00:43:05.510
people were more sensitive to androgens.

00:43:05.510 --> 00:43:06.730
So there's a syndrome called

00:43:06.730 --> 00:43:09.418
androgen insensitivity syndrome,

00:43:09.418 --> 00:43:13.440
AIS and that syndrome
was related to when men,

00:43:13.440 --> 00:43:16.640
who have the copy from their
mother who is a carrier,

00:43:16.640 --> 00:43:19.830
their AR gene, or androgen receptor gene,

00:43:19.830 --> 00:43:21.810
is completely insensitive.

00:43:21.810 --> 00:43:23.400
So think of it,

00:43:23.400 --> 00:43:25.290
it's not related to the CAG repeats,

00:43:25.290 --> 00:43:30.290
but think of that receptor
as just not working at all.

00:43:30.630 --> 00:43:31.950
So there's a continuum,

00:43:31.950 --> 00:43:34.460
so everybody's receptor
works a little bit better

00:43:34.460 --> 00:43:35.900
or a little bit worse.

00:43:35.900 --> 00:43:38.090
And the better your receptor works,

00:43:38.090 --> 00:43:40.930
the more likely you are to
have male pattern baldness.

00:43:40.930 --> 00:43:45.807
- To zoom out from this, but
still keeping an eye on DHT,

00:43:46.970 --> 00:43:51.970
what do you like to see
all women in all men do

00:43:52.090 --> 00:43:54.350
to optimize DHT?

00:43:54.350 --> 00:43:56.290
And here I'm talking
about regardless of age.

00:43:56.290 --> 00:43:59.200
So we're still in this
from puberty onward phase.

00:43:59.200 --> 00:44:01.880
We haven't yet micro-dissected
out decade by decade,

00:44:01.880 --> 00:44:02.713
which we will do,

00:44:02.713 --> 00:44:05.940
but what do you like to see
people do to keep DHT in check?

00:44:05.940 --> 00:44:07.600
But before you tell us that,

00:44:07.600 --> 00:44:11.930
could you tell us what
positive things DHT does

00:44:11.930 --> 00:44:13.730
when it's in the proper range?

00:44:13.730 --> 00:44:16.794
- Yeah, so DHT helps a lot for,

00:44:16.794 --> 00:44:18.300
it's the same reason
why testosterone helps,

00:44:18.300 --> 00:44:20.550
it activates the antigen receptor gene.

00:44:20.550 --> 00:44:22.500
It helps effort feel good.

00:44:22.500 --> 00:44:24.610
So it can be motivating.

00:44:24.610 --> 00:44:27.210
So that's how it's active in the CNS.

00:44:27.210 --> 00:44:30.420
It also is active in
cardiovascular tissue.

00:44:30.420 --> 00:44:34.640
So if you look at someone
that has heart failure

00:44:34.640 --> 00:44:37.410
or if someone has cardiac hypertrophy,

00:44:37.410 --> 00:44:41.010
the level of DHT can matter
because it's also binding

00:44:41.010 --> 00:44:43.203
to the androgen receptor in the myocardium

00:44:43.203 --> 00:44:45.230
or in the heart itself.

00:44:45.230 --> 00:44:48.660
So you think of the
classic bodybuilder heart.

00:44:48.660 --> 00:44:50.530
It's an easy example to make.

00:44:50.530 --> 00:44:52.370
They have very thickened muscle.

00:44:52.370 --> 00:44:53.680
Their muscle is very strong,

00:44:53.680 --> 00:44:57.770
because they're pumping blood
often with high blood pressure

00:44:57.770 --> 00:45:00.587
and that DHT and the testosterone

00:45:00.587 --> 00:45:05.430
and any DHT derivatives like
Masteron or oxandrolone,

00:45:05.430 --> 00:45:08.130
preamble and also bind to the heart,

00:45:08.130 --> 00:45:10.610
and they cause even more hypertrophy

00:45:10.610 --> 00:45:13.190
or enlargement of that muscle tissue.

00:45:13.190 --> 00:45:16.030
So then let's say the person
stops and they're recovering,

00:45:16.030 --> 00:45:18.810
and they're trying to
have cardiac remodeling,

00:45:18.810 --> 00:45:21.620
which is where you take
a very thick heart,

00:45:21.620 --> 00:45:23.250
and cardiac remodeling's important

00:45:23.250 --> 00:45:27.050
in a lot of different cardiac pathologies,

00:45:27.050 --> 00:45:29.620
but if you give them
finasteride or dutasteride,

00:45:29.620 --> 00:45:32.310
which inhibit the enzyme that
can converts testosterone

00:45:32.310 --> 00:45:35.170
to DHT, so making less activity

00:45:35.170 --> 00:45:37.240
at the androgen receptor gene,

00:45:37.240 --> 00:45:38.450
they have cardiac remodeling,

00:45:38.450 --> 00:45:40.240
and their heart health improves.

00:45:40.240 --> 00:45:42.280
- I see, so for the non-body builder,

00:45:42.280 --> 00:45:46.530
the typical woman or
man, younger or older,

00:45:46.530 --> 00:45:51.320
what sorts of things support
DHT, and thereby heart health?

00:45:51.320 --> 00:45:53.530
Presumably DHT she is involved
in some of the other things

00:45:53.530 --> 00:45:56.280
that testosterone is famous
for in both men and women.

00:45:56.280 --> 00:45:58.360
Things like libido, as you mentioned,

00:45:58.360 --> 00:45:59.300
making effort feel good.

00:45:59.300 --> 00:46:03.240
So motivation, drive and vitality is,

00:46:03.240 --> 00:46:06.400
I guess, could be the general phrase.

00:46:06.400 --> 00:46:07.950
What sorts of things support DHT?

00:46:07.950 --> 00:46:11.560
What sorts of things
create problems for DHT?

00:46:11.560 --> 00:46:14.390
- There's lots of dietary
changes and supplementation

00:46:14.390 --> 00:46:16.010
that you're probably doing right now

00:46:16.010 --> 00:46:17.470
that's affecting your DHT.

00:46:17.470 --> 00:46:19.640
- You mean me personally?
- Well, everybody.

00:46:19.640 --> 00:46:21.193
All of the listeners.

00:46:22.240 --> 00:46:25.010
Because let's say you have a diet high

00:46:25.010 --> 00:46:26.640
in plant polyphenols,

00:46:26.640 --> 00:46:28.950
many of those inhibit the enzyme

00:46:28.950 --> 00:46:31.013
that converts testosterone to DHT.

00:46:32.670 --> 00:46:34.590
- Could you give us an example

00:46:34.590 --> 00:46:37.830
of one of those, either
in supplementation form,

00:46:37.830 --> 00:46:39.610
or in food form?

00:46:39.610 --> 00:46:41.780
- Curcumins, certain curcuminoids,

00:46:41.780 --> 00:46:43.460
depending on the structure,

00:46:43.460 --> 00:46:46.510
will inhibit the enzyme
called 5-alpha-reductase

00:46:46.510 --> 00:46:48.380
that converts testosterone to DHT.

00:46:48.380 --> 00:46:50.160
- Turmeric?
- Yeah. Turmeric.

00:46:50.160 --> 00:46:51.460
Black pepper extract.

00:46:51.460 --> 00:46:55.370
So it's used often to
increase bioavailability.

00:46:55.370 --> 00:46:57.500
It's also called BioPerine.

00:46:57.500 --> 00:46:59.803
It's also a 5-alpha-reductase inhibitor.

00:47:01.910 --> 00:47:04.820
And on top of that, people
have different genetics too.

00:47:04.820 --> 00:47:07.710
So some people, they're
5-alpha-reductase enzymes,

00:47:07.710 --> 00:47:08.810
there's three of them.

00:47:09.840 --> 00:47:12.940
They're on chromosome two,
three, and four, I believe,

00:47:12.940 --> 00:47:15.390
but some of them are
active in the prostate,

00:47:15.390 --> 00:47:17.410
some of them are active in the brain.

00:47:17.410 --> 00:47:19.660
And so it depends on which tissue,

00:47:19.660 --> 00:47:23.150
they're tissue-specific
enzymes that depend on

00:47:23.150 --> 00:47:26.210
how much DHT you convert.

00:47:26.210 --> 00:47:28.070
- Do you recommend that
people avoid curcumin

00:47:28.070 --> 00:47:29.970
and turmeric for that reason?

00:47:29.970 --> 00:47:32.110
And is there any specific recommendations

00:47:32.110 --> 00:47:33.363
for men versus women.

00:47:34.460 --> 00:47:37.390
- If a man or a woman, by the
way, in women, a lot of times,

00:47:37.390 --> 00:47:39.970
if you just ask your
doctor for a DHT check,

00:47:39.970 --> 00:47:41.440
it's the same units as in men,

00:47:41.440 --> 00:47:43.460
so it's essentially undetectable.

00:47:43.460 --> 00:47:45.023
So you have to,

00:47:46.390 --> 00:47:48.160
especially if they're
on oral contraceptives,

00:47:48.160 --> 00:47:49.130
which is a front topic,

00:47:49.130 --> 00:47:51.750
their DHT is very likely undetectable,

00:47:51.750 --> 00:47:53.740
especially if it's free DHT.

00:47:53.740 --> 00:47:57.210
You can measure both a DHT and a free DHT.

00:47:57.210 --> 00:47:59.510
But if someone's DHT is already low,

00:47:59.510 --> 00:48:04.260
or if they have somewhat
insensitive androgen receptor

00:48:04.260 --> 00:48:07.420
via genetics or via lifestyle,

00:48:07.420 --> 00:48:11.180
then I recommend they avoid
bioavailable curcuminoids

00:48:11.180 --> 00:48:14.510
like bioavailable turmeric,
black pepper extract,

00:48:14.510 --> 00:48:16.670
and they might be a good
candidate for creatine.

00:48:16.670 --> 00:48:19.417
Creatine, like creatine monohydrate,

00:48:19.417 --> 00:48:21.700
can significantly increase the conversion

00:48:21.700 --> 00:48:23.180
of testosterone to DHT.

00:48:23.180 --> 00:48:24.190
- Interesting, there's also a lot

00:48:24.190 --> 00:48:26.540
of really interesting
data coming out now about

00:48:27.410 --> 00:48:30.030
the role of creatine as a brain fuel,

00:48:30.030 --> 00:48:32.210
and maybe even as a
cognitive enhancer over time.

00:48:32.210 --> 00:48:34.200
The data is still ongoing,

00:48:34.200 --> 00:48:36.550
but some of the studies in
humans are pretty impressive,

00:48:36.550 --> 00:48:38.150
at least to me.

00:48:38.150 --> 00:48:39.870
I'm glad you mentioned
this thing about curcumin

00:48:39.870 --> 00:48:40.703
and black pepper.

00:48:40.703 --> 00:48:42.680
I wish we had had this
conversation six years ago,

00:48:42.680 --> 00:48:46.710
because I had the experience
of jumping on the bandwagon

00:48:46.710 --> 00:48:48.080
of the excitement around turmeric,

00:48:48.080 --> 00:48:49.650
and I took a turmeric supplement.

00:48:49.650 --> 00:48:52.800
It was a couple capsules
of what I thought to be,

00:48:52.800 --> 00:48:54.930
and I think was high quality turmeric,

00:48:54.930 --> 00:48:58.010
and I've never felt as poor as I did

00:48:58.010 --> 00:48:59.583
in the subsequent few days,

00:49:00.456 --> 00:49:02.020
flat line of, let's just say everything

00:49:02.020 --> 00:49:05.330
that one would want to have
in life, energy, vitality,

00:49:05.330 --> 00:49:07.530
just it was a cliff.

00:49:07.530 --> 00:49:12.250
And a friend somehow knew that curcumin

00:49:12.250 --> 00:49:13.790
could inhibit 5-alpha reductase.

00:49:13.790 --> 00:49:17.030
It converts to testosterone
to DHT, as you pointed out.

00:49:17.030 --> 00:49:17.960
I stopped taking it,

00:49:17.960 --> 00:49:21.210
it was the only new addition
to my diet and supplementation,

00:49:21.210 --> 00:49:23.610
and things bounced back
within about three, four days.

00:49:23.610 --> 00:49:25.870
But it was remarkable.

00:49:25.870 --> 00:49:27.380
I mean, I felt like garbage.

00:49:27.380 --> 00:49:28.720
And it was actually kind of frightening

00:49:28.720 --> 00:49:32.550
to experience the sharpness of that cliff.

00:49:32.550 --> 00:49:35.530
But I know that some people like turmeric

00:49:35.530 --> 00:49:39.440
for its antiinflammatory
properties, et cetera.

00:49:39.440 --> 00:49:41.943
Sounds like people either
need to experiment,

00:49:43.665 --> 00:49:44.498
and if they do,

00:49:44.498 --> 00:49:45.960
obviously to approach that with caution.

00:49:45.960 --> 00:49:47.470
Anytime you add or remove something,

00:49:47.470 --> 00:49:49.170
you need to talk to your doctor.

00:49:49.170 --> 00:49:51.840
You're a doctor, and I'm guessing that

00:49:51.840 --> 00:49:53.323
if one were to experiment,

00:49:54.580 --> 00:49:56.390
would you say that most of these effects

00:49:56.390 --> 00:49:59.230
of things like curcumin are
reversible as they were in me?

00:49:59.230 --> 00:50:01.840
Or is there any potential
of permanent damage

00:50:01.840 --> 00:50:04.090
if people have been taking
them for a long time?

00:50:04.090 --> 00:50:06.880
- The effects are nearly always reversible

00:50:06.880 --> 00:50:09.720
when you're talking about
5-alpha reductase inhibition,

00:50:09.720 --> 00:50:11.673
so what turmeric does, but stronger.

00:50:12.770 --> 00:50:15.370
The most common story
that we hear is regarding

00:50:15.370 --> 00:50:17.510
a supplement known as saw palmetto,

00:50:17.510 --> 00:50:19.060
which a lot of older men take

00:50:19.060 --> 00:50:21.730
for their prostate health or finasteride,

00:50:21.730 --> 00:50:23.130
which you can take for your prostate,

00:50:23.130 --> 00:50:26.240
or your heart, or your
hair, or dutasteride.

00:50:26.240 --> 00:50:28.770
So if you're having side effects on these,

00:50:28.770 --> 00:50:31.560
then it's probably because of
a couple different reasons.

00:50:31.560 --> 00:50:36.290
One can be your ratio of
androgens to estrogens is off,

00:50:36.290 --> 00:50:37.750
and that needs addressed.

00:50:37.750 --> 00:50:40.780
Another one can be it's
inhibiting the conversion

00:50:40.780 --> 00:50:44.220
of your progesterone to that
other type of progesterone,

00:50:44.220 --> 00:50:46.310
the 5-alpha, 3-alpha, that
we talked about earlier

00:50:46.310 --> 00:50:48.550
that's helping with your
sleep and your brain,

00:50:48.550 --> 00:50:50.100
and your calmness.

00:50:50.100 --> 00:50:54.000
And that's definitely an effect.

00:50:54.000 --> 00:50:57.930
Another one is depending on
the type of supplement or med,

00:50:57.930 --> 00:51:01.860
they inhibit different isoenzymes
of that 5-alpha reductase.

00:51:01.860 --> 00:51:05.700
So if they're just inhibiting one and two,

00:51:05.700 --> 00:51:07.440
then that's going to be
a different effect than

00:51:07.440 --> 00:51:09.270
if they're inhibiting two and three.

00:51:09.270 --> 00:51:11.400
So finasteride does two and three,

00:51:11.400 --> 00:51:12.570
saw palmetto does one and two,

00:51:12.570 --> 00:51:15.940
and then dutasteride does all three.

00:51:15.940 --> 00:51:18.020
The third one is active in the brain

00:51:18.020 --> 00:51:19.860
and dutasteride inhibits that third one

00:51:19.860 --> 00:51:22.070
a little bit weaker in vivo,

00:51:22.070 --> 00:51:23.860
but strongly in vitro.

00:51:23.860 --> 00:51:26.240
So it's really hard to parse out.

00:51:26.240 --> 00:51:28.850
You can use biofeedback
and experimentation.

00:51:28.850 --> 00:51:32.400
I do think with supplements
it's safe to experiment.

00:51:32.400 --> 00:51:34.300
The time that it takes to set in

00:51:34.300 --> 00:51:36.330
is usually about three months.

00:51:36.330 --> 00:51:39.380
So the risk of, and this is anecdotally,

00:51:39.380 --> 00:51:42.180
there's been lots of
research published about

00:51:42.180 --> 00:51:46.580
if post-finasteride
syndrome is real or fake.

00:51:46.580 --> 00:51:48.640
And it is real,

00:51:48.640 --> 00:51:49.730
but it's one of those things

00:51:49.730 --> 00:51:53.120
that's a combination of
organic and inorganic disease.

00:51:53.120 --> 00:51:56.370
Almost kind of like fibromyalgia
where it's definitely real,

00:51:56.370 --> 00:51:58.840
And there's lots of things that
you can do to help with it,

00:51:58.840 --> 00:52:01.350
but it's very unlikely to occur

00:52:01.350 --> 00:52:04.360
if you stop taking your
supplement or medication

00:52:04.360 --> 00:52:05.620
after you have side effects.

00:52:05.620 --> 00:52:07.550
- Interesting, well, I
certainly feel better

00:52:07.550 --> 00:52:10.490
when I'm taking five grams of
creatine monohydrate per day.

00:52:10.490 --> 00:52:12.590
I know most people take
it for muscle growth

00:52:12.590 --> 00:52:15.040
and tissue repair and things of that sort,

00:52:15.040 --> 00:52:17.480
mainly I think brings water
into the muscle tissue,

00:52:17.480 --> 00:52:20.010
et cetera, but I take it
for the brain effects,

00:52:20.010 --> 00:52:22.080
and also because I like
to think that it gives me

00:52:22.080 --> 00:52:26.400
a little bit of a DHT bump
that I can actually see in

00:52:26.400 --> 00:52:28.200
my blood charts when I've done them.

00:52:29.190 --> 00:52:33.250
I know many people want
to avoid the hair loss

00:52:33.250 --> 00:52:34.530
that can sometimes be associated

00:52:34.530 --> 00:52:36.540
with DHT levels going too high.

00:52:36.540 --> 00:52:38.150
And so I've been asked many times,

00:52:38.150 --> 00:52:40.780
does creatine monohydrate cause hair loss?

00:52:40.780 --> 00:52:43.426
It would make sense that
if creatine increases DHT

00:52:43.426 --> 00:52:46.340
and DHT binding to the androgen receptor

00:52:46.340 --> 00:52:47.830
on the scalp can induce hair loss,

00:52:47.830 --> 00:52:49.290
that that would be the case.

00:52:49.290 --> 00:52:50.750
Is that that true or

00:52:51.700 --> 00:52:53.810
are people just overly
concerned about something

00:52:53.810 --> 00:52:55.893
that's trivial or non-existent?

00:52:57.050 --> 00:53:01.180
- Each male and fem, so yes,
it can potentially add it.

00:53:01.180 --> 00:53:02.930
I don't like to say it causes it,

00:53:02.930 --> 00:53:06.210
but it can be a little
bit more fuel to the fire.

00:53:06.210 --> 00:53:08.830
So just like everybody has
a different sensitivity

00:53:08.830 --> 00:53:10.180
of their androgen receptor,

00:53:10.180 --> 00:53:13.310
they have a different
amount of gene transcription

00:53:13.310 --> 00:53:16.260
that is going to cause
death of the follicle.

00:53:16.260 --> 00:53:17.790
That's an arbitrary threshold.

00:53:17.790 --> 00:53:20.460
So you don't really know
until you start losing hair.

00:53:20.460 --> 00:53:23.300
- And if somebody takes
a little bit of creatine

00:53:23.300 --> 00:53:24.310
to increase their DHT,

00:53:24.310 --> 00:53:25.840
maybe for the cognitive enhancing effects,

00:53:25.840 --> 00:53:26.860
or for whatever reason,

00:53:26.860 --> 00:53:30.010
and they notice a bit more
hair falling out in the sink,

00:53:30.010 --> 00:53:32.030
and they stop taking it,

00:53:32.030 --> 00:53:35.033
you said death of the follicle,
which sounds very dramatic.

00:53:36.010 --> 00:53:37.540
Are those little stem cell niches

00:53:37.540 --> 00:53:40.340
that reside in the follicle,
which hairs grow from,

00:53:40.340 --> 00:53:41.380
are those then abolished,

00:53:41.380 --> 00:53:42.940
like there's no going back,

00:53:42.940 --> 00:53:45.380
or can one rescue at the hair?

00:53:45.380 --> 00:53:47.740
- It takes months, if they're still there,

00:53:47.740 --> 00:53:48.950
the hair will come back.

00:53:48.950 --> 00:53:52.250
So the loss of the hair itself

00:53:52.250 --> 00:53:54.480
is a normal part of the hair cycle.

00:53:54.480 --> 00:53:57.380
So you have your antigen
phase, your catagen phase,

00:53:57.380 --> 00:54:00.070
your telogen phase, and
then your hair loss,

00:54:00.070 --> 00:54:01.746
and then a new follow.
- Of the stem cell niche

00:54:01.746 --> 00:54:03.380
in the hair follicle.
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:54:03.380 --> 00:54:05.240
Think of it like sharks have teeth.

00:54:05.240 --> 00:54:06.650
So shark loses a tooth,

00:54:06.650 --> 00:54:08.350
and they have a new
one that comes through.

00:54:08.350 --> 00:54:10.170
Or losing your baby tooth,
and you have a new one,

00:54:10.170 --> 00:54:12.010
but your hair just always
keeps coming through.

00:54:12.010 --> 00:54:15.180
So it's natural for it to die and lose.

00:54:15.180 --> 00:54:17.300
That's that's why when you start

00:54:17.300 --> 00:54:18.750
5-alpha reductase inhibitors,

00:54:18.750 --> 00:54:20.430
often you have a big shed.

00:54:20.430 --> 00:54:22.520
So what happens during that big shed

00:54:22.520 --> 00:54:26.180
is all of these cells that are unhealthy,

00:54:26.180 --> 00:54:27.100
they immediately jettison that hair

00:54:27.100 --> 00:54:30.830
and then they start making a
much healthier new follicle.

00:54:30.830 --> 00:54:32.560
So a lot of the hairs that are

00:54:32.560 --> 00:54:36.560
at the end of their telogen phase,

00:54:36.560 --> 00:54:39.570
then they have what's
called telogen effluvium,

00:54:39.570 --> 00:54:41.780
which also happens after pregnancy,

00:54:41.780 --> 00:54:44.730
also happens in thyroid pathologies.

00:54:44.730 --> 00:54:46.730
So you shed it, a new one in place,

00:54:46.730 --> 00:54:47.950
and you think that you're having

00:54:47.950 --> 00:54:51.011
a horrible hair loss
caused by your finasteride

00:54:51.011 --> 00:54:52.980
or whatever you're doing.

00:54:52.980 --> 00:54:54.750
And minoxidil does this too,

00:54:54.750 --> 00:54:57.600
but you're really just having
a new, healthier follicle.

00:54:57.600 --> 00:55:00.280
If you go a really long
time, if you go a year,

00:55:00.280 --> 00:55:03.100
then those hairs might come
back, and they might not.

00:55:03.100 --> 00:55:07.010
- So for simplicity's sake, if
somebody is concerned about,

00:55:07.010 --> 00:55:09.440
or is experiencing hair
loss, male or female,

00:55:09.440 --> 00:55:14.440
what are their options of
ways to offset that hair loss

00:55:15.260 --> 00:55:18.360
that are not going to negatively impact

00:55:18.360 --> 00:55:20.130
other tissues sensitive to DHT?

00:55:20.130 --> 00:55:22.490
And what I'm basically saying here is,

00:55:22.490 --> 00:55:26.740
I could imagine taking a DHT inhibitor,

00:55:26.740 --> 00:55:27.850
a pill of some sort,

00:55:27.850 --> 00:55:31.980
or an injection of some sort,
and offsetting hair loss,

00:55:31.980 --> 00:55:34.100
maybe even stimulate more hair growth.

00:55:34.100 --> 00:55:35.530
It's clear that I'm not doing that,

00:55:35.530 --> 00:55:36.810
but I know people that do,

00:55:36.810 --> 00:55:39.280
but then experience some of
the other negative effects

00:55:39.280 --> 00:55:41.870
of blunting DHT, reduced
affect, reduced libido,

00:55:41.870 --> 00:55:45.840
reduced drive, disruptions
in prostate function,

00:55:45.840 --> 00:55:48.660
or even sexual function generally.

00:55:48.660 --> 00:55:51.330
So what can people do
if they want to maintain

00:55:51.330 --> 00:55:52.163
or grow back hair,

00:55:52.163 --> 00:55:54.310
but they don't want all
those other effects?

00:55:54.310 --> 00:55:56.030
What should they avoid

00:55:56.030 --> 00:55:58.360
and what should they
perhaps consider talking

00:55:58.360 --> 00:55:59.980
to their doctor about?

00:55:59.980 --> 00:56:01.980
- Yeah, there's a whole host of options.

00:56:03.608 --> 00:56:06.080
I try to separate alopecia or hair loss

00:56:06.080 --> 00:56:08.640
into two different categories,
male pattern baldness,

00:56:08.640 --> 00:56:10.510
or androgenic alopecia,

00:56:10.510 --> 00:56:13.440
also known as androgenetic alopecia,

00:56:13.440 --> 00:56:17.710
versus other types of alopecia,
usually telogen effluvium.

00:56:17.710 --> 00:56:20.990
And if it's androgenetic alopecia

00:56:20.990 --> 00:56:23.750
or male pattern baldness,
even if they're female,

00:56:23.750 --> 00:56:26.020
perhaps say PCOS, something like that,

00:56:26.020 --> 00:56:30.440
then you want some sort of
strategy to decrease the activity

00:56:30.440 --> 00:56:31.690
of that androgen receptor.

00:56:31.690 --> 00:56:33.830
- So women can get male pattern baldness?

00:56:33.830 --> 00:56:34.663
- [Kyle] Absolutely.

00:56:34.663 --> 00:56:35.950
- Okay, I'm going to have to wrap my head

00:56:35.950 --> 00:56:37.760
around that one, but okay.

00:56:37.760 --> 00:56:40.920
- So there's a lot of different
things that you can do

00:56:40.920 --> 00:56:41.780
that are topical.

00:56:41.780 --> 00:56:45.090
The most promising is called
dutasteride mesotherapy.

00:56:45.090 --> 00:56:46.480
Essentially what it is

00:56:46.480 --> 00:56:49.430
is it's very localized injections in areas

00:56:49.430 --> 00:56:52.050
that are prone to male pattern baldness,

00:56:52.050 --> 00:56:54.350
whether they're female or male.

00:56:54.350 --> 00:56:57.350
And it acts locally only.

00:56:57.350 --> 00:56:59.970
And you repeat these
injections from time to time,

00:56:59.970 --> 00:57:03.020
it decreases the conversion
of testosterone to DHT

00:57:03.020 --> 00:57:04.930
just in the scalp.

00:57:04.930 --> 00:57:06.870
- So that can avoid prostate effects.

00:57:06.870 --> 00:57:08.510
And what are some of the negative effects

00:57:08.510 --> 00:57:12.720
of blocking D HT in
females, in the periphery?

00:57:12.720 --> 00:57:15.310
Meaning not on the scalp or in the brain?

00:57:15.310 --> 00:57:18.720
Where is DHT doing its stuff?

00:57:18.720 --> 00:57:20.270
- Yeah, so it's both DHT,

00:57:20.270 --> 00:57:23.530
and then also that 5-alpha,
3-alpha progesterone,

00:57:23.530 --> 00:57:27.520
which is called THP or dihydroprogesterone

00:57:27.520 --> 00:57:30.770
or tetrahydro, trihydroprogesterone.

00:57:30.770 --> 00:57:33.560
So they're active in the
central nervous system,

00:57:33.560 --> 00:57:36.250
but it's also just active, again,

00:57:36.250 --> 00:57:39.280
binding to the androgen
receptor in a female as well,

00:57:39.280 --> 00:57:42.550
causing them to have that
effort feel good, motivation.

00:57:42.550 --> 00:57:45.790
A lot of women that are sensitive to DHT,

00:57:45.790 --> 00:57:48.370
'cause women can be
sensitive to DHT as well,

00:57:48.370 --> 00:57:52.490
feel very different when they
start an oral contraceptive,

00:57:52.490 --> 00:57:55.860
not because it alters
their DHT to a huge amount.

00:57:55.860 --> 00:57:57.660
It does to some degree.

00:57:57.660 --> 00:57:59.700
Because the negative feedback inhibition

00:57:59.700 --> 00:58:02.350
in the pituitary and less
produced in the ovaries,

00:58:02.350 --> 00:58:05.713
but it increases SHBG really high.

00:58:06.610 --> 00:58:09.650
So because their SHBGs
are significantly higher,

00:58:09.650 --> 00:58:12.413
their free DHT is way lower.

00:58:12.413 --> 00:58:16.240
- I see, how does a woman
know if she has PCOS,

00:58:16.240 --> 00:58:18.160
polycystic ovarian syndrome?

00:58:18.160 --> 00:58:20.870
What are the issues with
polycystic ovarian syndrome?

00:58:20.870 --> 00:58:22.640
What can be done about PCOS?

00:58:22.640 --> 00:58:24.373
I confess, I was naive to PCOS.

00:58:26.420 --> 00:58:28.870
That wasn't supposed to
rhyme, but since it does,

00:58:28.870 --> 00:58:32.057
I do confess I was completely naive to it.

00:58:32.057 --> 00:58:33.920
And I started getting a
lot of questions about it

00:58:33.920 --> 00:58:35.350
in various forums.

00:58:35.350 --> 00:58:37.810
And I think that's actually the reason

00:58:37.810 --> 00:58:39.350
why I initially approached you.

00:58:39.350 --> 00:58:42.313
I know you have treated a lot of PCOS.

00:58:43.290 --> 00:58:48.150
What age women should be
about PCOS, what's PCOS?

00:58:48.150 --> 00:58:49.620
Teach us about PCOS, please.

00:58:49.620 --> 00:58:54.120
- Yeah, so PCOS is
polycystic ovarian syndrome.

00:58:54.120 --> 00:58:56.270
And this is one of those conditions

00:58:56.270 --> 00:58:58.650
which is underdiagnosed.

00:58:58.650 --> 00:59:02.600
So its prevalence is much
higher than we think it is.

00:59:02.600 --> 00:59:03.917
There's been a lot of studies.

00:59:03.917 --> 00:59:08.490
And some studies say a
prevalence of 10%, some say 20%.

00:59:08.490 --> 00:59:10.840
It's not completely clinically penetrant.

00:59:10.840 --> 00:59:13.110
So most people don't know they have PCOS

00:59:13.110 --> 00:59:16.230
until they have infertility
or subfertility.

00:59:16.230 --> 00:59:18.470
- And is PCOS happening at this frequency

00:59:18.470 --> 00:59:20.880
in 20-year old women,
in 30-year old women,

00:59:20.880 --> 00:59:22.100
in 40 and onward?

00:59:22.100 --> 00:59:25.500
- Most women find out they
have PCOS in their 30s,

00:59:25.500 --> 00:59:28.280
especially, it's on a
spectrum or a continuum,

00:59:28.280 --> 00:59:30.700
like a lot of things, where
you can have a weaker version,

00:59:30.700 --> 00:59:32.070
or a very severe version.

00:59:32.070 --> 00:59:33.910
- What are the symptoms?

00:59:33.910 --> 00:59:37.530
- There's criteria called
the Rotterdam criteria.

00:59:37.530 --> 00:59:39.050
And in the Rotterdam criteria,

00:59:39.050 --> 00:59:41.390
there's a couple different
ways that you can diagnose it.

00:59:41.390 --> 00:59:45.940
You're looking for androgen
excess, insulin resistance,

00:59:45.940 --> 00:59:47.900
and you could also look
for polycystic ovaries.

00:59:47.900 --> 00:59:50.200
You don't actually have to
have polycystic ovaries or

00:59:50.200 --> 00:59:53.270
to get an ultrasound of your
ovaries to be diagnosed.

00:59:53.270 --> 00:59:55.945
If you have androgen excess, for example,

00:59:55.945 --> 00:59:58.500
androgenic acne, or hormonal acne.

00:59:58.500 --> 00:59:59.490
If you have hair growth,

00:59:59.490 --> 01:00:02.820
like a hair growth on the
chin, it's called hirsutism.

01:00:02.820 --> 01:00:04.810
Or if you have,

01:00:04.810 --> 01:00:06.543
like deepening of the voice,

01:00:08.010 --> 01:00:09.680
any symptom of too much.

01:00:09.680 --> 01:00:12.250
And male pattern baldness,
if you're female,

01:00:12.250 --> 01:00:14.503
that's a symptom of PCOS as well.

01:00:15.560 --> 01:00:17.210
Then you can also have insulin resistance.

01:00:17.210 --> 01:00:19.260
So this is obesity.

01:00:19.260 --> 01:00:22.430
It's pre-diabetes, a high fasting insulin,

01:00:22.430 --> 01:00:24.670
a HOMA-IR over two,

01:00:24.670 --> 01:00:27.290
a fasting insulin of over six.

01:00:27.290 --> 01:00:30.570
So if you have significant
insulin resistance

01:00:30.570 --> 01:00:34.950
and also androgen dominance,
that's a sign of it.

01:00:34.950 --> 01:00:36.450
Androgen dominance often leads

01:00:36.450 --> 01:00:38.730
to what's called oligomenorrhea.

01:00:38.730 --> 01:00:42.170
So if you're having more
than 35-day intervals

01:00:42.170 --> 01:00:47.170
in between a period or if you
have less than nine per year,

01:00:47.780 --> 01:00:50.020
then that can be a sign
that you have oligo,

01:00:50.020 --> 01:00:53.493
which means too little,
menorrhea which means menses.

01:00:54.410 --> 01:00:56.623
So that's a very common sign of PCOS.

01:00:58.060 --> 01:00:59.290
If you have infertility,

01:00:59.290 --> 01:01:02.190
so if you're under the age
of 35 and you've been trying

01:01:02.190 --> 01:01:05.570
for more than a year, or if
you're over the age of 35,

01:01:05.570 --> 01:01:07.840
and you've been trying
for more than six months,

01:01:07.840 --> 01:01:08.850
then that can also be,

01:01:08.850 --> 01:01:10.760
it's a very common presenting complaint

01:01:10.760 --> 01:01:12.850
when somebody presents with PCOS.

01:01:12.850 --> 01:01:15.800
- And assuming that a woman is doing

01:01:15.800 --> 01:01:17.350
all these other things is paying attention

01:01:17.350 --> 01:01:19.430
to the six pillars that
you talked about earlier,

01:01:19.430 --> 01:01:22.020
diet, exercise, caloric
restriction, in some cases, right?

01:01:22.020 --> 01:01:24.450
Not everyone needs to
be caloric restricted.

01:01:24.450 --> 01:01:27.550
Stress, sleep, and sunlight, spirit.

01:01:27.550 --> 01:01:30.360
Assuming that they're
doing all those things,

01:01:30.360 --> 01:01:32.480
what other things in the realm of diet

01:01:32.480 --> 01:01:35.140
or supplementation can
help them avoid PCOS

01:01:35.140 --> 01:01:37.480
if they have subclinical PCOS

01:01:37.480 --> 01:01:39.450
or they have not developed it,

01:01:39.450 --> 01:01:40.540
but don't want to develop it?

01:01:40.540 --> 01:01:42.820
'Cause it doesn't sound like a good thing.

01:01:42.820 --> 01:01:45.540
- Yeah, so depending on where they are,

01:01:45.540 --> 01:01:49.350
if they're very strong on the
insulin resistance spectrum,

01:01:49.350 --> 01:01:52.360
then optimizing their body composition,

01:01:52.360 --> 01:01:53.820
decreasing their body fat,

01:01:53.820 --> 01:01:56.690
and treating that metabolic
syndrome can help.

01:01:56.690 --> 01:01:58.970
So a lot of people ask,

01:01:58.970 --> 01:02:00.573
well, does everybody that's on,

01:02:01.600 --> 01:02:04.160
like does everybody need to
be on metformin that has PCOS?

01:02:04.160 --> 01:02:06.890
Not necessarily, but
metformin is one of the tools

01:02:06.890 --> 01:02:10.070
that can help with insulin sensitization.

01:02:10.070 --> 01:02:12.870
Other tools that can help are inositol,

01:02:12.870 --> 01:02:16.240
so myo-inositol is an insulin sensitizer.

01:02:16.240 --> 01:02:21.209
Its cousin D-chiro-inositol is

01:02:21.209 --> 01:02:22.730
a weak antiandrogen.

01:02:22.730 --> 01:02:26.800
A lot of types of inositol
have both of those in it.

01:02:26.800 --> 01:02:29.930
So depending on if
you're a female or a male

01:02:29.930 --> 01:02:33.460
and you're on inositol, the
type of inositol does matter.

01:02:33.460 --> 01:02:35.610
- Yeah, this is a very important point.

01:02:35.610 --> 01:02:37.800
Just today I said I'm trying this new

01:02:39.520 --> 01:02:42.680
supplement inositol for its role in

01:02:43.570 --> 01:02:45.450
perhaps enhancing sleep even further.

01:02:45.450 --> 01:02:46.760
My sleep's generally pretty good.

01:02:46.760 --> 01:02:48.620
Lately it's been a little bit
off for a number of reasons.

01:02:48.620 --> 01:02:50.620
So I took it for the
first time last night,

01:02:50.620 --> 01:02:53.080
and I said, I thought it helped,

01:02:53.080 --> 01:02:55.317
and just subjectively, and you said,

01:02:55.317 --> 01:02:56.990
"What kind of inositol is it,

01:02:56.990 --> 01:03:00.190
because inositol is a very
potent androgen inhibitor.

01:03:00.190 --> 01:03:02.600
It turns out I was taking myo-inositol,

01:03:02.600 --> 01:03:05.023
which is not an androgen inhibitor.

01:03:06.027 --> 01:03:07.000
The other type that you mentioned,

01:03:07.000 --> 01:03:09.300
which is an androgen inhibitor is?

01:03:09.300 --> 01:03:11.280
- D-chiro-inositol.

01:03:11.280 --> 01:03:15.390
It's usually in a ratio
of 1 to 25 or 1 to 40,

01:03:15.390 --> 01:03:18.560
in a much lower amount
compared to myo-inositol.

01:03:18.560 --> 01:03:20.150
- In a supplement or in the body?

01:03:20.150 --> 01:03:23.390
- In a supplement to
help induce ovulation.

01:03:23.390 --> 01:03:26.370
- But for women who
have PCOS who might want

01:03:26.370 --> 01:03:28.550
to try and reduce androgen,

01:03:28.550 --> 01:03:32.630
then they would perhaps want
to take a form of inositol

01:03:32.630 --> 01:03:34.640
that reduce the androgen
receptor activity.

01:03:34.640 --> 01:03:35.970
Correct?
- Yeah. They want both.

01:03:35.970 --> 01:03:37.530
So if you're a woman
and you've ever talked

01:03:37.530 --> 01:03:40.810
to your doctor about getting
on the oral contraceptive

01:03:40.810 --> 01:03:43.700
or spironolactone, which
is also an anti-androgen,

01:03:43.700 --> 01:03:46.650
but it happens to be a
potassium-sparing diuretic

01:03:46.650 --> 01:03:48.250
blood pressure medicine as well.

01:03:49.150 --> 01:03:51.810
D-chiro-inositol might be a better option.

01:03:51.810 --> 01:03:55.420
DIM or diindolylmethane is another kind

01:03:55.420 --> 01:03:56.310
of weak antiestrogen,

01:03:56.310 --> 01:04:00.260
antiandrogen that a lot of
women should consider as well.

01:04:00.260 --> 01:04:02.710
- You mentioned oral contraception.

01:04:02.710 --> 01:04:06.180
I've done a few posts on these.

01:04:06.180 --> 01:04:07.130
Let's just call them,

01:04:07.130 --> 01:04:09.810
they really are perceptual effects whereby

01:04:09.810 --> 01:04:12.100
it's been demonstrated in
humans several times now,

01:04:12.100 --> 01:04:14.800
and what appeared to me
to be very solid studies

01:04:14.800 --> 01:04:19.240
where women that take oral contraceptives,

01:04:19.240 --> 01:04:23.330
there is both a shift in
their perception of men,

01:04:23.330 --> 01:04:25.913
'cause these studies only
looked at heterosexual,

01:04:27.050 --> 01:04:28.793
the sort of arrangements here,

01:04:30.050 --> 01:04:32.730
where women who are on oral contraception,

01:04:32.730 --> 01:04:35.230
because it blunts some
of the peaks and valleys

01:04:35.230 --> 01:04:37.803
of hormone output,

01:04:39.060 --> 01:04:42.500
no longer experience the
same peak and valleys

01:04:42.500 --> 01:04:44.680
in their assessment of
other men's attractiveness.

01:04:44.680 --> 01:04:47.800
So it sort of flattens their
perception, so to speak.

01:04:47.800 --> 01:04:49.520
They still find certain men attractive

01:04:49.520 --> 01:04:50.530
and certain men unattractive,

01:04:50.530 --> 01:04:55.530
but the degree of difference
is kind of mellowed out.

01:04:56.140 --> 01:04:58.140
And likewise, men,

01:04:58.140 --> 01:05:03.140
these data say that men
perceiving women's attractiveness,

01:05:04.740 --> 01:05:07.890
they still see women on oral
contraceptives as attractive,

01:05:07.890 --> 01:05:12.280
but a woman taking oral
contraception eliminates

01:05:12.280 --> 01:05:14.510
this kind of peak in her attractiveness

01:05:14.510 --> 01:05:16.200
that men would otherwise perceive.

01:05:16.200 --> 01:05:17.970
In other words, oral
contraceptives are changing

01:05:17.970 --> 01:05:19.480
the way that we perceive each other,

01:05:19.480 --> 01:05:23.460
at least in terms of these
male/female experiments.

01:05:23.460 --> 01:05:25.530
What is going on with that?

01:05:25.530 --> 01:05:27.593
Is that because oral contraceptives,

01:05:28.620 --> 01:05:31.080
blunt the increase in
testosterone that occurs

01:05:31.080 --> 01:05:33.010
just before ovulation,

01:05:33.010 --> 01:05:35.240
or is it because of a complex cascade?

01:05:35.240 --> 01:05:37.250
What is going on? I find this fascinating.

01:05:37.250 --> 01:05:41.160
- Yeah, so there's
differences in how your,

01:05:41.160 --> 01:05:43.750
and I wouldn't use the
word change necessarily,

01:05:43.750 --> 01:05:47.810
but alter the severity or alter the

01:05:48.680 --> 01:05:50.260
peak, as you said.

01:05:50.260 --> 01:05:53.580
So just like TRT is not going
to change you as a person,

01:05:53.580 --> 01:05:56.520
an oral contraceptive will
not change you as a person.

01:05:56.520 --> 01:06:01.350
It will just change your day
to day peaks and troughs in

01:06:03.530 --> 01:06:06.420
libido and attractiveness.

01:06:06.420 --> 01:06:09.260
So one of the main effects
of oral contraceptives,

01:06:09.260 --> 01:06:11.640
almost all of them have
a synthetic estrogen

01:06:11.640 --> 01:06:14.230
and a synthetic progestogen in them.

01:06:14.230 --> 01:06:17.213
One common type of synthetic
estrogen is ethanol estradiol.

01:06:18.120 --> 01:06:20.430
There is another new synthetic estrogen

01:06:20.430 --> 01:06:22.580
that's out there as well,
but that anecdotally,

01:06:22.580 --> 01:06:24.840
that seems to have even more side effects.

01:06:24.840 --> 01:06:29.250
So this ethanol estradiol
is 100 times more potent

01:06:29.250 --> 01:06:33.330
than endogenous or bioidentical
estradiol in the liver.

01:06:33.330 --> 01:06:36.570
So it binds to the estrogen
receptor in the liver,

01:06:36.570 --> 01:06:39.740
and it's going to increase
sex hormone-binding globulin,

01:06:39.740 --> 01:06:41.660
which secondarily, as you mentioned,

01:06:41.660 --> 01:06:43.920
decreases your free testosterone,

01:06:43.920 --> 01:06:46.390
and especially your free DHT.

01:06:46.390 --> 01:06:49.260
So that little testosterone
hump that you get

01:06:49.260 --> 01:06:51.290
when you're a female that's ovulating,

01:06:51.290 --> 01:06:53.930
that's really flatlined and

01:06:53.930 --> 01:06:56.920
it's a pretty insignificant difference.

01:06:56.920 --> 01:06:58.010
It's not negligible,

01:06:58.010 --> 01:06:59.810
but it's a little bit of a hump

01:06:59.810 --> 01:07:01.840
and you have significantly less

01:07:01.840 --> 01:07:03.800
of that when you're on
a oral contraceptive.

01:07:03.800 --> 01:07:06.330
- And does that blunt the
associated increase in libido

01:07:06.330 --> 01:07:10.050
that normally would occur from
that increase in androgen?

01:07:10.050 --> 01:07:11.597
- Yes.
- Yeah. Interesting.

01:07:11.597 --> 01:07:13.830
And what about other forms
of contraception, right?

01:07:13.830 --> 01:07:16.160
'Cause there are, there's copper IUD,

01:07:16.160 --> 01:07:18.570
there's various implants.

01:07:18.570 --> 01:07:20.960
There's rings, there's a huge number

01:07:20.960 --> 01:07:23.420
of different forms of these.

01:07:23.420 --> 01:07:26.130
So what we're talking
about is, as I understand,

01:07:26.130 --> 01:07:28.010
it is only the effect of

01:07:29.650 --> 01:07:33.140
oral contraception that
impacts hormone output.

01:07:33.140 --> 01:07:33.973
Is that correct?

01:07:33.973 --> 01:07:35.830
- Yeah, there's a lot of
other effects as well.

01:07:35.830 --> 01:07:39.360
For example, your choice
of synthetic progestin

01:07:39.360 --> 01:07:43.030
will alter how high your
platelets and SHBG go.

01:07:43.030 --> 01:07:46.530
It appears to be the higher your platelets

01:07:46.530 --> 01:07:48.260
and the higher your SHBG,

01:07:48.260 --> 01:07:50.170
the your higher risk of a blood clot.

01:07:50.170 --> 01:07:52.240
So a lot of women know that if they're

01:07:52.240 --> 01:07:53.460
on a oral contraceptive

01:07:53.460 --> 01:07:56.100
and they're already
predisposed to a blood clot

01:07:56.100 --> 01:07:58.370
or a venous thromboembolism,

01:07:58.370 --> 01:07:59.760
in their vein they have a blood clot

01:07:59.760 --> 01:08:01.600
in either their leg, or their lung,

01:08:01.600 --> 01:08:03.900
then it can increase that chance.

01:08:03.900 --> 01:08:07.830
So you can choose a synthetic
progestin that is not going

01:08:07.830 --> 01:08:10.313
to have as high of a response,

01:08:11.440 --> 01:08:13.050
but there's various pros and cons.

01:08:13.050 --> 01:08:16.900
Some synthetic progestins are
weak anti-androgens as well.

01:08:16.900 --> 01:08:19.290
For example, there's one known as Slynd,

01:08:19.290 --> 01:08:21.690
which is made from spironolactone.

01:08:21.690 --> 01:08:26.170
So some women are on
spironolactone and that as well,

01:08:26.170 --> 01:08:27.350
which is made from spironolactone,

01:08:27.350 --> 01:08:29.670
which probably isn't
particularly necessary

01:08:29.670 --> 01:08:32.350
unless they need it for a
diuretic or a hypertensive effect.

01:08:32.350 --> 01:08:35.220
- I see, I'm just going to
intentionally interrupt,

01:08:35.220 --> 01:08:36.080
and I apologize,

01:08:36.080 --> 01:08:39.483
but specifically because
I wanted to ask about,

01:08:40.850 --> 01:08:42.160
there is this notion

01:08:44.020 --> 01:08:46.860
that oral contraception taken
over long periods of time

01:08:46.860 --> 01:08:50.080
can disrupt fertility in
ways that are independent

01:08:50.080 --> 01:08:54.560
of just the age-related
decrease in fertility.

01:08:54.560 --> 01:08:56.160
Is that true?

01:08:56.160 --> 01:08:58.100
- It depends on what
you mean by a long time.

01:08:58.100 --> 01:09:00.460
6 to 12 months, it's possible.

01:09:00.460 --> 01:09:03.580
Past that, it seems very unlikely.

01:09:03.580 --> 01:09:06.970
However, the persistently elevated SHBG

01:09:06.970 --> 01:09:08.780
can be present for quite some time.

01:09:08.780 --> 01:09:11.300
- Wait, so if a woman
takes oral contraception

01:09:11.300 --> 01:09:13.790
for 6 to 12 months and then stops,

01:09:13.790 --> 01:09:17.460
will she essentially be aware
she would've been anyway

01:09:17.460 --> 01:09:19.830
in terms of her fertility at that age?

01:09:19.830 --> 01:09:22.910
Or are you saying that it
can cause permanent damage?

01:09:22.910 --> 01:09:25.370
- Her fertility would be equitable

01:09:25.370 --> 01:09:28.670
as if she had never taken it
if she's certainly 12 months,

01:09:28.670 --> 01:09:29.607
but probably six months off.

01:09:29.607 --> 01:09:30.970
- And what if she...

01:09:30.970 --> 01:09:32.850
I know of women that have
taken an oral contraception

01:09:32.850 --> 01:09:36.480
for many years are, in addition
to the age-related decline

01:09:36.480 --> 01:09:39.320
in fertility that occurs
that's inevitable,

01:09:39.320 --> 01:09:41.150
of course the slope is going
to be different depending

01:09:41.150 --> 01:09:42.650
on the individual,

01:09:42.650 --> 01:09:45.540
but are they

01:09:45.540 --> 01:09:50.540
quickening the transition to infertility?

01:09:50.610 --> 01:09:54.340
- Probably not, you could make a case that

01:09:54.340 --> 01:09:56.980
because they've been on
a oral contraceptive,

01:09:56.980 --> 01:09:59.800
they may have been
slightly more predisposed

01:09:59.800 --> 01:10:04.800
to insulin resistance
and/or lower lean body mass.

01:10:06.060 --> 01:10:08.870
But that's probably going to
be a negligible difference

01:10:08.870 --> 01:10:10.490
compared to their resistance training

01:10:10.490 --> 01:10:12.200
and also their caloric restriction

01:10:12.200 --> 01:10:13.647
or caloric maintenance so-

01:10:13.647 --> 01:10:16.180
- And of course there are also
effects of having children.

01:10:16.180 --> 01:10:17.013
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

01:10:17.013 --> 01:10:18.930
Right, I mean on all
these parameters, right?

01:10:18.930 --> 01:10:21.853
'Cause it's a major
lifestyle shift, right?

01:10:23.180 --> 01:10:25.380
That obviously people contend with

01:10:25.380 --> 01:10:29.133
and have since the beginning
of human time anyway.

01:10:30.990 --> 01:10:34.180
I want to ask some questions
about male hormone therapy

01:10:34.180 --> 01:10:35.330
and male hormones generally.

01:10:35.330 --> 01:10:36.340
But before I do that,

01:10:36.340 --> 01:10:38.700
I have a couple of burning questions

01:10:38.700 --> 01:10:41.393
that I get very often that
I'm just going to insert now.

01:10:43.100 --> 01:10:47.660
Marijuana, I've heard that
it can decrease testosterone

01:10:47.660 --> 01:10:48.820
in men and women.

01:10:48.820 --> 01:10:51.990
I've heard that it can
increase testosterone.

01:10:51.990 --> 01:10:54.870
Alcohol, I think there's general consensus

01:10:54.870 --> 01:10:58.040
that high alcohol intake,

01:10:58.040 --> 01:11:01.780
high barbiturate intake does
in fact reduce testosterone.

01:11:01.780 --> 01:11:03.710
What about modest increase of alcohol?

01:11:03.710 --> 01:11:06.020
I'm not a drinker, so I'm not
asking these questions for me.

01:11:06.020 --> 01:11:07.393
I don't smoke pot, and whatever.

01:11:07.393 --> 01:11:10.070
I just never really liked
marijuana or alcohol.

01:11:10.070 --> 01:11:11.170
They're not my thing.

01:11:11.170 --> 01:11:14.190
But many people want to
know the answers to these.

01:11:14.190 --> 01:11:17.150
And the data that I've
seen are very confused

01:11:17.150 --> 01:11:19.300
and conflicting, so what about marijuana,

01:11:19.300 --> 01:11:23.430
does it reduce testosterone to
a significant degree or not?

01:11:23.430 --> 01:11:27.240
- Cannabinoids itself,
whether it's THC or CBD,

01:11:27.240 --> 01:11:30.710
are not going to reduce
testosterone by themself.

01:11:30.710 --> 01:11:32.940
If it's smoked marijuana,

01:11:32.940 --> 01:11:36.630
then it's very likely to
increase your aromatase,

01:11:36.630 --> 01:11:39.310
which increases your estrogen.

01:11:39.310 --> 01:11:41.810
And that's going to,

01:11:41.810 --> 01:11:43.360
it's aromatizing from testosterone.

01:11:43.360 --> 01:11:45.770
So that is going to decrease testosterone.

01:11:45.770 --> 01:11:49.280
When you have an increased
estrogen, like estradiol,

01:11:49.280 --> 01:11:51.060
that's going to work on your pituitary

01:11:51.060 --> 01:11:55.280
to make less hormones that
cause release of testosterone.

01:11:55.280 --> 01:11:58.900
So you're going to have
less LH and less FSH.

01:11:58.900 --> 01:12:00.960
So it's almost kind of like

01:12:00.960 --> 01:12:03.550
opiates are well known to,

01:12:03.550 --> 01:12:08.370
opiate agonists, they're
going to decrease LH and FSH

01:12:08.370 --> 01:12:09.900
and subsequently testosterone.

01:12:09.900 --> 01:12:12.560
Smoked marijuana will as well.

01:12:12.560 --> 01:12:13.870
As far as alcohol,

01:12:13.870 --> 01:12:15.840
high alcohol will decrease testosterone

01:12:15.840 --> 01:12:19.200
as will any very potent GABA agonist,

01:12:19.200 --> 01:12:20.490
whether it's a barbiturate,

01:12:20.490 --> 01:12:23.240
or benzodiazepine, or
a non-benzo or alcohol,

01:12:23.240 --> 01:12:25.410
they're definitely going to.

01:12:25.410 --> 01:12:28.110
Moderate alcohol, I guess it
depends on what your definition

01:12:28.110 --> 01:12:28.943
of that is.

01:12:28.943 --> 01:12:31.340
The American Heart-
- I guess I'm thinking like,

01:12:31.340 --> 01:12:33.990
some people I know that
don't seem to be alcoholics,

01:12:33.990 --> 01:12:36.690
at least by my assessment,

01:12:36.690 --> 01:12:40.920
will have a glass or two
of wine four nights a week,

01:12:40.920 --> 01:12:43.640
which to me seems like
a tremendous amount,

01:12:43.640 --> 01:12:46.070
only because I don't like alcohol.

01:12:46.070 --> 01:12:48.090
I don't have a problem with
other people liking alcohol,

01:12:48.090 --> 01:12:51.680
but I think for many people
that would be considered low

01:12:51.680 --> 01:12:52.780
or moderate intake.

01:12:52.780 --> 01:12:55.580
- Yeah, I would consider that low intake.

01:12:55.580 --> 01:12:59.400
The American Heart
Association for men recommends

01:12:59.400 --> 01:13:02.260
between one and two
drinks a day on average.

01:13:02.260 --> 01:13:03.500
- They recommend it?
- So around, yeah.

01:13:03.500 --> 01:13:04.340
So around one per week.

01:13:04.340 --> 01:13:06.370
- Wait, so I'm making
my heart less healthy

01:13:06.370 --> 01:13:07.730
by not drinking alcohol.

01:13:07.730 --> 01:13:10.510
- Yeah, they recommend a very low amount

01:13:10.510 --> 01:13:12.260
of alcohol intake for men.

01:13:12.260 --> 01:13:14.760
For women, they recommend zero to one.

01:13:14.760 --> 01:13:17.223
So that's kind of hard to
interpret, zero to one.

01:13:18.250 --> 01:13:20.460
But the protective effect of alcohol,

01:13:20.460 --> 01:13:22.080
especially if it's a red wine

01:13:23.150 --> 01:13:25.370
with polyphenols in it,

01:13:25.370 --> 01:13:28.440
outweighs the deleterious effect.

01:13:28.440 --> 01:13:30.200
- Interesting, 'cause I've
seen some studies that point

01:13:30.200 --> 01:13:34.540
to the idea that even
low intake of alcohol

01:13:34.540 --> 01:13:35.670
over a prolonged period of time

01:13:35.670 --> 01:13:37.950
might actually decrease brain volume

01:13:37.950 --> 01:13:39.870
or at least volume of
particular brain areas.

01:13:39.870 --> 01:13:41.160
But of course we don't
know the consequence

01:13:41.160 --> 01:13:44.290
of decreasing the volume of
a given brain area either.

01:13:44.290 --> 01:13:46.220
I mean, one can imagine
it's decreasing the size

01:13:46.220 --> 01:13:47.880
of one's amygdala and
making them less stressed.

01:13:47.880 --> 01:13:49.670
Although there's no
evidence to support that.

01:13:49.670 --> 01:13:52.170
I've been told that I need
to drink many, many times,

01:13:52.170 --> 01:13:54.610
but I always reply that I
don't need to drink anything

01:13:54.610 --> 01:13:55.810
in order to speak my mind.

01:13:55.810 --> 01:13:59.010
So again, individual differences.

01:13:59.010 --> 01:14:02.170
Very interesting, so it sounds
like smoked marijuana may

01:14:02.170 --> 01:14:04.260
in fact reduce testosterone

01:14:04.260 --> 01:14:06.010
or at least increase the conversion

01:14:06.010 --> 01:14:07.548
of testosterone to estrogen, correct?

01:14:07.548 --> 01:14:08.381
- Yeah.
- Okay.

01:14:08.381 --> 01:14:10.060
- And with alcohol and GABA agonists,

01:14:10.060 --> 01:14:12.810
it's important to remember
that it shouldn't be daily.

01:14:12.810 --> 01:14:14.840
So one drink of alcohol a day

01:14:14.840 --> 01:14:17.540
is actually very mildly immunosuppressive.

01:14:17.540 --> 01:14:21.010
So it's better to have two
drinks of alcohol one day

01:14:21.010 --> 01:14:23.260
of the week and then two more drinks

01:14:23.260 --> 01:14:25.770
of alcohol another day of
the week and then no alcohol

01:14:25.770 --> 01:14:26.930
the rest of the time.

01:14:26.930 --> 01:14:29.060
The same could be said
even for supplements

01:14:29.060 --> 01:14:30.330
that have GABA in them.

01:14:30.330 --> 01:14:33.490
A lot of sleep supplements
have gamma-aminobutyric acid,

01:14:33.490 --> 01:14:34.740
which is GABA, so-
- Yeah, I occasionally take,

01:14:34.740 --> 01:14:35.573
oh, sorry to interrupt.

01:14:35.573 --> 01:14:39.100
I occasionally take 100
to 200 milligrams of GABA

01:14:39.100 --> 01:14:40.120
in order to enhance sleep.

01:14:40.120 --> 01:14:42.760
But I do it maybe every
third or four nights.

01:14:42.760 --> 01:14:44.750
No more than three or four nights a week.

01:14:44.750 --> 01:14:45.810
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

01:14:45.810 --> 01:14:46.950
- That's perfect.
- Okay.

01:14:46.950 --> 01:14:48.800
- So there's a lot of sleep supplements

01:14:48.800 --> 01:14:51.100
that should not be taken daily

01:14:51.100 --> 01:14:52.650
and GABA's one of them.

01:14:52.650 --> 01:14:56.000
Another one of them is Trazodone.

01:14:56.000 --> 01:14:58.650
And melatonin is kind of arguable

01:14:58.650 --> 01:15:00.600
and it depends on the situation.

01:15:00.600 --> 01:15:02.860
But in general, if you're
taking a sleep supplement,

01:15:02.860 --> 01:15:05.020
it should not be taken every night.

01:15:05.020 --> 01:15:08.750
- The sleep supplements that
I understand are okay to take

01:15:08.750 --> 01:15:10.070
every night or nearly every night

01:15:10.070 --> 01:15:11.790
are things like magnesium 3 and 8,

01:15:11.790 --> 01:15:15.690
apigenin, if that's not true, correct me.

01:15:15.690 --> 01:15:16.950
I certainly take them every night

01:15:16.950 --> 01:15:20.170
unless I forget them back
home when I'm traveling.

01:15:20.170 --> 01:15:21.633
- Magnesium's one of the exceptions.

01:15:21.633 --> 01:15:24.680
L-theanine is also another exception.

01:15:24.680 --> 01:15:26.420
- Great, well then at least
I haven't put anything

01:15:26.420 --> 01:15:30.393
into the world that's
wrong in that category yet.

01:15:31.270 --> 01:15:32.140
And hopefully I won't.

01:15:32.140 --> 01:15:34.340
But if I do, I'll correct myself.

01:15:34.340 --> 01:15:37.190
So let's talk about testosterone in males.

01:15:37.190 --> 01:15:40.900
You see these headlines all the times now

01:15:40.900 --> 01:15:43.950
that testosterone levels are dropping,

01:15:43.950 --> 01:15:45.453
sperm counts are dropping.

01:15:46.620 --> 01:15:48.980
Phenotypes of men are changing over time.

01:15:48.980 --> 01:15:51.700
And I can't quite follow
the literature on that,

01:15:51.700 --> 01:15:54.830
because obviously those are
hard controlled experiments

01:15:54.830 --> 01:15:58.670
to do, because techniques
change over time,

01:15:58.670 --> 01:16:01.130
and sensitivity of
techniques change over time.

01:16:01.130 --> 01:16:05.020
But regardless, I'm aware
that a lot of people

01:16:05.020 --> 01:16:07.270
are considering increasing

01:16:07.270 --> 01:16:09.820
their testosterone by taking testosterone.

01:16:09.820 --> 01:16:12.270
A few years ago that was
considered steroid use,

01:16:12.270 --> 01:16:14.760
and it was really extreme kind of stance.

01:16:14.760 --> 01:16:17.490
Nowadays it seems like there's
more discussion about it.

01:16:17.490 --> 01:16:18.790
First off I'd like to know

01:16:20.100 --> 01:16:22.730
does testosterone supplementation,

01:16:22.730 --> 01:16:25.530
and here I'm talking about
prescription from a doctor,

01:16:25.530 --> 01:16:28.720
does it make one more
prone to prostate cancer?

01:16:28.720 --> 01:16:31.770
That seems to always be the
first question that comes out.

01:16:31.770 --> 01:16:33.770
- Yeah, and there is a huge amount

01:16:33.770 --> 01:16:35.830
of misinformation about this too.

01:16:35.830 --> 01:16:40.160
So testosterone is not going
to cause a prostate cancer.

01:16:40.160 --> 01:16:43.830
However, normal aging
causes prostate cancer

01:16:43.830 --> 01:16:47.363
and testosterone will
grow your prostate cancer.

01:16:48.240 --> 01:16:52.830
So if you're a 80-year-old
male and you have an autopsy

01:16:52.830 --> 01:16:55.200
and there's at least say 50%
percent chance that you have

01:16:55.200 --> 01:16:58.180
a prostate cancer, if
you're 90 or 100 years old,

01:16:58.180 --> 01:17:00.600
there's at least a 90% chance.

01:17:00.600 --> 01:17:04.130
So for humans with a prostate,

01:17:04.130 --> 01:17:07.660
it's only a matter of time
until you get a prostate cancer.

01:17:07.660 --> 01:17:08.870
So that begs the question,

01:17:08.870 --> 01:17:11.150
do you want to take something
that's going to grow it

01:17:11.150 --> 01:17:13.840
for sure once you have it?

01:17:13.840 --> 01:17:16.010
So it's an individual assessment

01:17:16.010 --> 01:17:18.840
and it's important to follow
things like PSAs as well.

01:17:18.840 --> 01:17:22.080
- So a PSA of four or less, I mean,

01:17:22.080 --> 01:17:23.180
ideally you wouldn't be at four,

01:17:23.180 --> 01:17:24.730
'cause that's kind of the upper threshold,

01:17:24.730 --> 01:17:26.930
is the simplest read out of whether

01:17:26.930 --> 01:17:29.790
or not there's excessive prostate growth.

01:17:29.790 --> 01:17:31.500
There's benign prostate hyperplasia

01:17:31.500 --> 01:17:33.330
where the prostate is growing,

01:17:33.330 --> 01:17:35.740
but it's non-cancerous, correct?

01:17:35.740 --> 01:17:37.660
And then of course there
are the symptomologies,

01:17:37.660 --> 01:17:39.630
like people have
challenges with urination,

01:17:39.630 --> 01:17:42.080
they have sexual difficulties, et cetera.

01:17:42.080 --> 01:17:45.180
I'm always struck by the correlation

01:17:45.180 --> 01:17:46.980
that people draw between testosterone

01:17:46.980 --> 01:17:49.570
and prostate health and the fact that,

01:17:49.570 --> 01:17:50.770
or I should say the claim

01:17:50.770 --> 01:17:52.650
that testosterone makes
prostate health worse.

01:17:52.650 --> 01:17:53.920
Because if you think about it,

01:17:53.920 --> 01:17:57.310
young males have high testosterone often,

01:17:57.310 --> 01:17:59.963
if not always, or certainly often.

01:18:01.670 --> 01:18:03.877
And you don't see a lot
of prostate overgrowth

01:18:03.877 --> 01:18:05.830
and cancer in young males.

01:18:05.830 --> 01:18:07.610
So something's going on here.

01:18:07.610 --> 01:18:10.160
How should we conceptualize this?

01:18:10.160 --> 01:18:12.800
- So if you have a PSA of 3.9

01:18:12.800 --> 01:18:16.540
and you're a 25-year-old male

01:18:16.540 --> 01:18:21.480
versus a 75-year-old male
and you have a PSA of 5.9,

01:18:21.480 --> 01:18:25.270
the 3.9 PSA is significantly
more concerning.

01:18:25.270 --> 01:18:29.410
So think of your prostate
as taking cumulative damage

01:18:29.410 --> 01:18:31.380
from, not only testosterone,

01:18:31.380 --> 01:18:34.920
but also estrogen and also growth hormone.

01:18:34.920 --> 01:18:37.180
So that's why obese individuals

01:18:37.180 --> 01:18:39.900
have higher incidences of
prostate cancer as well,

01:18:39.900 --> 01:18:42.920
is because they don't have
those cell checkpoints

01:18:42.920 --> 01:18:47.040
where your immune system takes
a second and says, all right,

01:18:47.040 --> 01:18:50.490
stop replicating as fast prostate cells.

01:18:50.490 --> 01:18:52.080
Let's see if there's any atypical ones

01:18:52.080 --> 01:18:53.630
and then it finds those

01:18:53.630 --> 01:18:56.090
and it prevents them from reproducing.

01:18:56.090 --> 01:18:58.490
That's why immunotherapy
in cancer is so promising

01:18:58.490 --> 01:19:01.580
is because they can target
these certain things.

01:19:01.580 --> 01:19:05.010
So the older male is going to have

01:19:05.010 --> 01:19:07.830
that cumulative damage happen already

01:19:07.830 --> 01:19:11.993
and arguably prostate cancer is a normal,

01:19:15.090 --> 01:19:18.880
with aging, fast aging is abnormal.

01:19:18.880 --> 01:19:21.780
Very slow aging is normal.

01:19:21.780 --> 01:19:25.220
There's a fine line to
walk between those two.

01:19:25.220 --> 01:19:27.290
But there's a lot of
things that can be done

01:19:27.290 --> 01:19:28.970
to decrease the turnover,

01:19:28.970 --> 01:19:30.210
decrease the inflammation,

01:19:30.210 --> 01:19:33.910
and decrease the congestion
of the prostate over time.

01:19:33.910 --> 01:19:36.280
There's also a lot more than
just PSAs that can be done.

01:19:36.280 --> 01:19:38.143
There's prostate MRIs and things like that

01:19:38.143 --> 01:19:40.040
that can look at the structure

01:19:40.040 --> 01:19:41.300
and the function of the prostate.

01:19:41.300 --> 01:19:42.580
- So what should every male do

01:19:42.580 --> 01:19:44.300
to maintain the health of their prostate?

01:19:44.300 --> 01:19:45.480
And I realize that younger males

01:19:45.480 --> 01:19:46.680
probably aren't thinking about it at all.

01:19:46.680 --> 01:19:49.640
Although it seems like
nowadays I get these kind of

01:19:49.640 --> 01:19:52.480
what I call cryptic questions.

01:19:52.480 --> 01:19:54.080
I think women are more comfortable talking

01:19:54.080 --> 01:19:57.223
about their hormone and sexual
health because of they cycle,

01:19:58.110 --> 01:19:59.020
because of menstrual cycles.

01:19:59.020 --> 01:20:02.160
They're used to fluctuations
that sort of give them

01:20:02.160 --> 01:20:03.950
the experience of what it's
like to have different levels

01:20:03.950 --> 01:20:06.610
of progesterone, estrogen,
testosterone, et cetera.

01:20:06.610 --> 01:20:08.720
But I get these kind of
cryptic questions often

01:20:08.720 --> 01:20:10.040
in my direct messages

01:20:10.040 --> 01:20:12.683
where what I think people are asking is,

01:20:14.680 --> 01:20:16.170
is there something wrong with my prostate?

01:20:16.170 --> 01:20:17.550
What should I do for my prostate?

01:20:17.550 --> 01:20:18.740
These are often indirect questions

01:20:18.740 --> 01:20:21.590
for other aspects of their
life where they're suffering.

01:20:21.590 --> 01:20:23.290
And I don't say that ingest.

01:20:23.290 --> 01:20:26.750
I think more direct
discussion would be great.

01:20:26.750 --> 01:20:30.631
So what should all males do

01:20:30.631 --> 01:20:34.250
to maintain prostate health
throughout the lifespan?

01:20:34.250 --> 01:20:37.120
- Maintaining prostate health
can be looked at similarly

01:20:37.120 --> 01:20:40.970
how you can maintain a good
natural optimal testosterone.

01:20:40.970 --> 01:20:42.710
So you look for things that can hurt it.

01:20:42.710 --> 01:20:45.020
You don't necessarily look for one thing

01:20:45.020 --> 01:20:47.350
that can improve it or boost it.

01:20:47.350 --> 01:20:51.020
So for young males, those are prostatitis,

01:20:51.020 --> 01:20:54.160
so it goes hand in hand with epididymitis.

01:20:54.160 --> 01:20:56.960
So different infections of the prostate.

01:20:56.960 --> 01:20:58.280
The younger the male is,

01:20:58.280 --> 01:20:59.690
the more likely it is related

01:20:59.690 --> 01:21:02.970
to something that could
be sexually transmitted.

01:21:02.970 --> 01:21:05.040
But another very common cause

01:21:05.040 --> 01:21:08.960
is what we call gram negative
and anerobic bacteria.

01:21:08.960 --> 01:21:13.960
The prostate is right
by the end of the colon.

01:21:14.380 --> 01:21:16.890
So if you have chronic constipation

01:21:16.890 --> 01:21:20.700
or if you have colitis or if you,

01:21:20.700 --> 01:21:23.170
even just an E-coli
overgrowth in the colon

01:21:23.170 --> 01:21:25.970
is very likely to cause an infection

01:21:25.970 --> 01:21:27.620
of the prostate as well.

01:21:27.620 --> 01:21:30.180
- What should males do to prevent that?

01:21:30.180 --> 01:21:31.790
- Have a diet that has good,

01:21:31.790 --> 01:21:35.983
healthy prebiotic fiber,
probiotics as well.

01:21:37.200 --> 01:21:39.290
Make sure that they're having
regular bowel movements,

01:21:39.290 --> 01:21:41.640
that they don't have chronic constipation.

01:21:41.640 --> 01:21:43.540
Have good sources of dietary fiber,

01:21:43.540 --> 01:21:47.040
which is also as soluble fiber,
and enough insoluble fiber.

01:21:47.040 --> 01:21:50.640
Most people get enough
insoluble or non-dietary fiber.

01:21:50.640 --> 01:21:54.930
So that can help prevent the
chance of diverticulitis,

01:21:54.930 --> 01:21:57.400
which is another type of infection.

01:21:57.400 --> 01:21:59.850
It can also decrease the chance of colitis

01:21:59.850 --> 01:22:02.890
and decrease the chance of
prostate infections as well.

01:22:02.890 --> 01:22:06.300
- Are there any foods and/or supplements

01:22:06.300 --> 01:22:08.460
that men should take or avoid?

01:22:08.460 --> 01:22:10.610
What about, you hear
or about saw palmetto,

01:22:12.120 --> 01:22:13.890
yeah, supplements for,

01:22:13.890 --> 01:22:16.210
or supplements that support

01:22:16.210 --> 01:22:18.550
or cause issues for the prostate?

01:22:18.550 --> 01:22:21.380
- Yeah, if there's a strong
genetic predisposition

01:22:21.380 --> 01:22:23.610
to enlarged prostates,

01:22:23.610 --> 01:22:27.360
or even just really early
prostate cancers that grow fast,

01:22:27.360 --> 01:22:29.970
then they could consider
taking saw palmetto

01:22:29.970 --> 01:22:32.200
or even curcumin as an anti-androgen,

01:22:32.200 --> 01:22:33.950
as long as they're able to tolerate it.

01:22:33.950 --> 01:22:37.293
It's an individualized basis
and depends on their history.

01:22:38.360 --> 01:22:42.870
As far as making sure that
their prostate is not congested,

01:22:42.870 --> 01:22:47.870
there's an interesting
correlation between having girls

01:22:47.930 --> 01:22:49.112
and having prostate cancer.

01:22:49.112 --> 01:22:50.370
- Having girl offspring?
- Yeah.

01:22:50.370 --> 01:22:53.250
- So if your offspring are females,

01:22:53.250 --> 01:22:56.533
then you're slightly more
likely to have prostate cancer.

01:22:59.000 --> 01:23:02.540
There's hypotheses that link
estrogen to prostate cancer

01:23:02.540 --> 01:23:04.440
rather than testosterone.

01:23:04.440 --> 01:23:06.840
So if you have hypoestrogenism,

01:23:06.840 --> 01:23:10.770
your prostate has more atypical cells.

01:23:10.770 --> 01:23:13.720
In general, the higher
your C-reactive protein,

01:23:13.720 --> 01:23:16.060
which is the general marker
of inflammation in your body,

01:23:16.060 --> 01:23:20.500
we call it CRP, and the
test order is hsCRP,

01:23:20.500 --> 01:23:22.940
or high-sensitivity CRP.

01:23:22.940 --> 01:23:26.300
If your CRP raises up very high,

01:23:26.300 --> 01:23:27.960
if you have an autoimmune disease,

01:23:27.960 --> 01:23:31.960
like if you have a Crohn's
flare or if you have lupus

01:23:31.960 --> 01:23:35.600
or an infection or a sexually
transmitted infection,

01:23:35.600 --> 01:23:38.190
or even a colitis, or even the flu,

01:23:38.190 --> 01:23:40.620
your CRP is going to raise significantly.

01:23:40.620 --> 01:23:42.153
- That you would detect in a blood test

01:23:42.153 --> 01:23:42.986
of course.
- Correct.

01:23:42.986 --> 01:23:43.819
Yeah.
- Yeah.

01:23:43.819 --> 01:23:44.652
- So you want to get a baseline CRP

01:23:44.652 --> 01:23:47.990
when you haven't had any
of those things recently.

01:23:47.990 --> 01:23:49.980
And if your CRP is higher,

01:23:49.980 --> 01:23:52.720
you also have more female offspring.

01:23:52.720 --> 01:23:54.460
If your CRP is higher,

01:23:54.460 --> 01:23:56.830
then your reactive oxygen species,

01:23:56.830 --> 01:24:00.210
which are causing mutations
and atypical cell turnover

01:24:00.210 --> 01:24:02.740
in the prostate are also likely higher.

01:24:02.740 --> 01:24:05.460
So you want to keep a very low CRP.

01:24:05.460 --> 01:24:07.820
- Interesting, and what about blood flow,

01:24:07.820 --> 01:24:09.350
and pelvic floor in general?

01:24:09.350 --> 01:24:11.600
We should probably do a whole
episode on pelvic floor.

01:24:11.600 --> 01:24:14.720
There's so much interesting
data coming out of

01:24:14.720 --> 01:24:17.640
the fields of clinical
and research urology.

01:24:17.640 --> 01:24:19.140
I realize it's kind of the Netherlands

01:24:19.140 --> 01:24:20.780
of biology and medicine.

01:24:20.780 --> 01:24:22.460
People probably aren't
thinking so much about this,

01:24:22.460 --> 01:24:26.270
but pelvic floor is obviously a confluence

01:24:26.270 --> 01:24:29.360
of a ton of of vasculature, of nerves,

01:24:29.360 --> 01:24:31.100
and of course the prostate resides there.

01:24:31.100 --> 01:24:33.823
And of course the genitals
reside there as well.

01:24:35.370 --> 01:24:38.293
So I would imagine that
one of the six pillars,

01:24:39.582 --> 01:24:42.300
exercise, being able to
maintain adequate blood flow

01:24:42.300 --> 01:24:43.960
to those regions is key.

01:24:43.960 --> 01:24:45.220
What about just postural things?

01:24:45.220 --> 01:24:49.390
People sitting too much,
not hydrating well enough,

01:24:49.390 --> 01:24:51.590
you mentioned avoiding constipation.

01:24:51.590 --> 01:24:52.720
What are some other things,

01:24:52.720 --> 01:24:55.940
including medications that can
serve to support the prostate

01:24:55.940 --> 01:24:59.340
over time and maybe even
support pelvic floor in general,

01:24:59.340 --> 01:25:01.660
both in males and females over time?

01:25:01.660 --> 01:25:03.240
- Absolutely, and this is something

01:25:03.240 --> 01:25:05.470
that's rightfully getting
more and more attention.

01:25:05.470 --> 01:25:09.520
The way I explain the pelvic
floor is your abdominal cavity,

01:25:09.520 --> 01:25:11.610
which includes your
peritoneum or where most

01:25:11.610 --> 01:25:15.470
of your organs are, your
retroperitoneum, your pelvic space.

01:25:15.470 --> 01:25:16.670
Think of it as a box.

01:25:16.670 --> 01:25:18.760
And your abs are the front of the box.

01:25:18.760 --> 01:25:20.320
Your back muscles are the back.

01:25:20.320 --> 01:25:22.610
Your diaphragm is the top of the box.

01:25:22.610 --> 01:25:24.080
And your pelvic floor,

01:25:24.080 --> 01:25:26.750
that's where your port
is to the outside world.

01:25:26.750 --> 01:25:29.690
Especially important,
it has muscles as well.

01:25:29.690 --> 01:25:31.060
And you can do exercises.

01:25:31.060 --> 01:25:33.620
Pelvic floor physical
therapists are becoming more

01:25:33.620 --> 01:25:35.810
and more utilized,
especially after childbirth,

01:25:35.810 --> 01:25:37.560
but in other situations as well,

01:25:37.560 --> 01:25:41.470
including by men getting
care from urologists.

01:25:41.470 --> 01:25:44.740
So you want to both strengthen
that pelvic pelvic floor

01:25:44.740 --> 01:25:48.480
and make sure that the
tubes that are docked

01:25:48.480 --> 01:25:51.770
to the outside world
are working well enough,

01:25:51.770 --> 01:25:52.790
but they're not too loose.

01:25:52.790 --> 01:25:54.700
They're not working too well.

01:25:54.700 --> 01:25:59.420
So there's a lot of medications
that can be positives

01:25:59.420 --> 01:26:01.820
or negatives for your pelvic floor.

01:26:01.820 --> 01:26:03.100
We kind of talked about your gut

01:26:03.100 --> 01:26:05.090
and colon health in general.

01:26:05.090 --> 01:26:07.030
As far as your prostate health

01:26:07.030 --> 01:26:11.370
and as far as your bladder
and urinary system health,

01:26:11.370 --> 01:26:13.160
you think about a couple
different classes.

01:26:13.160 --> 01:26:14.640
So you have your phosphodiesterase.

01:26:14.640 --> 01:26:16.333
You have your tadalafil.

01:26:17.950 --> 01:26:20.860
Basically this is going to
help decrease congestion

01:26:20.860 --> 01:26:22.620
in the prostate.

01:26:22.620 --> 01:26:25.030
A lot of people take it for ED,

01:26:25.030 --> 01:26:26.280
but it can actually
help you decrease your-

01:26:26.280 --> 01:26:27.650
- Could you define that?

01:26:27.650 --> 01:26:31.590
- A lot of men take to
tadalafil, generic is Cialis,

01:26:31.590 --> 01:26:34.190
has a much longer half-life
than Viagra or Levitra.

01:26:34.190 --> 01:26:36.130
Its half-life is almost a day.

01:26:36.130 --> 01:26:37.660
So you can take a very low dose of it.

01:26:37.660 --> 01:26:39.090
Instead of taking 20 milligrams,

01:26:39.090 --> 01:26:41.000
you take two or two and a half milligrams.

01:26:41.000 --> 01:26:43.270
- So you're saying that
a lot of men take it

01:26:43.270 --> 01:26:45.200
for erectile dysfunction?
- Yes.

01:26:45.200 --> 01:26:47.480
- But that at it at lower doses,

01:26:47.480 --> 01:26:50.740
it may have served purposes
for prostate health,

01:26:50.740 --> 01:26:53.310
independent of erection?

01:26:53.310 --> 01:26:56.770
- Correct, the most common
scenario is if a male

01:26:56.770 --> 01:26:59.910
is waking up twice at
night to pee, on average,

01:26:59.910 --> 01:27:01.420
it'll cut that down to once.

01:27:01.420 --> 01:27:03.600
So if they're waking up
at four times at night,

01:27:03.600 --> 01:27:05.810
then it can cut that
down to twice at night,

01:27:05.810 --> 01:27:07.490
just because you have easier blood flow.

01:27:07.490 --> 01:27:09.840
We used to use other
medications like Flomax,

01:27:09.840 --> 01:27:11.530
which is tamsulosin.

01:27:11.530 --> 01:27:13.010
That's an alpha antagonist,

01:27:13.010 --> 01:27:16.410
so it basically binds to a
receptor in smooth muscle,

01:27:16.410 --> 01:27:18.920
and it helps relax that.

01:27:18.920 --> 01:27:21.710
There's several other alpha antagonists.

01:27:21.710 --> 01:27:23.290
And then you also have your medications

01:27:23.290 --> 01:27:24.940
that are hormonal like finasteride

01:27:24.940 --> 01:27:27.240
that a lot of people
take for prostate health

01:27:27.240 --> 01:27:29.840
to decrease the enlargement
of the prostate.

01:27:29.840 --> 01:27:33.360
The periurethral area,
or periurethral lobe,

01:27:33.360 --> 01:27:35.960
there's several lobes of the prostate,

01:27:35.960 --> 01:27:40.650
that tends to be especially
enlarged in cases of BPH and-

01:27:40.650 --> 01:27:41.550
- BPH?

01:27:41.550 --> 01:27:45.070
- Prostate hyperplasia
or an enlarged prostate.

01:27:45.070 --> 01:27:48.050
And if you are able to shrink that area,

01:27:48.050 --> 01:27:51.250
then at that point, it's
just a plumbing problem.

01:27:51.250 --> 01:27:53.700
And the urine is able to get by easier.

01:27:53.700 --> 01:27:57.250
- Yeah, my understanding is
that now there's a growing,

01:27:57.250 --> 01:27:59.050
I don't want to say a movement, [chuckles]

01:27:59.050 --> 01:28:03.170
but the idea of taking very low dose,

01:28:03.170 --> 01:28:06.590
like 2.5 milligram or
5 milligram tadalafil,

01:28:06.590 --> 01:28:09.810
even daily is becoming pretty common

01:28:09.810 --> 01:28:12.670
for many men who do not
have erectile dysfunction,

01:28:12.670 --> 01:28:16.210
simply to either maintain
or enhance prostate health.

01:28:16.210 --> 01:28:17.280
Is that correct?

01:28:17.280 --> 01:28:18.190
- Yeah, that's correct.

01:28:18.190 --> 01:28:21.890
- And do you see any negative
effects of doing that?

01:28:21.890 --> 01:28:23.350
- There can be negative effects.

01:28:23.350 --> 01:28:24.800
It can lower blood pressure.

01:28:24.800 --> 01:28:27.350
So theoretically it can
increase your chance

01:28:27.350 --> 01:28:29.450
of vasovagal syncope.

01:28:29.450 --> 01:28:32.330
A lot of people take it
as a alternative to pump,

01:28:32.330 --> 01:28:35.303
because it kind of works
similarly to citrulline,

01:28:36.220 --> 01:28:38.810
or different pump products in pre-workout,

01:28:38.810 --> 01:28:40.250
and it can certainly help with that.

01:28:40.250 --> 01:28:42.440
But if you're about to go do a deadlift

01:28:42.440 --> 01:28:44.030
where you might pass out anyway,

01:28:44.030 --> 01:28:46.710
it can certainly increase
the chance of that happens,

01:28:46.710 --> 01:28:49.630
because you don't have
that compensatory exercise,

01:28:49.630 --> 01:28:51.450
hypertension response.

01:28:51.450 --> 01:28:54.590
- Could someone just take
it away from exercise?

01:28:54.590 --> 01:28:57.160
- They could, if you took tadalafil,

01:28:57.160 --> 01:28:59.160
then that's going to be,

01:28:59.160 --> 01:29:00.980
has a long half-life.

01:29:00.980 --> 01:29:03.540
Whereas Viagra and Levitra
is just a few hours,

01:29:03.540 --> 01:29:05.503
tadalafil almost today.

01:29:06.480 --> 01:29:09.560
Some interesting studies on
Viagra have been done as well.

01:29:09.560 --> 01:29:13.620
It can potentially alter your
rays and cones in your eye.

01:29:13.620 --> 01:29:17.810
So the usual recommendation
for pilots that need

01:29:17.810 --> 01:29:21.380
to have red-green discrimination
from very long distances

01:29:21.380 --> 01:29:23.630
with very small indicator lights

01:29:23.630 --> 01:29:26.410
is to not take Viagra.

01:29:26.410 --> 01:29:28.140
So I usually say

01:29:28.140 --> 01:29:29.850
if you're a pilot and
that's your profession,

01:29:29.850 --> 01:29:31.990
perhaps hold off from that for a while.

01:29:31.990 --> 01:29:34.990
There's also studies with
Viagra that significantly,

01:29:34.990 --> 01:29:38.600
which is also known as
sildenafil as the generic now,

01:29:38.600 --> 01:29:41.130
it can increase eyebrow hair growth.

01:29:41.130 --> 01:29:45.420
So potentially what it
does is it helps vasodilate

01:29:45.420 --> 01:29:48.380
and relax the veins,
especially in older men.

01:29:48.380 --> 01:29:50.100
And when those veins are relaxed,

01:29:50.100 --> 01:29:52.010
you have better blood flow.

01:29:52.010 --> 01:29:54.700
That's one of the proposals or theories

01:29:54.700 --> 01:29:59.330
behind why older men get the
androgenetic alopecia more.

01:29:59.330 --> 01:30:01.490
You're having less
blood flow in the scalp.

01:30:01.490 --> 01:30:04.247
So theoretically it can
also help prevent that,

01:30:04.247 --> 01:30:05.390
but it's not going to-
- So in theory,

01:30:05.390 --> 01:30:06.330
increasing blood, oh,

01:30:06.330 --> 01:30:08.580
because it increases
blood flow systemically

01:30:08.580 --> 01:30:09.650
throughout the body?
- Yeah.

01:30:09.650 --> 01:30:12.620
- Not just in specific tissues.

01:30:12.620 --> 01:30:14.990
Well, I find it incredibly
interesting that, yeah,

01:30:14.990 --> 01:30:16.800
there are these online
forums building up now

01:30:16.800 --> 01:30:19.533
around low dose tadalafil,

01:30:20.880 --> 01:30:22.960
daily use of low dose tadalafil, again,

01:30:22.960 --> 01:30:26.010
not for sexual or erectile dysfunction,

01:30:26.010 --> 01:30:29.220
but for sake of longterm prostate health.

01:30:29.220 --> 01:30:31.290
Is there any reason why women might want

01:30:31.290 --> 01:30:33.283
to take low dose tadalafil?

01:30:34.940 --> 01:30:39.940
- tadalafil is also a weak
androgen receptor sensitizer,

01:30:40.407 --> 01:30:42.070
kind of like L-carnitine,

01:30:42.070 --> 01:30:45.130
where the density of the
available androgen receptors

01:30:45.130 --> 01:30:48.120
to bind increases slightly.

01:30:48.120 --> 01:30:52.540
So there could potentially
be a benefit from that,

01:30:52.540 --> 01:30:55.170
but most of the time it's used in men.

01:30:55.170 --> 01:30:58.130
- Very interesting, we
haven't really talked

01:30:58.130 --> 01:31:01.763
about testosterone and
optimizing testosterone in males.

01:31:02.930 --> 01:31:05.763
Assuming someone is paying
attention to the six pillars,

01:31:07.630 --> 01:31:10.260
there's kind of a gap as, I see it,

01:31:10.260 --> 01:31:13.750
between doing all those things and TRT,

01:31:13.750 --> 01:31:15.820
hormone replacement therapy.

01:31:15.820 --> 01:31:18.950
And again, the R, the replacement in TRT

01:31:18.950 --> 01:31:21.970
is a little bit of in quotes nowadays,

01:31:21.970 --> 01:31:24.980
because a lot of people
who have testosterone

01:31:24.980 --> 01:31:29.070
in that 300 to 900 nanogram
per deciliter range opt

01:31:29.070 --> 01:31:30.930
to take low dose testosterone anyway.

01:31:30.930 --> 01:31:35.230
My understanding is that
there have been some new kind

01:31:35.230 --> 01:31:38.080
of movements in this area
toward, for instance,

01:31:38.080 --> 01:31:43.080
not doing big, large doses
injected infrequently,

01:31:43.730 --> 01:31:46.380
but rather low doses quite frequently,

01:31:46.380 --> 01:31:47.630
obviously prescribed by a doctor,

01:31:47.630 --> 01:31:49.970
monitored by a doctor, et cetera.

01:31:49.970 --> 01:31:53.250
Is that generally what you
like to see in your patients

01:31:53.250 --> 01:31:55.360
if they're going to take this route?

01:31:55.360 --> 01:31:57.110
- If they're a hypogonadal patient

01:31:57.110 --> 01:32:01.810
whose benefits outweigh risks of TRT,

01:32:01.810 --> 01:32:05.100
then you want to have a
nice even steady state.

01:32:05.100 --> 01:32:06.730
It's not going to be exactly the same

01:32:06.730 --> 01:32:10.660
as producing pulsatile
testosterone release endogenously

01:32:11.500 --> 01:32:12.850
from your own body.

01:32:12.850 --> 01:32:14.740
When you have a steady state,

01:32:14.740 --> 01:32:16.320
you don't have a peak or a trough.

01:32:16.320 --> 01:32:17.720
And when you have a peak,

01:32:17.720 --> 01:32:20.850
that's when the antigen
receptor gene is overactive,

01:32:20.850 --> 01:32:24.210
that's when you get more
erythropoietin or EPO release,

01:32:24.210 --> 01:32:27.570
and that leads to a lot of the
side effects of thick blood,

01:32:27.570 --> 01:32:29.690
so higher hemoglobins, and hematocrits.

01:32:29.690 --> 01:32:33.920
And then when you have a
crash, you don't feel good.

01:32:33.920 --> 01:32:37.050
So it's definitely not optimal.

01:32:37.050 --> 01:32:38.960
There's a lot of ways to get around this.

01:32:38.960 --> 01:32:41.550
So when you're doing
testosterone replacement,

01:32:41.550 --> 01:32:43.430
if you're someone that needs it,

01:32:43.430 --> 01:32:46.000
you can have different types of esters,

01:32:46.000 --> 01:32:48.560
or you could do topical testosterone.

01:32:48.560 --> 01:32:51.450
So the Ester is basically something

01:32:51.450 --> 01:32:54.770
that's attached to increase
the biological half-life.

01:32:54.770 --> 01:32:57.300
The most common ones are
cypionate, enanthate,

01:32:57.300 --> 01:32:59.300
there's also a very
short-acting propionate,

01:32:59.300 --> 01:33:01.700
which has almost no clinical relevance.

01:33:01.700 --> 01:33:03.900
And there's also very long-acting ones,

01:33:03.900 --> 01:33:06.105
decanoate, and undecanoate,

01:33:06.105 --> 01:33:08.660
and different mixtures of all those.

01:33:08.660 --> 01:33:12.600
So if you're someone who
has a very, very low SHBG,

01:33:12.600 --> 01:33:14.900
you're going to have trouble of regulating

01:33:14.900 --> 01:33:17.540
your serum testosterone in the long run.

01:33:17.540 --> 01:33:18.660
If you do it topically,

01:33:18.660 --> 01:33:21.980
then the testosterone is
absorbed, hopefully bound to SHBG,

01:33:21.980 --> 01:33:24.150
and then a lot of times
you reapply twice daily

01:33:24.150 --> 01:33:26.970
or once daily, but you
have lots of variations.

01:33:26.970 --> 01:33:28.530
So for most people,

01:33:28.530 --> 01:33:31.580
especially for people
who can't absorb it well,

01:33:31.580 --> 01:33:33.090
that's not going to be a great option.

01:33:33.090 --> 01:33:34.730
So injections would be preferred.

01:33:34.730 --> 01:33:36.650
Most people end up injecting,

01:33:36.650 --> 01:33:39.030
because they have either
side effects from too high,

01:33:39.030 --> 01:33:42.060
too low, or just too much of a varied dose

01:33:42.060 --> 01:33:43.300
when they do topical.

01:33:43.300 --> 01:33:47.640
There's also a capsule with a
special lymphatic absorption.

01:33:47.640 --> 01:33:49.570
So it's not being absorbed
through the liver,

01:33:49.570 --> 01:33:51.000
it's not hepatically metabolized,

01:33:51.000 --> 01:33:52.970
but it's absorbed through the lymph.

01:33:52.970 --> 01:33:56.097
And it's essentially
testosterone undecanoate,

01:33:56.097 --> 01:33:57.693
and then put into a capsule.

01:33:59.200 --> 01:34:01.280
And that's taken twice daily.

01:34:01.280 --> 01:34:03.100
It has fairly steady half-lifes,

01:34:03.100 --> 01:34:05.770
but you have to take it at
specific times of the day.

01:34:05.770 --> 01:34:07.410
So that being said,

01:34:07.410 --> 01:34:09.780
and it's new enough to where
there isn't a huge amount

01:34:09.780 --> 01:34:12.500
of data on it, but it is FDA approved.

01:34:12.500 --> 01:34:16.190
So it is brand name now.
it's called JATENZO.

01:34:16.190 --> 01:34:19.520
But the injectables in general,

01:34:19.520 --> 01:34:23.250
the lower your SHBG, the
longer of an ester you want,

01:34:23.250 --> 01:34:24.910
because when you inject it,

01:34:24.910 --> 01:34:26.940
whether it's intramuscular
or subcutaneous,

01:34:26.940 --> 01:34:28.610
just talk to your doctor about the risks

01:34:28.610 --> 01:34:29.550
and the benefits of those.

01:34:29.550 --> 01:34:32.110
Subcutaneous has slightly
longer active half-life,

01:34:32.110 --> 01:34:34.340
because the esterases take longer to reach

01:34:34.340 --> 01:34:36.483
that supinate or an estered clavate.

01:34:37.770 --> 01:34:41.130
So most men, a lot of
people ask me about like

01:34:41.130 --> 01:34:42.180
what a usual dose is.

01:34:43.400 --> 01:34:46.110
For most people, it would
be a total of about 100

01:34:46.110 --> 01:34:49.560
to 120 per week for an
actual replacement dose.

01:34:49.560 --> 01:34:51.040
- Milligrams?
- Milligrams.

01:34:51.040 --> 01:34:53.940
120 to 100 milligrams per week

01:34:53.940 --> 01:34:56.170
administered two to three times per week.

01:34:56.170 --> 01:34:58.960
- And you're not, so you're
saying dividing that into two

01:34:58.960 --> 01:34:59.793
or three, right?

01:34:59.793 --> 01:35:01.160
'Cause I'm sure a bunch of
people out there are thinking,

01:35:01.160 --> 01:35:02.640
oh yeah, 103 times a week,

01:35:02.640 --> 01:35:04.720
which is actually quite a high dose.

01:35:04.720 --> 01:35:07.220
Yeah, there really does seem to be a shift

01:35:07.220 --> 01:35:10.810
toward spreading these dosages out into,

01:35:10.810 --> 01:35:13.520
dividing them into two
or three smaller doses.

01:35:13.520 --> 01:35:16.393
And then along those lines,

01:35:17.270 --> 01:35:18.470
5, 10 years ago,

01:35:18.470 --> 01:35:21.020
it was common to hear
about inhibiting estrogen

01:35:21.020 --> 01:35:22.460
through aromatase inhibitors.

01:35:22.460 --> 01:35:25.180
Nowadays you hear, and I think it's true,

01:35:25.180 --> 01:35:27.360
at least by my read of the literature,

01:35:27.360 --> 01:35:30.280
that inhibiting estrogen
can disrupt brain function,

01:35:30.280 --> 01:35:32.180
can cause connective tissue issues,

01:35:32.180 --> 01:35:35.160
and even can cause reductions in libido.

01:35:35.160 --> 01:35:38.720
So a lot of people think they estrogen,

01:35:38.720 --> 01:35:42.040
if you crash estrogen, that
basically libido goes up,

01:35:42.040 --> 01:35:43.670
but actually the opposite is often true.

01:35:43.670 --> 01:35:45.720
You don't want estrogen
too high or too low,

01:35:45.720 --> 01:35:46.553
is that correct?

01:35:46.553 --> 01:35:47.423
And for that reason,

01:35:48.640 --> 01:35:53.640
do you shy away from people
taking aromatase inhibitors?

01:35:53.810 --> 01:35:58.810
- Yeah, very few people truly
need aromatase inhibitor.

01:35:59.150 --> 01:36:01.780
There's almost always
lifestyle interventions.

01:36:01.780 --> 01:36:04.160
It can just depend on which gene,

01:36:04.160 --> 01:36:06.290
how active your aromatase gene is.

01:36:06.290 --> 01:36:09.190
Some people's aromatase
gene is very active.

01:36:09.190 --> 01:36:13.770
A lot of times these individuals
have pubertal gynecomastia,

01:36:13.770 --> 01:36:16.250
which is breast tissue growth in males,

01:36:16.250 --> 01:36:18.360
even despite no other risk factor.

01:36:18.360 --> 01:36:19.593
- Even if they're lean?

01:36:20.630 --> 01:36:22.320
- Some people get it if they're lean.

01:36:22.320 --> 01:36:23.917
- I remember growing up-
- It's possible.

01:36:23.917 --> 01:36:25.920
- There were a few kids
that got mild cases

01:36:25.920 --> 01:36:27.820
of gynecomastia that were transient.

01:36:27.820 --> 01:36:29.960
Like it's sort of like
they developed gynecomastia

01:36:29.960 --> 01:36:31.340
and then it went away.

01:36:31.340 --> 01:36:33.890
- Often it's unilateral on one side too.

01:36:33.890 --> 01:36:38.080
So growth hormone a lot of
times is the fuel to that fire.

01:36:38.080 --> 01:36:39.230
- Oh, interesting.
- Yeah.

01:36:39.230 --> 01:36:40.350
- Yeah, there were a couple of kids.

01:36:40.350 --> 01:36:43.730
I mean, they took some
teasing 'cause back then,

01:36:43.730 --> 01:36:45.670
there wasn't online
discussions about hormones

01:36:45.670 --> 01:36:48.070
and things like that, but
then it would seem transient.

01:36:48.070 --> 01:36:48.903
And they were,

01:36:48.903 --> 01:36:51.510
the people I'm thinking of
were actually lean individuals.

01:36:51.510 --> 01:36:52.640
So they weren't overweight,

01:36:52.640 --> 01:36:54.890
which of course can cause gynecomastia,

01:36:54.890 --> 01:36:57.450
because adipose fat tissue

01:36:57.450 --> 01:37:00.230
can convert testosterone into estrogen.

01:37:00.230 --> 01:37:02.460
So it sounds like,
except in special cases,

01:37:02.460 --> 01:37:05.210
that avoiding aromatase inhibitors

01:37:05.210 --> 01:37:07.110
is probably going to be a good idea.

01:37:07.110 --> 01:37:08.130
- Yeah, there's several other ways

01:37:08.130 --> 01:37:10.100
that you can control
your estrogen and keep it

01:37:10.100 --> 01:37:12.210
at a healthy level, which
you do have to check.

01:37:12.210 --> 01:37:14.980
There's a lot of patients who assure me

01:37:14.980 --> 01:37:16.930
that their estrogen's going to be sky high

01:37:16.930 --> 01:37:20.020
and it's actually very low and vice versa.

01:37:20.020 --> 01:37:22.590
But calcium D-glucarate is a supplement

01:37:22.590 --> 01:37:24.490
that can help with estrogen control.

01:37:24.490 --> 01:37:26.960
- What's a typical dosage
of calcium D-glucarate?

01:37:26.960 --> 01:37:28.960
- 500 To 1,000 milligrams.

01:37:28.960 --> 01:37:31.170
- But is there the risk
that if someone's estrogen

01:37:31.170 --> 01:37:33.920
is in normal range and
they take the supplement,

01:37:33.920 --> 01:37:35.600
that their estrogen will go too low?

01:37:35.600 --> 01:37:37.460
Is it that potent?

01:37:37.460 --> 01:37:38.340
- It's not that potent.

01:37:38.340 --> 01:37:40.660
It's not near as potent
as an aromatase inhibitor.

01:37:40.660 --> 01:37:43.900
So it helps with excretion
and also the sensitivity

01:37:43.900 --> 01:37:46.100
of the estrogen receptor itself.

01:37:46.100 --> 01:37:48.770
And it kind of like helps outcompete it.

01:37:48.770 --> 01:37:50.710
Some people will also take DIM

01:37:50.710 --> 01:37:53.923
or different cruciferous vegetable,

01:37:54.800 --> 01:37:58.820
they get 'em from cruciferous
vegetables like kale but,

01:37:58.820 --> 01:38:02.910
or broccoli and that
is both an antiestrogen

01:38:02.910 --> 01:38:04.660
and an antiandrogen.

01:38:04.660 --> 01:38:07.020
So if you're on TRT and you're on that,

01:38:07.020 --> 01:38:09.200
then you're probably just on too much TRT.

01:38:09.200 --> 01:38:10.840
- Yeah, I remember a few
years ago I had a friend,

01:38:10.840 --> 01:38:13.377
and it truly is, it's not
like I have a friend thing,

01:38:13.377 --> 01:38:14.900
'cause I'm very cautious just about

01:38:14.900 --> 01:38:15.840
which supplements I take.

01:38:15.840 --> 01:38:17.520
I think people might get the impression

01:38:17.520 --> 01:38:19.640
that I'm very cavalier
about this, but I'm not.

01:38:19.640 --> 01:38:21.240
I always alter one thing at a time.

01:38:21.240 --> 01:38:22.393
I talk to physicians.

01:38:23.280 --> 01:38:25.050
What I suggest other
people do I actually do

01:38:25.050 --> 01:38:26.750
and have done for a long period of time.

01:38:26.750 --> 01:38:31.040
And I recall wanting to take
DIM, 'cause I thought, well,

01:38:31.040 --> 01:38:34.130
back then you hear, okay, reduce estrogen.

01:38:34.130 --> 01:38:35.900
My estrogen levels weren't out of range,

01:38:35.900 --> 01:38:36.980
so they were fine, but I thought, well,

01:38:36.980 --> 01:38:38.900
what would the experience
be of bringing those down?

01:38:38.900 --> 01:38:41.660
But someone I know is quite
informed in this area said,

01:38:41.660 --> 01:38:42.870
yeah, exactly what you said,

01:38:42.870 --> 01:38:44.510
which is that DIM can reduce estrogen,

01:38:44.510 --> 01:38:45.550
but also testosterone.

01:38:45.550 --> 01:38:48.150
So I just never opted to try and take it.

01:38:48.150 --> 01:38:50.420
I do want, we're sort of
airing in this direction,

01:38:50.420 --> 01:38:54.240
but we went straight from
the six pillars to TRT

01:38:54.240 --> 01:38:56.810
or to what some people
now call sports TRT,

01:38:56.810 --> 01:38:58.990
which is basically code language

01:38:58.990 --> 01:39:02.440
for saying taking exogenous testosterone

01:39:02.440 --> 01:39:04.320
even though one doesn't
need it to get into

01:39:04.320 --> 01:39:09.320
a semi-super physiological
range or a high end,

01:39:09.850 --> 01:39:12.440
like 900 to 1,000 nanogram
per deciliter range.

01:39:12.440 --> 01:39:15.010
And people always point out,
I should mention that, oh,

01:39:15.010 --> 01:39:15.990
well in certain countries,

01:39:15.990 --> 01:39:18.700
the high end range is 1,200
nanograms per deciliter.

01:39:18.700 --> 01:39:19.637
In the US, it's 900.

01:39:19.637 --> 01:39:22.700
And so if you're 1,200, are
you really super physiological?

01:39:22.700 --> 01:39:24.420
All that aside,

01:39:24.420 --> 01:39:27.470
I neglected to ask about
that gap in between

01:39:27.470 --> 01:39:30.920
where individuals could
think about supplementation,

01:39:30.920 --> 01:39:32.470
meaning non-prescription approaches

01:39:32.470 --> 01:39:33.880
to increasing testosterone,

01:39:33.880 --> 01:39:36.600
and here we should probably
also talk about things like,

01:39:36.600 --> 01:39:40.520
is it true that ice baths
increase testosterone or not?

01:39:40.520 --> 01:39:43.150
Lifestyle factors that
go beyond the six pillars

01:39:43.150 --> 01:39:44.550
for increasing testosterone.

01:39:44.550 --> 01:39:46.510
If you could comment on
those, that would be terrific.

01:39:46.510 --> 01:39:47.910
Supplements that are useful.

01:39:47.910 --> 01:39:50.310
And it'd be wonderful if you could mention

01:39:50.310 --> 01:39:52.030
where some of these same practices

01:39:52.030 --> 01:39:55.110
and supplements might be
useful for women as well as men

01:39:55.110 --> 01:39:56.330
to increase testosterone

01:39:56.330 --> 01:39:58.170
for all the reasons we
talked about earlier.

01:39:58.170 --> 01:39:59.770
- Yeah, so this is where

01:39:59.770 --> 01:40:02.670
a true individualized approach comes in.

01:40:02.670 --> 01:40:06.480
When you're talking about what
dose of TRT you should be on,

01:40:06.480 --> 01:40:09.480
one thing to keep in mind is
the law of diminishing returns.

01:40:10.680 --> 01:40:13.890
Quality of life is a subjective thing

01:40:13.890 --> 01:40:15.490
and it's different for each person.

01:40:15.490 --> 01:40:18.400
So some people are more willing to give up

01:40:18.400 --> 01:40:21.170
a little bit of athleticism
or body composition.

01:40:21.170 --> 01:40:22.990
Some people are more willing to give up,

01:40:22.990 --> 01:40:26.640
or not willing to give up
libido or sexual health.

01:40:26.640 --> 01:40:28.550
And as we mentioned earlier,

01:40:28.550 --> 01:40:32.590
everybody's androgen receptor
is less or more sensitive.

01:40:32.590 --> 01:40:36.160
So you can make a case that if
somebody's androgen receptor

01:40:36.160 --> 01:40:40.090
is half as sensitive as somebody else,

01:40:40.090 --> 01:40:43.800
the person with the less
sensitive receptor does need

01:40:43.800 --> 01:40:46.660
a level of 1,000 or 1,200.

01:40:46.660 --> 01:40:48.010
There's no great way to know that.

01:40:48.010 --> 01:40:49.913
And you can alter the sensitivity
of your androgen receptor

01:40:49.913 --> 01:40:53.070
with things like L-carnitine
and tadalafil as mentioned.

01:40:53.070 --> 01:40:54.720
- And we'll definitely
come back to L-carnitine,

01:40:54.720 --> 01:40:58.250
because I'm really intrigued
by the data on L-carnitine,

01:40:58.250 --> 01:41:01.010
both for women and men
in terms of egg quality,

01:41:01.010 --> 01:41:02.210
sperm quality, fertility,

01:41:02.210 --> 01:41:03.840
and a bunch of other interesting effects.

01:41:03.840 --> 01:41:05.440
So we'll come back to L-carnitine.

01:41:05.440 --> 01:41:09.960
- But a lot of how you feel,
the biofeedback or subjective,

01:41:09.960 --> 01:41:12.280
I feel like this, comes from the ratio

01:41:12.280 --> 01:41:14.900
of your androgens to your estrogens.

01:41:14.900 --> 01:41:16.650
And a lot of that is lifestyle.

01:41:16.650 --> 01:41:18.300
So if someone's also on hCG,

01:41:18.300 --> 01:41:20.700
that could upregulate aromatase as well.

01:41:20.700 --> 01:41:25.320
- hCG, you might want to just,
human chorionic gonadotropin?

01:41:25.320 --> 01:41:26.153
- [Kyle] Yeah.

01:41:26.153 --> 01:41:27.070
Used to be found in pregnant,

01:41:27.070 --> 01:41:28.430
is still found in pregnant women's urine.

01:41:28.430 --> 01:41:29.568
- Still found in

01:41:29.568 --> 01:41:30.966
pregnant women, yeah.
- But used to be,

01:41:30.966 --> 01:41:32.340
believe it or not,
there was a black market

01:41:32.340 --> 01:41:34.540
for pregnant women's urine

01:41:34.540 --> 01:41:36.940
before this stuff was
developed synthetically.

01:41:36.940 --> 01:41:40.090
So in other words, what
we're saying is men typically

01:41:40.090 --> 01:41:42.650
would buy pregnant women's urine

01:41:42.650 --> 01:41:46.270
through black markets
in order to get the hCG

01:41:46.270 --> 01:41:49.960
in order to get the
testosterone-enhancing effects of hCG.

01:41:49.960 --> 01:41:50.793
So in other words,

01:41:50.793 --> 01:41:52.710
men were using pregnant
women's urine for hCG.

01:41:52.710 --> 01:41:55.210
I do not want to how they
got it into their body.

01:41:55.210 --> 01:41:57.770
Let's just skip to what you
were going to say next instead.

01:41:57.770 --> 01:41:59.933
- Yeah. So that's hCG.

01:42:00.800 --> 01:42:03.200
There's a lot of other things
that upregulate estrogen.

01:42:03.200 --> 01:42:06.690
Alcohol significantly increases aromatase.

01:42:06.690 --> 01:42:08.260
So if you're very sensitive to estrogen,

01:42:08.260 --> 01:42:10.810
then you probably shouldn't even consume

01:42:10.810 --> 01:42:12.563
two glasses three times a week.

01:42:13.580 --> 01:42:16.890
High fat meals also upregulate aromatase.

01:42:16.890 --> 01:42:18.960
So if you're on a ketogenic diet,

01:42:18.960 --> 01:42:21.180
but you have hyperestrogenism,

01:42:21.180 --> 01:42:23.250
then you should take
care with that as well.

01:42:23.250 --> 01:42:25.720
- All kinds of fats or
just saturated fats?

01:42:25.720 --> 01:42:27.610
- I'm not sure if it's
just saturated fats,

01:42:27.610 --> 01:42:29.760
but fat definitely increases,

01:42:29.760 --> 01:42:32.390
both fat and your body and consumption

01:42:32.390 --> 01:42:35.260
of a high amount of calories
increases aromatase.

01:42:35.260 --> 01:42:37.033
- So the it's the ratio of
testosterone and estrogen.

01:42:37.033 --> 01:42:38.040
I don't want to break your flow,

01:42:38.040 --> 01:42:40.090
but since we're talking
about fat, I have to ask,

01:42:40.090 --> 01:42:42.510
since estrogen and testosterone
are both synthesized

01:42:42.510 --> 01:42:44.083
from the cholesterol molecule,

01:42:45.530 --> 01:42:49.580
I've heard that ingesting
some amount of saturated fat

01:42:49.580 --> 01:42:51.850
can be useful because of
the way that cholesterol

01:42:51.850 --> 01:42:55.240
can serve as a precursor
to these molecules.

01:42:55.240 --> 01:42:58.360
Now I once said on a podcast
that I like butter so much

01:42:58.360 --> 01:43:00.100
that I occasionally eat pats of butter.

01:43:00.100 --> 01:43:02.910
Somehow that got misinterpreted to mean

01:43:02.910 --> 01:43:05.406
that I eat entire many pats of butter.

01:43:05.406 --> 01:43:07.460
I'm saying like one or two
pats of butter here and there,

01:43:07.460 --> 01:43:08.780
and I have no guilt or shame about it.

01:43:08.780 --> 01:43:11.560
My blood lipids are in great
shape also, so I feel good.

01:43:11.560 --> 01:43:14.390
But is it possible that people

01:43:14.390 --> 01:43:18.380
who are ingesting too
little of saturated fats

01:43:18.380 --> 01:43:22.820
could directly or indirectly reduce

01:43:22.820 --> 01:43:25.090
or somehow disrupt the
proper ratio of testosterone

01:43:25.090 --> 01:43:27.100
to estrogen in men and women?

01:43:27.100 --> 01:43:28.600
- It's theoretically possible,

01:43:28.600 --> 01:43:31.920
but it probably doesn't
happen in developed countries

01:43:31.920 --> 01:43:33.610
just like it's theoretically possible

01:43:33.610 --> 01:43:36.340
to have not enough omega-6 fatty acids,

01:43:36.340 --> 01:43:38.500
but that probably does not
happen in developed countries.

01:43:38.500 --> 01:43:40.030
- So I don't need the butter pats,

01:43:40.030 --> 01:43:41.650
but I'm going to do it anyway.

01:43:41.650 --> 01:43:42.500
I'm just curious.

01:43:42.500 --> 01:43:43.333
- Yeah.
- Okay.

01:43:43.333 --> 01:43:46.500
- Grass-fed butter has good
omega-3 content as well.

01:43:46.500 --> 01:43:49.800
So grass-fed foods in general.

01:43:49.800 --> 01:43:50.887
It's not the end all be all

01:43:50.887 --> 01:43:53.580
and everybody doesn't
need grass-fed foods,

01:43:53.580 --> 01:43:57.380
but they are one of the only
sources of healthy trans fat.

01:43:57.380 --> 01:44:01.300
So a naturally occurring trans
fat comes from ruminants.

01:44:01.300 --> 01:44:05.150
So ruminants, think of like cows and

01:44:06.660 --> 01:44:09.430
the rumination in the different stomachs

01:44:09.430 --> 01:44:12.480
can change your omega-3 and omega-6

01:44:12.480 --> 01:44:16.850
to trans-linolenic and
trans-linoleic fatty acids.

01:44:16.850 --> 01:44:18.120
- Which are healthy for us.
- Yeah.

01:44:18.120 --> 01:44:20.730
So it's actually omega-3s and omega-6s

01:44:20.730 --> 01:44:24.413
that just happened to have a
trans instead of cis-isomer.

01:44:25.300 --> 01:44:28.220
- And these healthy
trans fats would be found

01:44:28.220 --> 01:44:31.510
in ruminant cheese and milk and butter

01:44:31.510 --> 01:44:33.965
from ruminants and the meat-
- And the meat.

01:44:33.965 --> 01:44:34.840
- And the meats?
- Yes.

01:44:35.730 --> 01:44:38.740
- And for people who are following
a purely plant-based diet

01:44:38.740 --> 01:44:40.940
or mostly plant-based diet,

01:44:40.940 --> 01:44:44.270
are they at risk of not
getting enough of certain types

01:44:44.270 --> 01:44:46.840
of fats or other nutrients to
maintain that healthy ratio

01:44:46.840 --> 01:44:49.310
of testosterone to estrogen or not?

01:44:49.310 --> 01:44:51.580
- If they're a vegetarian,
they're probably not at risk.

01:44:51.580 --> 01:44:54.760
If they're a vegan, they
very well could be at risk.

01:44:54.760 --> 01:44:59.070
Most vegans are aware of this very acutely

01:44:59.070 --> 01:45:00.640
and they'll supplement with

01:45:02.470 --> 01:45:05.600
algae or they'll supplement
with other sources

01:45:05.600 --> 01:45:07.710
of healthy fats.

01:45:07.710 --> 01:45:10.970
- I see, so the takeaway
that I'm drawing from this

01:45:10.970 --> 01:45:14.850
is that less so than
getting saturated fat,

01:45:14.850 --> 01:45:18.390
it's key to get these healthy
trans fats from ruminants.

01:45:18.390 --> 01:45:19.240
- [Kyle] Yes.

01:45:19.240 --> 01:45:21.040
- Or the food products of those ruminants

01:45:21.040 --> 01:45:25.520
as well as to get proper
amounts of omega-3s.

01:45:25.520 --> 01:45:28.240
- Yeah, and to be clear, you
don't need any trans fats.

01:45:28.240 --> 01:45:31.570
It just happens that those
omega-3s and omega-6s

01:45:31.570 --> 01:45:33.580
are in a trans-isomer.

01:45:33.580 --> 01:45:35.310
- I see, okay, so that's nutrition.

01:45:35.310 --> 01:45:37.930
What other supplements can
support healthy testosterone

01:45:37.930 --> 01:45:39.690
to estrogen ratios?

01:45:39.690 --> 01:45:42.530
- Anything that alters aromatase

01:45:42.530 --> 01:45:45.350
can support healthy
testosterone to estrogen.

01:45:45.350 --> 01:45:50.350
And your testosterone to estrogen ratio,

01:45:50.560 --> 01:45:53.800
think about it as how
much estrogen activity

01:45:53.800 --> 01:45:55.860
do you have at the beta estradiol receptor

01:45:55.860 --> 01:45:57.790
and your alpha estradiol receptor.

01:45:57.790 --> 01:45:58.623
- How would I know that?

01:45:58.623 --> 01:46:01.810
- So [chuckles] it's hard to tell,

01:46:01.810 --> 01:46:03.490
but depending on what you're eating,

01:46:03.490 --> 01:46:06.390
if you have a lot of plant-based
diets or polyphenols,

01:46:06.390 --> 01:46:09.530
many of these are beta
estradiol receptors.

01:46:09.530 --> 01:46:13.340
People know about Turkesterone
and also Beta-Ecdysterone,

01:46:13.340 --> 01:46:14.940
which are two ecdysteroids

01:46:14.940 --> 01:46:17.590
that are beta estradiol receptor agonist.

01:46:17.590 --> 01:46:20.610
So they activate the
beta estradiol receptor.

01:46:20.610 --> 01:46:23.140
So if you have a very low
amount of estrogen naturally,

01:46:23.140 --> 01:46:24.800
you're probably a better candidate for it.

01:46:24.800 --> 01:46:26.197
- For taking Turkesterone or ecdysterone?

01:46:26.197 --> 01:46:28.553
- Yeah, ecdysterone.
- I've never tried them,

01:46:28.553 --> 01:46:30.800
but I know my understanding

01:46:30.800 --> 01:46:33.480
is that they work tremendously
well for some people.

01:46:33.480 --> 01:46:35.270
- Yeah.
- And not at all for others.

01:46:35.270 --> 01:46:37.020
And so one just simply has to try.

01:46:37.020 --> 01:46:41.380
But in promoting the activity
of this estrogen receptor,

01:46:41.380 --> 01:46:43.800
is there a risk that
Turkesterone or ecdysterone

01:46:43.800 --> 01:46:47.440
could cause some of the
quote/unquote problems associated

01:46:47.440 --> 01:46:49.780
with increasing estrogen activity,

01:46:49.780 --> 01:46:52.860
like reduced libido, water retention?

01:46:52.860 --> 01:46:54.943
- Water retention, yes.

01:46:55.930 --> 01:46:58.360
Reduced libido, probably not.

01:46:58.360 --> 01:47:00.220
Closing growth plates in the bone, no,

01:47:00.220 --> 01:47:03.140
because that's the
alpha-estradiol receptor.

01:47:03.140 --> 01:47:04.610
- I've talked before on a couple

01:47:04.610 --> 01:47:08.020
of podcasts about tongkat ali,

01:47:08.020 --> 01:47:10.120
which is Indonesian herb, I guess,

01:47:10.120 --> 01:47:13.220
is also made and found in Malaysia.

01:47:13.220 --> 01:47:16.470
But it seems to be the
Indonesian variety of tongkat ali

01:47:16.470 --> 01:47:19.190
that's most effective for potentially

01:47:19.190 --> 01:47:21.750
for reducing sex hormone
and binding globulin

01:47:21.750 --> 01:47:24.230
and thereby freeing up testosterone.

01:47:24.230 --> 01:47:26.390
Whether or not the effects
are through that pathway,

01:47:26.390 --> 01:47:27.740
through another pathway,

01:47:27.740 --> 01:47:31.530
a lot of people report
improvements in things like libido

01:47:31.530 --> 01:47:36.120
and maybe androgen-like phenotypes, right?

01:47:36.120 --> 01:47:37.650
Feeling more vital, et cetera.

01:47:37.650 --> 01:47:40.540
And of course, some of that
could be placebo, correct?

01:47:40.540 --> 01:47:42.590
But what are your thoughts on tongkat ali?

01:47:42.590 --> 01:47:45.100
And please challenge my
statements about tongkat ali

01:47:45.100 --> 01:47:46.080
if they're incorrect.

01:47:46.080 --> 01:47:48.120
I'm not looking for validation here.

01:47:48.120 --> 01:47:50.470
I just really want to know
what your thoughts are on it.

01:47:50.470 --> 01:47:54.160
Do you ever recommend
it to patients, when?

01:47:54.160 --> 01:47:56.580
Men, women, one or the other?

01:47:56.580 --> 01:47:59.600
- Yeah, so tongkat ali or longjack

01:48:00.760 --> 01:48:02.440
has multiple mechanisms of action

01:48:02.440 --> 01:48:04.630
and there have been several

01:48:04.630 --> 01:48:06.840
placebo controlled studies on it.

01:48:06.840 --> 01:48:09.090
Some of them show decrease in SHBG,

01:48:09.090 --> 01:48:12.370
at least one of them did
not show any change in SHBG.

01:48:12.370 --> 01:48:16.380
However, it does act on
aromatase very weakly.

01:48:16.380 --> 01:48:18.260
Probably not so strongly
that you would have

01:48:18.260 --> 01:48:20.763
to be concerned of hypoestrogenism.

01:48:20.763 --> 01:48:23.870
- So it reduces aromatase and thereby

01:48:23.870 --> 01:48:24.810
can reduce estrogen.

01:48:24.810 --> 01:48:25.643
- Correct.
- Okay.

01:48:25.643 --> 01:48:28.560
- It's also a weak, it's not SERM,

01:48:28.560 --> 01:48:31.630
so it's not a selective
estrogen receptor modifier,

01:48:31.630 --> 01:48:34.950
but it's probably a weak,
it's probably an ERM as well

01:48:34.950 --> 01:48:38.370
or a non-selective
estrogen receptor modifier.

01:48:38.370 --> 01:48:40.290
And that should help

01:48:40.290 --> 01:48:42.850
with decreasing negative
feedback inhibition

01:48:42.850 --> 01:48:45.830
of estradiol in various locations

01:48:45.830 --> 01:48:47.930
and also increasing testosterone.

01:48:47.930 --> 01:48:48.763
- Interesting, yeah,

01:48:48.763 --> 01:48:51.510
the dosage that I've been
using for years now is,

01:48:51.510 --> 01:48:54.083
it's 400 milligrams taken once a day,

01:48:55.230 --> 01:48:57.430
typically early in the day,
'cause it can kind of have

01:48:57.430 --> 01:48:59.563
a mild stimulant effect, very mild.

01:49:00.847 --> 01:49:02.550
And I know that some of
the products out there

01:49:02.550 --> 01:49:04.370
recommend dosages that are much higher.

01:49:04.370 --> 01:49:07.950
Anytime I've taken more than
400, I don't feel very good.

01:49:07.950 --> 01:49:09.690
I don't know how to describe it other than

01:49:09.690 --> 01:49:12.100
it's just a little overly
stimulatory in terms

01:49:12.100 --> 01:49:13.910
of makes me kind of,

01:49:13.910 --> 01:49:15.380
it's like drinking too much coffee.

01:49:15.380 --> 01:49:16.350
- [Kyle] Yeah.

01:49:16.350 --> 01:49:18.510
- So that's interesting.

01:49:18.510 --> 01:49:22.840
And so would women ever
want to take tongkat ali

01:49:22.840 --> 01:49:23.730
for any reason?

01:49:23.730 --> 01:49:25.070
- Yeah, absolutely.

01:49:25.070 --> 01:49:27.670
So there's a lot of women
that have hyperestrogenism

01:49:28.800 --> 01:49:31.620
and unlike adrenal fatigue or andropause,

01:49:31.620 --> 01:49:35.118
there's actually ICD 10
codes for hypoestrogenism.

01:49:35.118 --> 01:49:36.520
- ICD 10 codes?
- Yeah.

01:49:36.520 --> 01:49:37.353
- That's doctor speak, right?
- Yeah.

01:49:37.353 --> 01:49:39.180
- Okay.
- So there's codes

01:49:39.180 --> 01:49:40.130
to where your doctor

01:49:40.130 --> 01:49:41.530
can actually diagnose you with something.

01:49:41.530 --> 01:49:43.110
So if you go to your doctor and you say,

01:49:43.110 --> 01:49:45.900
I have adrenal fatigue, they
can't diagnose you with that.

01:49:45.900 --> 01:49:47.290
Or if you say I have andropause,

01:49:47.290 --> 01:49:49.293
they also can't diagnose you with that.

01:49:50.420 --> 01:49:52.870
But if you say you have hypoestrogenism,

01:49:52.870 --> 01:49:55.050
the most common complaint
that comes with it

01:49:55.050 --> 01:49:58.570
is endometriosis, which is
overgrowth of the lining

01:49:58.570 --> 01:50:00.360
of the uterus.

01:50:00.360 --> 01:50:03.350
And those people could potentially,

01:50:03.350 --> 01:50:06.480
I think, that's one
area where we might see

01:50:06.480 --> 01:50:09.560
tongkat supplementation more and more,

01:50:09.560 --> 01:50:11.950
because not only does
it decrease aromatase.

01:50:11.950 --> 01:50:12.783
Like we mentioned,

01:50:12.783 --> 01:50:14.110
testosterone in females is higher

01:50:14.110 --> 01:50:15.810
than estrogen in females.

01:50:15.810 --> 01:50:19.590
So a lot of females get estrogen
from aromatization as well.

01:50:19.590 --> 01:50:21.930
Peripheral estrogen is
sometimes what we call it,

01:50:21.930 --> 01:50:25.000
because it's not directly
produced in the ovaries.

01:50:25.000 --> 01:50:26.740
But they could be good
candidates for tongkat

01:50:26.740 --> 01:50:27.940
if that's the case.

01:50:27.940 --> 01:50:29.510
- Very interesting and my understanding

01:50:29.510 --> 01:50:30.970
is that people should
be looking for sources

01:50:30.970 --> 01:50:33.480
of Indonesian tongkat ali in particular.

01:50:33.480 --> 01:50:34.313
- Correct.
- Right.

01:50:34.313 --> 01:50:38.090
- Another interesting
application is essentially a,

01:50:38.090 --> 01:50:39.430
I'll call it a PCT,

01:50:39.430 --> 01:50:41.194
but essentially-
- What that means is?

01:50:41.194 --> 01:50:44.410
- PCT means, I'll defined
it as post-cycle therapy.

01:50:44.410 --> 01:50:46.470
- Physicians love acronyms,
scientists love acronyms,

01:50:46.470 --> 01:50:48.453
military love acronym, but we, yeah.

01:50:48.453 --> 01:50:50.790
PCT, post cycle therapy, so
this would be people coming

01:50:50.790 --> 01:50:52.320
off hormone therapy or steroids.

01:50:52.320 --> 01:50:54.770
- This would actually be for
women that are coming off

01:50:54.770 --> 01:50:56.230
of their birth control pill,

01:50:56.230 --> 01:50:59.200
because perhaps it can help
lower that SHBG back to normal,

01:50:59.200 --> 01:51:01.660
which is sometimes persistently elevated,

01:51:01.660 --> 01:51:02.810
and then it can help prevent

01:51:02.810 --> 01:51:05.830
the subsequent
hypoestrogenism that happens.

01:51:05.830 --> 01:51:07.650
- Does tongkat ali need to be cycled?

01:51:07.650 --> 01:51:09.620
When I first started taking
it, I would cycle it.

01:51:09.620 --> 01:51:11.230
I would do a few, three, four months,

01:51:11.230 --> 01:51:12.190
and I would take some time off.

01:51:12.190 --> 01:51:15.108
Now I've just been taking
it continuously for years.

01:51:15.108 --> 01:51:15.941
- [Kyle] Yeah.

01:51:15.941 --> 01:51:16.900
- And I should say I do blood work

01:51:16.900 --> 01:51:19.960
to check my liver enzymes
and everything else and

01:51:19.960 --> 01:51:21.560
I don't see any reason

01:51:21.560 --> 01:51:23.660
for me to cease taking it.

01:51:23.660 --> 01:51:25.810
- Yeah. Probably not.

01:51:25.810 --> 01:51:28.630
There's been human studies
on both tongkat and Fadogia.

01:51:28.630 --> 01:51:29.780
And full disclosure,

01:51:29.780 --> 01:51:32.230
I did help design Derek's new

01:51:32.230 --> 01:51:34.190
testosterone optimization supplement,

01:51:34.190 --> 01:51:36.440
which has both Fadogia agrestis

01:51:36.440 --> 01:51:38.140
and also tongkat ali in it.

01:51:38.140 --> 01:51:40.390
- Yeah. Let's talk about
Fadogia separately in a moment.

01:51:40.390 --> 01:51:44.670
But let's say someone is
only taking tongkat ali

01:51:44.670 --> 01:51:48.280
for whatever reason, do
they need to cycle off?

01:51:48.280 --> 01:51:51.010
- Likely not, but I would just to be safe,

01:51:51.010 --> 01:51:54.130
because it does both affect your aromatase

01:51:54.130 --> 01:51:57.870
and it's an estrogen receptor modifier.

01:51:57.870 --> 01:52:00.980
- And what would be a
reasonable cycle off?

01:52:00.980 --> 01:52:03.830
So how long to take and how long to stop

01:52:03.830 --> 01:52:04.960
before taking it again?

01:52:04.960 --> 01:52:07.850
- Yeah, there's a couple
different protocols

01:52:07.850 --> 01:52:08.683
that you can do,

01:52:08.683 --> 01:52:11.850
but 11 months on, 1 month off for tongkat

01:52:11.850 --> 01:52:13.210
is pretty reasonable.

01:52:13.210 --> 01:52:14.740
Now I guess this is,

01:52:14.740 --> 01:52:15.880
we'll talk about this later too,

01:52:15.880 --> 01:52:17.980
but if it's combined with Fadogia,

01:52:17.980 --> 01:52:21.310
the protocol that I would
do is three weeks on,

01:52:21.310 --> 01:52:23.080
one week off.

01:52:23.080 --> 01:52:24.150
- So that's tongkat ali.

01:52:24.150 --> 01:52:28.370
But I'm curious what your
thoughts are on Fadogia agrestis,

01:52:28.370 --> 01:52:32.730
this Nigerian shrub or this
extract from Nigerian shrubs

01:52:32.730 --> 01:52:34.340
that at least in my experience,

01:52:34.340 --> 01:52:35.670
in my read of the literature,

01:52:35.670 --> 01:52:38.290
has the potential to increase testosterone

01:52:38.290 --> 01:52:40.680
and probably other hormones as well

01:52:40.680 --> 01:52:42.860
by way of increasing luteinizing hormone.

01:52:42.860 --> 01:52:44.750
Something that we haven't
really talked about much

01:52:44.750 --> 01:52:45.880
up until now.

01:52:45.880 --> 01:52:48.380
What are your thoughts
about Fadogia agrestis?

01:52:48.380 --> 01:52:51.250
What are your ideas about
the proposed mechanism

01:52:51.250 --> 01:52:55.090
or mechanisms and where
might this be useful

01:52:55.090 --> 01:52:59.483
for people on or off
hormone replacement therapy?

01:53:00.320 --> 01:53:04.480
- Yeah, Fadogia agrestis
has just reached a point

01:53:04.480 --> 01:53:06.670
where we have enough evidence till we know

01:53:06.670 --> 01:53:10.370
it probably helps both with
luteinizing hormone release,

01:53:10.370 --> 01:53:12.370
which stimulates Leydig
cells in the testes

01:53:12.370 --> 01:53:14.150
to produce more testosterone.

01:53:14.150 --> 01:53:18.520
And probably with LH receptor sensitivity

01:53:18.520 --> 01:53:20.920
as well, which is a good
combination of the two.

01:53:22.090 --> 01:53:24.520
It does come from the Nigerian shrub,

01:53:24.520 --> 01:53:28.710
but there is not quite
enough evidence for me

01:53:28.710 --> 01:53:30.660
to be able to say

01:53:30.660 --> 01:53:33.370
it's safe for someone to
take this all the time,

01:53:33.370 --> 01:53:35.080
which again, full disclosure,

01:53:35.080 --> 01:53:36.940
that's why I recommended that we

01:53:38.090 --> 01:53:41.710
recommended for people
to cycle this supplement.

01:53:41.710 --> 01:53:46.490
So three weeks on, one week
off, that's likely safe.

01:53:46.490 --> 01:53:49.020
The only toxicity studies in general are

01:53:49.020 --> 01:53:51.610
in rats and in humans,
it looks quite safe.

01:53:51.610 --> 01:53:54.610
- My understanding is
that the toxicity studies

01:53:54.610 --> 01:53:59.610
in rats showed toxicity
to the testicular cells,

01:53:59.800 --> 01:54:01.180
so that's certainly concerning,

01:54:01.180 --> 01:54:05.270
but that the dosages that
were used or translating

01:54:05.270 --> 01:54:08.640
the dosages used to humans would lead

01:54:08.640 --> 01:54:10.490
to a situation where
the dosages that humans

01:54:10.490 --> 01:54:12.460
would have to take would
be very, very large.

01:54:12.460 --> 01:54:15.780
So the amount of, I no
longer take Fadogia,

01:54:15.780 --> 01:54:18.887
but I took it at 600 milligrams
per day for a long time.

01:54:18.887 --> 01:54:22.320
And I ceased taking it
because I was experimenting

01:54:22.320 --> 01:54:25.490
with other things and I didn't
want to confound those things.

01:54:25.490 --> 01:54:27.293
Not because I had any
negative side effects.

01:54:27.293 --> 01:54:29.800
In fact, I was monitoring blood work,

01:54:29.800 --> 01:54:33.180
and other biological parameters
that would've told me

01:54:33.180 --> 01:54:35.977
if there was testicular
toxicity, and there wasn't.

01:54:35.977 --> 01:54:36.890
Let's put it that way.

01:54:36.890 --> 01:54:38.450
- Yeah. I think it's extremely safe.

01:54:38.450 --> 01:54:41.850
And I'm just not convinced

01:54:41.850 --> 01:54:44.220
that there's enough overwhelming evidence

01:54:44.220 --> 01:54:48.790
for longterm consistent administration.

01:54:48.790 --> 01:54:53.370
- So do you recommend this to
people who are not taking TRT

01:54:53.370 --> 01:54:55.550
and do you recommend to men and women?

01:54:55.550 --> 01:54:58.670
- Yeah, so if you have a really high LH,

01:54:58.670 --> 01:55:01.310
then there's probably a gonadal issue,

01:55:01.310 --> 01:55:03.960
whether it's heat damage to
the testes, a varicocele,

01:55:05.250 --> 01:55:06.980
a history of testicular cancer

01:55:06.980 --> 01:55:09.200
where your LH is going to be higher.

01:55:09.200 --> 01:55:11.260
So if your LH is already very high,

01:55:11.260 --> 01:55:14.040
increasing it even more is
probably not going to help.

01:55:14.040 --> 01:55:16.120
However, if your LH is low,

01:55:16.120 --> 01:55:18.300
then obviously try to find out is it low?

01:55:18.300 --> 01:55:20.920
Is it deficient or is it
just a little bit low?

01:55:20.920 --> 01:55:23.360
If it's low and you don't
have an issue with prolactin,

01:55:23.360 --> 01:55:26.880
you don't have an issue with
opioid receptor antagonism,

01:55:26.880 --> 01:55:29.650
and naltrexone can actually
potentially help antagonize

01:55:29.650 --> 01:55:31.260
that to increase LH as well,

01:55:31.260 --> 01:55:34.400
especially in people
recovering from opiates

01:55:34.400 --> 01:55:36.380
or likely even alcohol.

01:55:36.380 --> 01:55:39.530
So you're looking for a
subclinical secondary hypogonadism,

01:55:39.530 --> 01:55:41.950
which is essentially, just
think of that as low LH.

01:55:41.950 --> 01:55:45.830
So in people with that lower
LH and their estrogen is fine

01:55:45.830 --> 01:55:48.120
and their prolactin is fine,

01:55:48.120 --> 01:55:51.640
then Fadogia is a
particularly good option.

01:55:51.640 --> 01:55:53.410
- Interesting, so three weeks on,

01:55:53.410 --> 01:55:57.860
one week off for 600 milligrams Fadogia,

01:55:57.860 --> 01:56:00.810
400 milligrams tongkat
ali, Indonesian tongkat ali

01:56:01.810 --> 01:56:02.937
could potentially you be good.

01:56:02.937 --> 01:56:04.410
And of course, everyone
should always check

01:56:04.410 --> 01:56:05.260
with their physician,

01:56:05.260 --> 01:56:07.130
clear this, do blood work, et cetera.

01:56:07.130 --> 01:56:09.120
I always say we don't just
say that to protect us.

01:56:09.120 --> 01:56:12.853
We say that to protect
you, meaning the consumer.

01:56:13.861 --> 01:56:15.480
And it's very, very important.

01:56:15.480 --> 01:56:16.750
You don't want to get,

01:56:16.750 --> 01:56:18.860
you don't want to fly blind
with any of the stuff.

01:56:18.860 --> 01:56:20.320
You want to do blood work, right?

01:56:20.320 --> 01:56:21.960
- That's the catch-22 with supplements

01:56:21.960 --> 01:56:24.160
is most of them are
safer than medications,

01:56:24.160 --> 01:56:26.520
but the only difference
between them and a medication

01:56:26.520 --> 01:56:28.690
is one's prescribed and one's not.

01:56:28.690 --> 01:56:30.100
- And oftentimes with supplements,

01:56:30.100 --> 01:56:32.500
it's unclear whether or not
what's listed on the bottle

01:56:32.500 --> 01:56:33.880
is actually what's in the bottle but.

01:56:33.880 --> 01:56:34.713
- Yeah.

01:56:34.713 --> 01:56:37.440
- But I think there are a
number of reputable brands now.

01:56:39.980 --> 01:56:41.360
The other supplement I want to talk about

01:56:41.360 --> 01:56:44.620
in terms of testosterone
augmentation is boron.

01:56:44.620 --> 01:56:47.930
What is boron thought to do?
Does it actually do that?

01:56:47.930 --> 01:56:50.400
And do you ever recommend boron?

01:56:50.400 --> 01:56:53.320
- Yeah, so boron is actually an element.

01:56:53.320 --> 01:56:55.880
And you can find it on the periodic table.

01:56:55.880 --> 01:56:59.100
It's more plentiful in rich soils.

01:56:59.100 --> 01:57:03.120
So frequent farming can
deplete the soils of boron.

01:57:03.120 --> 01:57:04.950
It's very plentiful in
the Mediterranean area

01:57:04.950 --> 01:57:06.430
like Greece and Turkey,

01:57:06.430 --> 01:57:09.410
so a lot of people will
just eat dates or raisins

01:57:09.410 --> 01:57:10.398
that are grown there.

01:57:10.398 --> 01:57:11.606
- I thought you were going
to tell me people eat dirt,

01:57:11.606 --> 01:57:12.439
but there are people

01:57:12.439 --> 01:57:13.272
who eat dirt.
- There are people

01:57:13.272 --> 01:57:14.910
who eat dirt.
- And there's a phenomenon

01:57:14.910 --> 01:57:15.890
called pica, right?

01:57:15.890 --> 01:57:19.270
Where people in a, and that's
not a good thing, they-

01:57:19.270 --> 01:57:21.100
- Often assign a iron deficiency.

01:57:21.100 --> 01:57:23.340
- Okay, but they're
eating grapes and dates

01:57:23.340 --> 01:57:26.251
that were grown in soil that
has high amounts of boron.

01:57:26.251 --> 01:57:27.210
Is that right?
- Yeah.

01:57:27.210 --> 01:57:30.300
Yep, so boron can help regulate SHBG,

01:57:30.300 --> 01:57:32.690
but its effect is mostly acute.

01:57:32.690 --> 01:57:36.040
So it's unlikely to have a bad effect,

01:57:36.040 --> 01:57:37.330
so a lot of people take boron

01:57:37.330 --> 01:57:39.530
because it's probably not going to hurt

01:57:39.530 --> 01:57:43.070
and it will lower SHBG even if it

01:57:43.070 --> 01:57:45.410
is for a short period of time.

01:57:45.410 --> 01:57:47.730
So I guess you could make a
case that maybe cycling boron

01:57:47.730 --> 01:57:48.800
can help too.

01:57:48.800 --> 01:57:49.880
- What sorts of dosages

01:57:49.880 --> 01:57:52.860
are useful for boron supplementation?

01:57:52.860 --> 01:57:55.150
- Three to six milligrams
once to twice a day.

01:57:55.150 --> 01:57:57.200
- Oh, interesting, so that's
higher than the amounts

01:57:57.200 --> 01:57:58.610
that I've been taking.

01:57:58.610 --> 01:58:02.070
I've long been doing this
cocktail of tongkat ali,

01:58:02.070 --> 01:58:03.570
again, I stopped taking Fadogia,

01:58:03.570 --> 01:58:07.120
but for a long time
with Fadogia, and boron,

01:58:07.120 --> 01:58:08.890
I think it was two to
four milligrams per day,

01:58:08.890 --> 01:58:10.440
but maybe I could afford to go higher.

01:58:10.440 --> 01:58:13.500
Although my blood work is
where I want it, thankfully.

01:58:13.500 --> 01:58:15.253
So circling back to Fadogia.

01:58:16.093 --> 01:58:19.160
Fadogia was attractive
to me as a supplement,

01:58:19.160 --> 01:58:22.100
because I saw increases
in LH, testosterone,

01:58:22.100 --> 01:58:23.520
and free testosterone.

01:58:23.520 --> 01:58:25.360
My estrogen stayed in check,

01:58:25.360 --> 01:58:29.610
but I also did not see
a down-regulation of LH

01:58:29.610 --> 01:58:31.620
when I would cycle off.

01:58:31.620 --> 01:58:35.630
Whereas with hCG, human
chorionic gonadotropin,

01:58:35.630 --> 01:58:38.230
which does now arrive

01:58:39.380 --> 01:58:41.750
in forms not from pregnant
women's urine only,

01:58:41.750 --> 01:58:43.970
but the synthetic forms
that people inject,

01:58:43.970 --> 01:58:44.960
that, as I understand,

01:58:44.960 --> 01:58:47.480
it can actually suppress
endogenous hormone output

01:58:49.120 --> 01:58:50.590
if one takes it for a long period of time.

01:58:50.590 --> 01:58:54.080
So why would a man or
woman want to take hCG?

01:58:54.080 --> 01:58:58.290
And what are the potential risks
and benefits of taking hCG?

01:58:58.290 --> 01:59:01.810
- Yeah, so hCG or human
chorionic gonadotropin

01:59:01.810 --> 01:59:03.983
is actually very similar to TSH.

01:59:04.890 --> 01:59:06.120
- Thyroid stimulating hormone?

01:59:06.120 --> 01:59:09.900
- Correct, so when a woman is pregnant,

01:59:09.900 --> 01:59:11.970
she produces more hCG,

01:59:11.970 --> 01:59:14.130
especially in the first trimester.

01:59:14.130 --> 01:59:15.450
When you take a pregnancy test,

01:59:15.450 --> 01:59:17.870
whether it's qualitative or quantitative,

01:59:17.870 --> 01:59:19.890
you see the hCG rise,

01:59:19.890 --> 01:59:22.730
and it actually doubles every 48 hours.

01:59:22.730 --> 01:59:26.270
So if you're five weeks pregnant,
you can get a hCG level.

01:59:26.270 --> 01:59:29.030
And then two days later,
five weeks and two days,

01:59:29.030 --> 01:59:30.190
you can see your hCG,

01:59:30.190 --> 01:59:33.210
and maybe it went from 500 to 1,000.

01:59:33.210 --> 01:59:36.013
So it precipitously increases.

01:59:37.420 --> 01:59:39.050
It does a few things.

01:59:39.050 --> 01:59:42.010
One thing is it prevents hypothyroidism

01:59:42.010 --> 01:59:44.810
or hypothyroxinemia of pregnancy,

01:59:44.810 --> 01:59:48.270
which is one of the most
common causes of miscarriage.

01:59:48.270 --> 01:59:51.300
It's also why if you are,

01:59:51.300 --> 01:59:53.870
if you have hypothyroidism
and you get pregnant

01:59:53.870 --> 01:59:54.920
in the first trimester,

01:59:54.920 --> 01:59:58.850
you want to increase
your dose from 25 to 40%

01:59:58.850 --> 02:00:02.210
to keep your free T4
high as much as possible.

02:00:02.210 --> 02:00:04.060
And the reason why you have to do that

02:00:04.060 --> 02:00:07.380
as opposed to somebody who
does not have hypothyroidism,

02:00:07.380 --> 02:00:08.860
is if you have hypothyroidism,

02:00:08.860 --> 02:00:11.780
then likely your thyroid will not respond

02:00:11.780 --> 02:00:15.500
to either TSH or hCG.

02:00:15.500 --> 02:00:18.800
So the increased hCG does
not compensate for that.

02:00:18.800 --> 02:00:20.850
So if you take hCG,

02:00:20.850 --> 02:00:23.610
then it can potentially
improve your thyroid function.

02:00:23.610 --> 02:00:26.643
So that along with selenium
are likely the two best things

02:00:26.643 --> 02:00:28.530
that you can do for thyroid health.

02:00:28.530 --> 02:00:30.250
- hCG and selenium?
- Yeah.

02:00:30.250 --> 02:00:33.070
- Well, I definitely make
sure I get enough selenium

02:00:33.070 --> 02:00:36.270
by eating three to five
Brazil nuts per day.

02:00:36.270 --> 02:00:38.020
- Yeah.
- Which I very much enjoy

02:00:38.020 --> 02:00:39.203
the taste of also.

02:00:40.900 --> 02:00:44.460
Who should take hCG and can hCG suppress

02:00:44.460 --> 02:00:47.050
one's normal luteinizing hormone output?

02:00:47.050 --> 02:00:51.090
- Yeah, it suppresses LH
in a dose-dependent manner.

02:00:51.090 --> 02:00:53.980
So the higher the dose of hCG you take,

02:00:53.980 --> 02:00:55.540
the more it suppresses LH.

02:00:55.540 --> 02:00:57.540
A common dose for fertility,

02:00:57.540 --> 02:01:00.120
fertility is usually
why hCG is prescribed.

02:01:00.120 --> 02:01:01.100
- In men or women?

02:01:01.100 --> 02:01:05.240
- In both, is 10,000 IUs

02:01:05.240 --> 02:01:07.620
all at one time, which is quite a bit.

02:01:07.620 --> 02:01:10.120
- That's a tremendous dose.

02:01:10.120 --> 02:01:11.920
- Yeah, in fact, some formulations,

02:01:11.920 --> 02:01:15.840
some brand names of hCG
come in autoinjector pins

02:01:15.840 --> 02:01:19.010
to where you cannot even
dose lower than 5,000 units

02:01:19.010 --> 02:01:19.843
at a time.

02:01:19.843 --> 02:01:20.676
- Wow.
- Yeah.

02:01:20.676 --> 02:01:22.720
- But I know a number
of people who take hCG

02:01:22.720 --> 02:01:24.550
to maintain testicular function while

02:01:24.550 --> 02:01:28.340
on testosterone therapy or
augmentation of some sort.

02:01:28.340 --> 02:01:30.600
Does it work to do that?

02:01:30.600 --> 02:01:33.573
- Yeah, some people
are on hCG monotherapy.

02:01:34.460 --> 02:01:38.210
It can be slightly better on your lipids

02:01:38.210 --> 02:01:40.150
than being on TRT.

02:01:40.150 --> 02:01:42.460
- Oh, so people are using hCG alone

02:01:42.460 --> 02:01:43.420
as a kind of

02:01:44.270 --> 02:01:46.820
neither sort of a indirect

02:01:46.820 --> 02:01:48.280
hormone augmentation.
- Yeah.

02:01:48.280 --> 02:01:53.280
Some clinics advertise it as
a non-suppressive alternative

02:01:53.950 --> 02:01:56.490
to TRT, but it is suppressive of LH.

02:01:56.490 --> 02:01:58.940
- But it could also increase
estrogen pretty potently?

02:01:58.940 --> 02:01:59.773
- Yeah.

02:01:59.773 --> 02:02:04.490
- And is it true that
increasing LH and/or hCG

02:02:04.490 --> 02:02:08.360
can improve sensitivity of the genitals?

02:02:08.360 --> 02:02:09.400
And is that true for men and women?

02:02:09.400 --> 02:02:11.060
Yeah, I've heard this anecdotally.

02:02:11.060 --> 02:02:14.960
People say hCG makes sexual
activity more pleasurable

02:02:14.960 --> 02:02:17.070
for people because of some,

02:02:17.070 --> 02:02:19.040
is it a direct effect on some

02:02:19.040 --> 02:02:21.830
of the nerve cells in the genitals?

02:02:21.830 --> 02:02:26.390
- Yeah, so LH is also an
agonist in the prostate

02:02:26.390 --> 02:02:29.130
and in genital tissue in general.

02:02:29.130 --> 02:02:32.400
So it's a very common treatment

02:02:32.400 --> 02:02:36.220
for post-finasteride syndrome
or post-5-alpha reductase

02:02:36.220 --> 02:02:38.700
when you've blocked the conversion of DHT

02:02:38.700 --> 02:02:42.600
for a long time, it
helps re-upregulate DHT.

02:02:42.600 --> 02:02:44.450
- So someone who's been taking finasteride

02:02:44.450 --> 02:02:46.783
to prevent hair loss, comes off it,

02:02:48.090 --> 02:02:49.120
maybe 'cause they felt lousy,

02:02:49.120 --> 02:02:51.142
but then feels even lousier for reasons

02:02:51.142 --> 02:02:52.070
that you talked about earlier.

02:02:52.070 --> 02:02:55.550
And then they might use hCG
as a transition treatment

02:02:55.550 --> 02:02:58.990
to transition back to
normal hormone health.

02:02:58.990 --> 02:02:59.823
Is that right?
- Yeah.

02:02:59.823 --> 02:03:02.240
- It's extremely helpful in many cases.

02:03:02.240 --> 02:03:03.600
Now when you come off the hCG,

02:03:03.600 --> 02:03:06.160
then you need to have a
strategy of how to return

02:03:06.160 --> 02:03:08.610
to your normal as fast
as possible as well.

02:03:08.610 --> 02:03:11.540
But it will upregulate those
5-alpha reductase enzymes.

02:03:11.540 --> 02:03:13.120
You have, in your genital skin,

02:03:13.120 --> 02:03:17.170
both scrotal skin and penile
skin, and perineum in general,

02:03:17.170 --> 02:03:20.260
you have, I believe what's
called stratum lucidum.

02:03:20.260 --> 02:03:24.030
It's skin layer that is very, very thin,

02:03:24.030 --> 02:03:28.420
but it has the highest
concentration of 5-alpha reductase.

02:03:28.420 --> 02:03:30.820
So you have a lot of activity.

02:03:30.820 --> 02:03:35.820
And after you've been on something
that inhibits the enzyme,

02:03:35.820 --> 02:03:38.220
the 5-AR enzyme in those tissues,

02:03:38.220 --> 02:03:41.470
then you do something else
to upregulate those enzymes,

02:03:41.470 --> 02:03:43.610
whether it's waiting and taking time,

02:03:43.610 --> 02:03:45.390
whether it's trying tadalafil,

02:03:45.390 --> 02:03:47.970
whether it's trying creatine even,

02:03:47.970 --> 02:03:50.300
or whether it's trying HCG,

02:03:50.300 --> 02:03:51.700
a lot of times those are the go-tos

02:03:51.700 --> 02:03:53.410
for post-finasteride syndrome.

02:03:53.410 --> 02:03:58.070
- Any risks for women
taking HCG on their ability

02:03:58.070 --> 02:04:02.170
to get pregnant or risks generally?

02:04:02.170 --> 02:04:05.240
- Yeah, obviously it'll make
any pregnancy test positive.

02:04:05.240 --> 02:04:07.720
So that's a risk that
some women don't know.

02:04:07.720 --> 02:04:09.880
- So one could, in theory,
fake a pregnancy test

02:04:09.880 --> 02:04:10.950
by injecting hCG.

02:04:10.950 --> 02:04:11.860
- Absolutely.

02:04:11.860 --> 02:04:13.520
- Interesting.
- Yeah.

02:04:13.520 --> 02:04:15.480
- I have no motivation to do that.

02:04:15.480 --> 02:04:16.962
I was just curious.

02:04:16.962 --> 02:04:18.480
[Kyle chuckles]

02:04:18.480 --> 02:04:19.313
- Yeah.

02:04:19.313 --> 02:04:21.403
- What about prolactin?

02:04:22.480 --> 02:04:24.670
The simple version of
this that I was taught,

02:04:24.670 --> 02:04:26.020
because I was taught mainly

02:04:26.020 --> 02:04:28.090
from the neuroendocrine perspective was

02:04:29.030 --> 02:04:31.200
dopamine is a kind of close
cousin of testosterone,

02:04:31.200 --> 02:04:33.440
and also estrogen for that matter,

02:04:33.440 --> 02:04:34.790
drives appetitive behaviors,

02:04:34.790 --> 02:04:38.320
including pursuit of sexual
partners, sex itself,

02:04:38.320 --> 02:04:40.180
motivated behaviors generally,

02:04:40.180 --> 02:04:45.020
then postcopulatory, post-orgasmic states

02:04:45.020 --> 02:04:46.960
are accompanied by a prolactin increase.

02:04:46.960 --> 02:04:48.900
That's the refractory
period for mating in males,

02:04:48.900 --> 02:04:51.530
and maybe even in females as well,

02:04:51.530 --> 02:04:53.980
involved in milk letdown, et cetera.

02:04:53.980 --> 02:04:54.890
What are sort of

02:04:54.890 --> 02:04:57.270
the general contours of syndromes

02:04:57.270 --> 02:04:59.350
or things that people
could be on the lookout for

02:04:59.350 --> 02:05:03.280
of having too much prolactin
or too little prolactin?

02:05:03.280 --> 02:05:05.440
And I'm aware of a number of people

02:05:05.440 --> 02:05:10.120
who take dopamine agonists,
L-tyrosine, cabergoline,

02:05:10.120 --> 02:05:13.050
things like that, to really
boost their dopamine levels.

02:05:13.050 --> 02:05:15.550
And that isn't always a
good thing as it turns out.

02:05:15.550 --> 02:05:18.250
Oftentimes people become
kind of hyper-dopaminergic

02:05:18.250 --> 02:05:19.440
and so they have the drive

02:05:19.440 --> 02:05:23.030
to do all these appetitive
things, fill in the blanks,

02:05:23.030 --> 02:05:25.711
but they don't always have the ability,

02:05:25.711 --> 02:05:26.544
because it seems,

02:05:26.544 --> 02:05:27.860
just as testosterone
and estrogen need to be

02:05:27.860 --> 02:05:29.240
in the proper ratios,

02:05:29.240 --> 02:05:32.350
dopamine and prolactin need to
be in the appropriate ratios.

02:05:32.350 --> 02:05:34.367
So how should we think about

02:05:34.367 --> 02:05:37.520
and perhaps act on our prolactin systems?

02:05:37.520 --> 02:05:39.770
- Absolutely, the way I describe it

02:05:39.770 --> 02:05:41.510
is the dopamine wave pool.

02:05:41.510 --> 02:05:44.210
So if you're increasing
your dopamine too much,

02:05:44.210 --> 02:05:46.270
you're going to overflow and
then you're going to have

02:05:46.270 --> 02:05:47.970
that wave crash too much.

02:05:47.970 --> 02:05:50.100
So you want to have nice even waves

02:05:50.100 --> 02:05:52.150
that are not going too far above the pool

02:05:52.150 --> 02:05:55.050
of dopamine and prolactin will follow.

02:05:55.050 --> 02:05:58.180
So prolactin and estrogen
are quite close cousins.

02:05:58.180 --> 02:06:01.560
Estrogen upregulates a
gene called the PRL gene

02:06:01.560 --> 02:06:03.110
or prolactin gene

02:06:03.110 --> 02:06:06.840
that directly increases
prolactin synthesis.

02:06:06.840 --> 02:06:11.280
So prolactin is going to also inhibit

02:06:11.280 --> 02:06:14.900
the release of testosterone
from the pituitary.

02:06:14.900 --> 02:06:17.500
So if you're using a dopamine agonist,

02:06:17.500 --> 02:06:22.180
then you're to help decrease
the prolactin-producing cells,

02:06:22.180 --> 02:06:25.320
including if you have a
prolactin-producing microadenoma

02:06:25.320 --> 02:06:26.190
in the pituitary.

02:06:26.190 --> 02:06:27.100
- How common are those?

02:06:27.100 --> 02:06:31.310
Because, I mean, I hear a lot
about these hypogonadism or,

02:06:31.310 --> 02:06:34.320
and of course that can be due
to an issue at the testicles

02:06:34.320 --> 02:06:39.070
or hypergonadism could
also be of course in like

02:06:39.070 --> 02:06:41.370
ovarian syndromes and
then there's of course

02:06:41.370 --> 02:06:42.203
the brain side of it

02:06:42.203 --> 02:06:44.070
where the signals aren't
coming from the brain.

02:06:44.070 --> 02:06:46.657
Not enough gonadotropin, not
enough luteinizing hormone.

02:06:46.657 --> 02:06:49.030
And there are ways of teasing this apart

02:06:49.030 --> 02:06:50.770
with an endocrinologist
that are quite elegant

02:06:50.770 --> 02:06:51.603
in fact, right?

02:06:51.603 --> 02:06:54.000
Using stimulating hormones,
too much to dive into here.

02:06:54.000 --> 02:06:56.770
But how often does one actually

02:06:56.770 --> 02:06:59.180
have one of these pituitary tumors?

02:06:59.180 --> 02:07:02.490
I have heard that people that play a lot

02:07:02.490 --> 02:07:05.690
of high contact sport,
so boxing, football,

02:07:05.690 --> 02:07:08.223
people that headed the
soccer ball quite a lot,

02:07:09.480 --> 02:07:14.210
sadly people whose jobs force
them to take head blows for,

02:07:14.210 --> 02:07:15.280
could be military.

02:07:15.280 --> 02:07:17.500
And so they were firing 50 caliber guns

02:07:17.500 --> 02:07:19.210
and the kind of woodpeckering of the brain

02:07:19.210 --> 02:07:20.323
inside of the skull.

02:07:21.380 --> 02:07:24.160
And construction workers
or just a concussion

02:07:24.160 --> 02:07:27.210
can cause the pituitary
to go malfunctional.

02:07:27.210 --> 02:07:30.370
Is that really common or
is this something that

02:07:31.220 --> 02:07:33.340
is a rare like 1%?

02:07:33.340 --> 02:07:34.920
- Yeah, it's extremely common.

02:07:34.920 --> 02:07:36.460
It's another one of those conditions where

02:07:36.460 --> 02:07:39.020
a lot of people never know they have it.

02:07:39.020 --> 02:07:40.950
They just feel a little bit more fatigued.

02:07:40.950 --> 02:07:44.670
They have that high prolactin
feeling all the time.

02:07:44.670 --> 02:07:47.890
Pituitary microadenomas can
be non-producing as well.

02:07:47.890 --> 02:07:49.970
So your prolactin can be totally normal.

02:07:49.970 --> 02:07:52.190
Your growth hormone and
IGF-1 can be totally normal.

02:07:52.190 --> 02:07:54.850
That's the second most common
producing microadenoma,

02:07:54.850 --> 02:07:57.460
is growth hormone causing
either acromegaly,

02:07:57.460 --> 02:07:59.840
which is growth of cartilage or gigantism.

02:07:59.840 --> 02:08:01.690
- This is the big brow.

02:08:01.690 --> 02:08:02.890
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

02:08:02.890 --> 02:08:05.730
- So those are fairly
common causes of adenomas,

02:08:05.730 --> 02:08:09.053
but a lot of people that
have a very small adenoma,

02:08:09.940 --> 02:08:11.970
much less than one centimeter,

02:08:11.970 --> 02:08:13.510
it's hard to see on imaging

02:08:13.510 --> 02:08:16.960
even if you have a contrast
that specifically looks

02:08:16.960 --> 02:08:20.720
at the pituitary and many
people aren't symptomatic.

02:08:20.720 --> 02:08:24.677
So it's one of those
things along with PCOS

02:08:24.677 --> 02:08:28.810
and pre-diabetes that
are much more frequent

02:08:28.810 --> 02:08:31.590
when it comes to prevalence,
which is the amount,

02:08:31.590 --> 02:08:32.657
the percentage of people that have it

02:08:32.657 --> 02:08:35.130
in the general population.

02:08:35.130 --> 02:08:37.010
- I'm glad you mentioned
the dopamine wave pool.

02:08:37.010 --> 02:08:39.240
I know nowadays there's a lot of interest

02:08:39.240 --> 02:08:40.733
in augmenting dopamine.

02:08:41.670 --> 02:08:42.870
I know a number of people that do this

02:08:42.870 --> 02:08:46.140
through prescription drugs,
Adderall, Ritalin, modafinil,

02:08:46.140 --> 02:08:48.300
and those drugs of course
hit many transmitter systems,

02:08:48.300 --> 02:08:49.830
but dopamine is certainly involved.

02:08:49.830 --> 02:08:53.320
People taking antidepressants
like Wellbutrin tap

02:08:53.320 --> 02:08:55.000
into that system.

02:08:55.000 --> 02:08:58.430
And of course people are
trying to inhibit prolactin

02:08:58.430 --> 02:09:01.140
and promote serotonin or reduce serotonin.

02:09:01.140 --> 02:09:04.480
To me, it all seems like a
very delicate dance, right?

02:09:04.480 --> 02:09:07.220
I mean, to just imagine the a arousal arc

02:09:08.438 --> 02:09:10.600
for mating behavior,
for sexual reproduction,

02:09:10.600 --> 02:09:13.990
is such an in an elaborate
dance between sympathetic drive

02:09:13.990 --> 02:09:15.120
and parasympathetic drive,

02:09:15.120 --> 02:09:17.660
even with across the
span of minutes, right?

02:09:17.660 --> 02:09:19.243
I mean, I've talked about
this before on the podcast

02:09:19.243 --> 02:09:23.120
that the arousal is kind
of more parasympathetic,

02:09:23.120 --> 02:09:26.290
orgasm in itself is a
sympathetic response,

02:09:26.290 --> 02:09:28.090
a completely different set of neurons.

02:09:28.090 --> 02:09:31.540
And so where do you see
people getting into trouble

02:09:31.540 --> 02:09:34.630
just trying to hit the
gas pedal on dopamine

02:09:34.630 --> 02:09:36.140
and where do you think there is a place

02:09:36.140 --> 02:09:39.190
for people who perhaps
are experiencing low drive

02:09:39.190 --> 02:09:42.350
and motivation, not just
sexual, but in general,

02:09:42.350 --> 02:09:44.770
to increase the amount
of dopamine circulating

02:09:44.770 --> 02:09:45.950
in their brain and body?

02:09:45.950 --> 02:09:46.950
How do you think about that,

02:09:46.950 --> 02:09:49.420
given this wave pool analogy?

02:09:49.420 --> 02:09:51.420
- Yeah, so it's important to parse it out

02:09:51.420 --> 02:09:55.230
and start with the least
powerful interventions.

02:09:55.230 --> 02:09:57.350
So if someone's concerned about dopamine

02:09:57.350 --> 02:09:59.960
or maybe they have a
slightly higher prolactin,

02:09:59.960 --> 02:10:01.010
then they eliminate things

02:10:01.010 --> 02:10:03.550
that could be increasing that prolactin.

02:10:03.550 --> 02:10:06.630
- Such as?
- Casein or gluten,

02:10:06.630 --> 02:10:09.360
which are mu opioid receptor agonists

02:10:09.360 --> 02:10:12.560
or any mu opioid receptor
agonist in the gut.

02:10:12.560 --> 02:10:14.380
- Casein, so milk protein?

02:10:14.380 --> 02:10:16.110
- Correct.
- Can increase prolactin?

02:10:16.110 --> 02:10:17.210
- Correct.

02:10:17.210 --> 02:10:18.043
- Interesting.

02:10:18.043 --> 02:10:19.080
- In addition to that,

02:10:19.080 --> 02:10:22.240
they should, if they need a pituitary MRI,

02:10:22.240 --> 02:10:23.830
then they should get a pituitary MRI.

02:10:23.830 --> 02:10:25.210
If they don't have an adenoma

02:10:25.210 --> 02:10:27.490
or if they don't have a
high enough prolactin level

02:10:27.490 --> 02:10:29.640
to where they need an MRI,

02:10:29.640 --> 02:10:31.050
if they're having visual symptoms,

02:10:31.050 --> 02:10:33.920
or if they're having olfactory
symptoms with the nose,

02:10:33.920 --> 02:10:35.670
then it's more likely that they do.

02:10:36.810 --> 02:10:38.420
But if they don't,

02:10:38.420 --> 02:10:40.910
a lot of times a prolactin under about 40

02:10:40.910 --> 02:10:42.740
is not too big of a deal.

02:10:42.740 --> 02:10:46.700
They can take dopamine agonist
that agonize that D2 receptor

02:10:46.700 --> 02:10:51.010
like P5P, which is essentially vitamin B6.

02:10:51.010 --> 02:10:53.494
It's pyridoxine-5-pyrophosphate.

02:10:53.494 --> 02:10:55.720
And pyridoxine is vitamin B6.

02:10:55.720 --> 02:10:59.490
So that can help, 50
milligrams once to twice a day.

02:10:59.490 --> 02:11:01.460
Vitamin E can also help,

02:11:01.460 --> 02:11:03.660
especially if it's mixed to tocopherols.

02:11:03.660 --> 02:11:07.530
A lot of people have
high levels of vitamin E,

02:11:07.530 --> 02:11:11.060
but low levels of the
gamma form of vitamin E.

02:11:11.060 --> 02:11:12.340
So that can also help.

02:11:12.340 --> 02:11:17.180
- Fascinating, I'm so glad you
mentioned vitamin B6 and P5P.

02:11:17.180 --> 02:11:19.160
I have heard

02:11:19.160 --> 02:11:21.640
that one can shorten the refractory period

02:11:22.787 --> 02:11:26.640
after orgasm, essentially to
be able to have sex again,

02:11:26.640 --> 02:11:28.040
to be quite direct about it,

02:11:29.241 --> 02:11:32.890
by way of vitamin B6 blunting
of the prolactin response,

02:11:32.890 --> 02:11:34.563
which turns out to quite potent.

02:11:35.430 --> 02:11:38.340
But I've also heard that
vitamin B6 can be neurotoxic,

02:11:38.340 --> 02:11:39.590
especially in the periphery,

02:11:39.590 --> 02:11:41.170
that it can cause peripheral neuropathies

02:11:41.170 --> 02:11:42.770
if it's taken at high doses.

02:11:42.770 --> 02:11:45.590
But that P5P is the safer form.

02:11:45.590 --> 02:11:47.000
Is that true?

02:11:47.000 --> 02:11:50.960
- It's pre-activated,
so it does not build up.

02:11:50.960 --> 02:11:55.320
Think of it as a allegory
to how folate can build up.

02:11:55.320 --> 02:11:57.940
It's not methyl folate,

02:11:57.940 --> 02:12:01.690
but it builds up and it can
increase levels of homocystine.

02:12:01.690 --> 02:12:03.600
Or if you have too much vitamin B12,

02:12:03.600 --> 02:12:05.620
another water soluble B vitamin,

02:12:05.620 --> 02:12:08.830
you can have too much
methylmalonic acid or MMA.

02:12:08.830 --> 02:12:11.530
So depending on what your
enzymatic conversion is

02:12:11.530 --> 02:12:13.470
to the active form of the enzyme,

02:12:13.470 --> 02:12:17.010
often it's just safer to take
the active form of the enzyme.

02:12:17.010 --> 02:12:19.130
- Yeah. Very interesting.
- Yeah.

02:12:19.130 --> 02:12:20.430
- Okay, well, at risk of going

02:12:20.430 --> 02:12:22.180
down every hormonal pathway

02:12:22.180 --> 02:12:24.810
and talking about supplementation,
lifestyle factors,

02:12:24.810 --> 02:12:26.850
I think touching on, as we have,

02:12:26.850 --> 02:12:29.290
testosterone and estrogen,
and now prolactin,

02:12:29.290 --> 02:12:32.140
I'd love to chat a little
bit about L-carnitine.

02:12:32.140 --> 02:12:33.860
We talked about this earlier,

02:12:33.860 --> 02:12:37.050
but I want to raise this
discussion about L-carnitine,

02:12:37.050 --> 02:12:39.330
not in the context of L-carnitine itself,

02:12:39.330 --> 02:12:42.060
but in the context of fertility.

02:12:42.060 --> 02:12:45.300
Because my read of the
literature is that L-carnitine

02:12:45.300 --> 02:12:48.690
can be very beneficial for
enhancing sperm quality

02:12:48.690 --> 02:12:51.713
and egg quality and even
rates of conception.

02:12:53.320 --> 02:12:55.240
What forms does L-carnitine come in

02:12:55.240 --> 02:12:57.890
that people can reasonably consider?

02:12:57.890 --> 02:13:00.600
Again, talk to your doctor, folks.

02:13:00.600 --> 02:13:02.280
What is it doing?

02:13:02.280 --> 02:13:03.590
And do we know how it's doing it?

02:13:03.590 --> 02:13:07.230
And do you often use
this in your patients?

02:13:07.230 --> 02:13:10.330
- Yeah, so the way I
think about L-carnitine,

02:13:10.330 --> 02:13:12.390
and I'll try to tie this in with creatine,

02:13:12.390 --> 02:13:14.000
and other things as well,

02:13:14.000 --> 02:13:17.400
is if your cell is an
energy factory or car,

02:13:17.400 --> 02:13:22.400
then L-carnitine is the
shuttle that helps get the fuel

02:13:22.460 --> 02:13:24.270
into the motor to use the motor.

02:13:24.270 --> 02:13:27.230
The motor is mostly due
to lifestyle factors.

02:13:27.230 --> 02:13:30.600
So like your diet and your exercise.

02:13:30.600 --> 02:13:34.600
And the type of fuel itself is NAD+.

02:13:34.600 --> 02:13:36.860
We don't need to get into
NAD precursors or NMN

02:13:36.860 --> 02:13:38.480
or NR, anything.

02:13:38.480 --> 02:13:42.020
And then the accessory fuel
tank is your creatine phosphate.

02:13:42.020 --> 02:13:44.550
So creatine is your accessory fuel tank.

02:13:44.550 --> 02:13:45.970
Your NAD status,

02:13:45.970 --> 02:13:47.930
which is largely determined
by your REM sleep

02:13:47.930 --> 02:13:50.280
and quality sleep and exercise along

02:13:50.280 --> 02:13:52.330
with supplementation as the fuel,

02:13:52.330 --> 02:13:54.430
the carnitine shuttle is

02:13:55.354 --> 02:13:57.570
carnitine palmitoyl coenzyme A.

02:13:57.570 --> 02:13:59.770
And that takes medium-chain fatty acids,

02:13:59.770 --> 02:14:01.610
it takes different molecules of fat.

02:14:01.610 --> 02:14:04.520
You have two main energy
sources other than ketones.

02:14:04.520 --> 02:14:06.130
You have your glucose or carbs.

02:14:06.130 --> 02:14:08.057
You have your fat or fatty acids.

02:14:08.057 --> 02:14:12.380
And that takes it across the
layer of the mitochondria

02:14:12.380 --> 02:14:13.950
so that it can be utilized.

02:14:13.950 --> 02:14:15.710
So upregulates that,

02:14:15.710 --> 02:14:18.890
that's why things that
have flagella in general,

02:14:18.890 --> 02:14:21.070
the flagella are going to
work better, like sperm.

02:14:21.070 --> 02:14:22.280
- The flagella being anything,

02:14:22.280 --> 02:14:24.820
sort of the wavy little
tenders on cell types

02:14:24.820 --> 02:14:26.030
of which they're everywhere, right?

02:14:26.030 --> 02:14:27.270
In the gut too, right, yeah.

02:14:27.270 --> 02:14:28.103
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

02:14:28.103 --> 02:14:30.250
- So those are going to
work significantly better.

02:14:30.250 --> 02:14:32.870
And in general, you're mitochondria
are going to work better.

02:14:32.870 --> 02:14:35.440
So the worst your
mitochondria are off the bat,

02:14:35.440 --> 02:14:38.510
the better they're going to
be helped by these shuttle

02:14:38.510 --> 02:14:40.330
that shuttles them across.

02:14:40.330 --> 02:14:42.710
It also slightly increases the density

02:14:42.710 --> 02:14:45.000
of the androgen receptor as well.

02:14:45.000 --> 02:14:46.030
- Is that a local effect?

02:14:46.030 --> 02:14:48.540
So if an L-carnitine is injected
into a particular muscle,

02:14:48.540 --> 02:14:50.350
will it increase the density
of androgen receptors

02:14:50.350 --> 02:14:51.490
in that muscle?

02:14:51.490 --> 02:14:52.490
- Likely so.

02:14:52.490 --> 02:14:54.140
- So how are people taking L-carnitine?

02:14:54.140 --> 02:14:56.600
There are capsule forms and
there are injectable forms.

02:14:56.600 --> 02:14:59.020
Most people are going to be
taking the capsule forms,

02:14:59.020 --> 02:15:00.580
because that's all they're
going to have access to.

02:15:00.580 --> 02:15:02.040
And then we should also ask,

02:15:02.040 --> 02:15:04.030
can you get L-carnitine from food?

02:15:04.030 --> 02:15:08.580
- Yeah, so L-carnitine
is just a combination of,

02:15:08.580 --> 02:15:10.380
it's actually a very small peptide.

02:15:10.380 --> 02:15:13.930
So glutathione is just
a three amino acids.

02:15:13.930 --> 02:15:16.830
L-carnitine is the smallest peptide, two.

02:15:16.830 --> 02:15:19.470
So peptide is just a
protein that has amino acids

02:15:19.470 --> 02:15:21.670
between two and about 200.

02:15:21.670 --> 02:15:24.520
And L-carnitine is just two amino acids.

02:15:24.520 --> 02:15:27.250
- Amazing, so it's like a micro-peptide?

02:15:27.250 --> 02:15:29.480
- Yeah, so your body synthesizes enough.

02:15:29.480 --> 02:15:32.150
It likes to absorb the
amino acids by themselves.

02:15:32.150 --> 02:15:34.150
And then if it puts them together,

02:15:34.150 --> 02:15:35.840
there it makes L-carnitine.

02:15:35.840 --> 02:15:38.540
It's not very bioavailable if you take it.

02:15:38.540 --> 02:15:40.560
A lot of people take
L-carnitine, L-tartrate,

02:15:40.560 --> 02:15:42.580
or a acetyl-L-carnitine,

02:15:42.580 --> 02:15:45.260
and that's about 10% bioavailable.

02:15:45.260 --> 02:15:47.703
So if you want 1 gram or 1,000 milligrams

02:15:47.703 --> 02:15:51.680
of L-carnitine, you can take
10 grams of oral L-carnitine.

02:15:51.680 --> 02:15:54.040
- Is the one gram the typical dose,

02:15:54.040 --> 02:15:56.040
you recommend one gram per day?

02:15:56.040 --> 02:15:58.740
- For fertility and androgen
receptor upregulation.

02:15:58.740 --> 02:16:01.510
- So that means taking 10
grams of the capsule form?

02:16:01.510 --> 02:16:05.810
- Yeah. So it's about 15 to
20 capsules, which is a lot.

02:16:05.810 --> 02:16:06.643
- [Andrew] That is a lot.

02:16:06.643 --> 02:16:08.540
- It can also potentially increase TMAO.

02:16:08.540 --> 02:16:09.640
- Yeah, I want to ask about that,

02:16:09.640 --> 02:16:13.600
because TMAO on your blood chart is,

02:16:13.600 --> 02:16:14.433
when that's elevated,

02:16:14.433 --> 02:16:16.340
that's going to cause some concern.

02:16:16.340 --> 02:16:17.380
You taught me a trick,

02:16:17.380 --> 02:16:22.380
however, that one can take 600
milligrams of garlic capsule

02:16:22.930 --> 02:16:24.010
for the allicin.

02:16:24.010 --> 02:16:25.440
Is that what it's called?
- Allicin is in it, yeah.

02:16:25.440 --> 02:16:27.340
- It's like the name
Allison but with two L's?

02:16:27.340 --> 02:16:28.173
- Yeah.
- Okay.

02:16:29.160 --> 02:16:33.400
And that had a remarkable
effect in reducing TMAO.

02:16:33.400 --> 02:16:35.240
So that's quite potent and also

02:16:36.140 --> 02:16:38.680
was it just coincidence that

02:16:38.680 --> 02:16:41.973
it really brought my LDL down as well?

02:16:43.000 --> 02:16:45.270
- I'm not sure if the
LDL is a coincidence,

02:16:45.270 --> 02:16:49.083
but depending on your gut
microbiome or your microbiota,

02:16:49.940 --> 02:16:54.210
some microbiome beneficial bacteria

02:16:54.210 --> 02:16:57.670
will convert carnitine and also choline.

02:16:57.670 --> 02:17:00.000
So any choline precursor like Alpha-GPC

02:17:00.000 --> 02:17:01.725
or phosphatidylserine,

02:17:01.725 --> 02:17:04.500
it'll will convert them
more or less to TMAO.

02:17:04.500 --> 02:17:06.280
So TMAO is something
that you can get measured

02:17:06.280 --> 02:17:08.620
in a blood test and see
if it's high or low.

02:17:08.620 --> 02:17:11.090
Some people might not even need allicin.

02:17:11.090 --> 02:17:11.923
- Interesting.
- Some people

02:17:11.923 --> 02:17:12.830
do benefit from it.

02:17:12.830 --> 02:17:15.810
- Interesting, although I think it was you

02:17:15.810 --> 02:17:16.643
that also told me

02:17:16.643 --> 02:17:19.290
that allicin in garlic
can have positive effects

02:17:20.195 --> 02:17:22.420
on cardiovascular tone
and blood flow generally.

02:17:22.420 --> 02:17:23.253
Is that right?

02:17:23.253 --> 02:17:24.086
- Yeah.
- Okay.

02:17:25.146 --> 02:17:28.490
So is 600 milligrams
garlic an excessive amount

02:17:28.490 --> 02:17:29.650
or can I just eat garlic?

02:17:29.650 --> 02:17:30.483
- You can just eat-
- I mean,

02:17:30.483 --> 02:17:31.340
I like eating garlic.

02:17:31.340 --> 02:17:32.173
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

02:17:32.173 --> 02:17:34.620
So, okay, so one could
also just eat garlic.

02:17:34.620 --> 02:17:37.630
If one were going to take
L-carnitine in injectable form,

02:17:37.630 --> 02:17:39.323
how much of that is bioavailable?

02:17:40.170 --> 02:17:41.990
- 100% if you inject it.

02:17:41.990 --> 02:17:44.060
It is in a aqueous solution,

02:17:44.060 --> 02:17:47.060
so it's bacteria static water essentially.

02:17:47.060 --> 02:17:49.410
So it's not in a carrier oil.

02:17:49.410 --> 02:17:53.480
So it's going to burn a lot if
you inject it subcutaneously.

02:17:53.480 --> 02:17:57.470
So it's going to be absorbed
faster and more evenly

02:17:57.470 --> 02:17:59.960
and also just hurt a lot
less if you inject it

02:17:59.960 --> 02:18:01.350
into a muscle.

02:18:01.350 --> 02:18:05.430
- But one could then just
take one gram per day injected

02:18:05.430 --> 02:18:07.150
or divide it up into a couple doses?

02:18:07.150 --> 02:18:07.990
- Yeah, or 500,

02:18:07.990 --> 02:18:11.350
the minimally efficacious
dose for injectable's probably

02:18:11.350 --> 02:18:14.760
around 200 when it
comes to sperm motility,

02:18:14.760 --> 02:18:16.960
the androgen receptor upregulation.

02:18:16.960 --> 02:18:19.580
So it really depends on
why you're taking it.

02:18:19.580 --> 02:18:20.610
- In terms of fertility,

02:18:20.610 --> 02:18:22.510
and in terms of blood tests generally,

02:18:23.820 --> 02:18:28.060
I always say that if possible,

02:18:28.060 --> 02:18:32.270
either by way of insurance
or by way of some other way,

02:18:32.270 --> 02:18:34.580
affording it, it would be great for people

02:18:34.580 --> 02:18:35.710
to have blood tests

02:18:35.710 --> 02:18:38.330
to know what their hormone
levels and other levels

02:18:38.330 --> 02:18:40.890
of other things like metabolic
markers and lipids were

02:18:40.890 --> 02:18:43.830
in their 20s, also in their
30s, also in their 40s.

02:18:43.830 --> 02:18:46.210
I think there's this idea that
you only take a blood test

02:18:46.210 --> 02:18:48.490
when you have a problem,
but then of course

02:18:48.490 --> 02:18:51.700
one can't actually do the comparison

02:18:51.700 --> 02:18:52.570
that you mentioned earlier

02:18:52.570 --> 02:18:55.470
or state the comparison to one's physician

02:18:55.470 --> 02:18:57.580
that things are changing over time.

02:18:57.580 --> 02:19:00.630
And it seems to me that
basically everyone should get

02:19:00.630 --> 02:19:02.560
at least a once-a-year blood test.

02:19:02.560 --> 02:19:04.600
Is there the hope that insurance

02:19:04.600 --> 02:19:06.120
will someday just cover it for everybody?

02:19:06.120 --> 02:19:07.310
This will be standard care?

02:19:07.310 --> 02:19:10.510
I would think that everybody
should know what sorts

02:19:10.510 --> 02:19:12.150
of things are floating
around in their bloodstream

02:19:12.150 --> 02:19:14.740
and what they need more
of and less of in life.

02:19:14.740 --> 02:19:17.960
- I doubt it will ever
be covered by insurance.

02:19:17.960 --> 02:19:18.793
In many cases,

02:19:18.793 --> 02:19:21.300
you could make an argument
that it's indicated.

02:19:21.300 --> 02:19:23.740
As insurance begins to cover more

02:19:23.740 --> 02:19:26.730
of the population for pathologies,

02:19:26.730 --> 02:19:31.160
the things like FSAs
or HSAs or care credit

02:19:31.160 --> 02:19:34.430
will likely cover this advanced testing,

02:19:34.430 --> 02:19:37.490
which it continues to come
down and down in price.

02:19:37.490 --> 02:19:40.010
So it'll be affordable,
but it won't be free.

02:19:40.010 --> 02:19:41.400
- Got it. Yeah.

02:19:41.400 --> 02:19:42.900
I'd like to shift gears slightly

02:19:42.900 --> 02:19:46.230
and talk about social interactions

02:19:46.230 --> 02:19:49.130
and relational effects on hormones.

02:19:49.130 --> 02:19:50.670
Something that I just find fascinating.

02:19:50.670 --> 02:19:52.240
We touched on this a little bit earlier

02:19:52.240 --> 02:19:53.480
in terms of oral contraception,

02:19:53.480 --> 02:19:55.370
but now that we have the backdrop

02:19:55.370 --> 02:19:57.290
of what these various hormones do,

02:19:57.290 --> 02:20:00.060
some involvement in neurotransmitter
systems like dopamine

02:20:00.060 --> 02:20:02.650
and pro prolactin and associated pathways.

02:20:02.650 --> 02:20:04.830
Prolactin of course being a
hormone. Not a neurotransmitter.

02:20:04.830 --> 02:20:08.950
But there's a phenomenon

02:20:08.950 --> 02:20:12.350
in human beings where people
get very excited about

02:20:12.350 --> 02:20:13.890
a new partner and

02:20:15.240 --> 02:20:16.690
that excitement no doubt is related

02:20:16.690 --> 02:20:19.000
to the dopamine system
among other systems.

02:20:19.000 --> 02:20:22.350
And that excitement can be
maintained or can wane over time.

02:20:22.350 --> 02:20:23.620
And here I'm talking about attraction,

02:20:23.620 --> 02:20:25.460
but I'm also talking about
just general excitement

02:20:25.460 --> 02:20:26.450
in the sense of novelty,

02:20:26.450 --> 02:20:29.380
because that's what
dopamine's associated with.

02:20:29.380 --> 02:20:33.510
Given that you work with human beings

02:20:33.510 --> 02:20:36.560
and they have lives and
relationships and lifestyles,

02:20:36.560 --> 02:20:39.250
and they have hormones, and
all these things interact,

02:20:39.250 --> 02:20:42.360
what are some of the ways
that we could think about

02:20:42.360 --> 02:20:47.360
adjusting our relationships
in order to optimize hormones

02:20:48.090 --> 02:20:51.490
as opposed to just thinking
about how to optimize hormones

02:20:51.490 --> 02:20:52.610
for sake of our relationship?

02:20:52.610 --> 02:20:55.070
Because it's bidirectional of course.

02:20:55.070 --> 02:20:57.910
And this assumes, I should say,

02:20:57.910 --> 02:20:59.910
that one is already paying attention

02:20:59.910 --> 02:21:02.340
to the six pillars talked about earlier,

02:21:02.340 --> 02:21:04.440
that people are doing most things right.

02:21:04.440 --> 02:21:07.140
How should we think about
relationships in hormones:

02:21:07.140 --> 02:21:08.750
friendships, romantic relationships,

02:21:08.750 --> 02:21:11.113
new partners, longterm partners,

02:21:12.580 --> 02:21:15.100
yeah, how do you think
about this kind of stuff?

02:21:15.100 --> 02:21:18.440
- Yeah, so if you have a new partner,

02:21:18.440 --> 02:21:22.180
then it is largely regulated
by the dopaminergic system,

02:21:22.180 --> 02:21:23.510
which changes over time.

02:21:23.510 --> 02:21:25.950
So people may have heard
the saying that you have

02:21:25.950 --> 02:21:28.200
to go through a full calendar year

02:21:28.200 --> 02:21:29.560
with someone that you're in a relationship

02:21:29.560 --> 02:21:30.790
so that you-
- Very good advice,

02:21:30.790 --> 02:21:32.332
by the way.
- So that

02:21:32.332 --> 02:21:34.800
you really know what to
do and what not to do.

02:21:34.800 --> 02:21:37.960
But because you experience
both of your families

02:21:37.960 --> 02:21:40.200
in the holidays and all
the different situations.

02:21:40.200 --> 02:21:44.470
But I would argue until
you have moved in together,

02:21:44.470 --> 02:21:45.303
had a baby,

02:21:45.303 --> 02:21:48.740
and then raised that baby,
preferably breastfeeding,

02:21:48.740 --> 02:21:51.699
because that's when you
get the prolactin spikes,

02:21:51.699 --> 02:21:54.090
you haven't really gone through
every stage in life yet.

02:21:54.090 --> 02:21:55.790
Now you can't really do
that with every person

02:21:55.790 --> 02:21:56.623
that you're considering.

02:21:56.623 --> 02:21:57.470
- Well, some people do,

02:21:57.470 --> 02:22:00.730
but it can be quite
costly in terms of time

02:22:00.730 --> 02:22:03.240
and finances and emotionally costly.

02:22:03.240 --> 02:22:04.378
- Yeah.

02:22:04.378 --> 02:22:05.900
- And then here, I'm
definitely not referring to

02:22:05.900 --> 02:22:06.970
any personal experience

02:22:06.970 --> 02:22:08.730
of having done all that many times over,

02:22:08.730 --> 02:22:12.010
but what would you suggest people

02:22:13.210 --> 02:22:16.587
do or think about as they
enter a relationship or

02:22:16.587 --> 02:22:18.500
for people that are in
longterm relationships

02:22:18.500 --> 02:22:21.210
where they feel like
something has shifted,

02:22:21.210 --> 02:22:24.860
and indeed those shifts
may reflect the output

02:22:24.860 --> 02:22:27.130
of different hormone systems
and neurotransmitter systems.

02:22:27.130 --> 02:22:28.940
It almost certainly has
to be the case, right?

02:22:28.940 --> 02:22:33.580
- Yeah, so just like women who
spend a lot of time together,

02:22:33.580 --> 02:22:35.060
whether they're coworkers or whatever,

02:22:35.060 --> 02:22:38.450
a lot of times their
menstrual cycles will align.

02:22:38.450 --> 02:22:42.040
There is a lot of pheromonal
and hormonal crosstalk,

02:22:42.040 --> 02:22:44.810
including prolactin between men and women.

02:22:44.810 --> 02:22:48.270
So spending 100% of the time together,

02:22:48.270 --> 02:22:51.080
this is why people think
it's so hard to work together

02:22:51.080 --> 02:22:51.950
and live together.

02:22:51.950 --> 02:22:54.230
They're around each other 24/7.

02:22:54.230 --> 02:22:57.230
You don't have the reprieve where you let

02:22:57.230 --> 02:22:58.310
that dopamine settle down,

02:22:58.310 --> 02:23:00.160
and then you're excited
when you see them again.

02:23:00.160 --> 02:23:03.050
A lot of guys know that if they've gone on

02:23:03.050 --> 02:23:05.130
a hunting trip or if they've
gone on a trip for a long time,

02:23:05.130 --> 02:23:07.860
they come back and they see their partner,

02:23:07.860 --> 02:23:10.130
and it's like a new, not
quite like a new relationship,

02:23:10.130 --> 02:23:11.970
but almost like a new relationship.

02:23:11.970 --> 02:23:13.650
And they have that excitement again.

02:23:13.650 --> 02:23:16.440
And purposely building that
into every relationship

02:23:16.440 --> 02:23:18.190
can help significantly,

02:23:18.190 --> 02:23:21.770
especially if you choose to
have a child or get pregnant

02:23:21.770 --> 02:23:23.080
or be breastfeeding,

02:23:23.080 --> 02:23:26.120
because you just plan ahead
for both of your prolactins

02:23:26.120 --> 02:23:28.830
to be high and both of
your dopamines to be low.

02:23:28.830 --> 02:23:31.951
And both of your testosterones to be low.

02:23:31.951 --> 02:23:36.680
So there's a lot of
planning that you can do.

02:23:36.680 --> 02:23:41.680
Essentially every relationship
goes through a crisis.

02:23:41.740 --> 02:23:46.580
And that crisis is personal
between the two of you.

02:23:46.580 --> 02:23:49.440
And you can plan ahead and

02:23:49.440 --> 02:23:52.670
figure out a way, maybe
it's not supplementation.

02:23:52.670 --> 02:23:55.660
Maybe it's not even the
amount of time you spend away

02:23:55.660 --> 02:23:56.870
from each other.

02:23:56.870 --> 02:24:00.400
But plan ahead to have good times

02:24:00.400 --> 02:24:02.610
if you know you're about
to go into a crisis.

02:24:02.610 --> 02:24:04.590
- Got it, and so it sounds like time apart

02:24:04.590 --> 02:24:05.423
and time together,

02:24:05.423 --> 02:24:07.470
which is actually built
into a number of cultures

02:24:07.470 --> 02:24:08.910
where men and women

02:24:08.910 --> 02:24:11.390
will purposefully avoid each
other for some period of time,

02:24:11.390 --> 02:24:13.630
avoid physical touch
and maybe in proximity,

02:24:13.630 --> 02:24:14.660
and then will reconvene,

02:24:14.660 --> 02:24:18.310
and yet those are very stable
relationships over time often.

02:24:18.310 --> 02:24:21.010
Is the inverse also true?

02:24:21.010 --> 02:24:22.010
For instance, for people that are

02:24:22.010 --> 02:24:24.160
in long distance relationships,

02:24:24.160 --> 02:24:25.680
where they're only seeing each other three

02:24:25.680 --> 02:24:27.630
or four days a week or two days a week,

02:24:28.870 --> 02:24:32.080
does this explain the fact that
some of those relationships

02:24:32.080 --> 02:24:33.650
can go on for a very long period of time

02:24:33.650 --> 02:24:36.220
without ever actually entering the,

02:24:36.220 --> 02:24:38.040
let's call it the hyper-prolactin phase

02:24:38.040 --> 02:24:40.950
of actually moving in together
and et cetera, et cetera.

02:24:40.950 --> 02:24:42.130
Like in other words,

02:24:42.130 --> 02:24:45.990
is that a way in which people are spiking

02:24:45.990 --> 02:24:48.340
and troughing dopamine
that keeps them attached?

02:24:48.340 --> 02:24:49.623
This kind of elusive,

02:24:51.210 --> 02:24:52.510
this sort of, what is it called?

02:24:52.510 --> 02:24:54.320
I think it's called like a cat string.

02:24:54.320 --> 02:24:56.590
Like if you play with a cat
and you move the string away,

02:24:56.590 --> 02:24:57.423
they'll keep reaching,

02:24:57.423 --> 02:24:58.740
but you throw the string on
the ground, they're like,

02:24:58.740 --> 02:25:00.560
they're totally uninterested in it.

02:25:00.560 --> 02:25:01.393
Is that what's going on?

02:25:01.393 --> 02:25:03.150
'Cause that's a dopaminergic phenomenon,

02:25:03.150 --> 02:25:04.490
the cat string example.

02:25:04.490 --> 02:25:06.150
We know this experimentally.

02:25:06.150 --> 02:25:09.440
- In those cases, the relationship
hasn't really progressed,

02:25:09.440 --> 02:25:10.940
in many of those cases,

02:25:10.940 --> 02:25:13.450
past the dopamine spike,

02:25:13.450 --> 02:25:15.830
the fun initial stage, honeymoon stage,

02:25:15.830 --> 02:25:17.080
whatever you want to call it.

02:25:17.080 --> 02:25:19.360
So it's almost kind of like a roommate.

02:25:19.360 --> 02:25:20.590
If you're looking for a roommate,

02:25:20.590 --> 02:25:23.360
if it was for college or
after college or whatever,

02:25:23.360 --> 02:25:26.310
you can fill out forms and
look for common interests,

02:25:26.310 --> 02:25:28.890
but until you're actually together

02:25:28.890 --> 02:25:31.330
a significant proportion of the time,

02:25:31.330 --> 02:25:32.381
you're not really going to know

02:25:32.381 --> 02:25:34.460
if you're going to be compatible or not.

02:25:34.460 --> 02:25:39.430
- And is there evidence
that the appearance

02:25:39.430 --> 02:25:41.120
of an infant changes,

02:25:41.120 --> 02:25:43.400
obviously there're going
to be hormonal shifts.

02:25:43.400 --> 02:25:47.470
We know actually that for
in both women and in men,

02:25:47.470 --> 02:25:48.870
there's a prolactin increase

02:25:50.470 --> 02:25:52.313
when couples are expecting a child.

02:25:53.780 --> 02:25:55.270
It's almost like a brooding phenomenon.

02:25:55.270 --> 02:25:58.400
You see this in birds where
it's actually called brooding

02:25:58.400 --> 02:26:00.360
and it's caused by prolactin increase,

02:26:00.360 --> 02:26:03.190
but it turns out this
also occurs in humans.

02:26:03.190 --> 02:26:05.250
And some people would argue this causes

02:26:05.250 --> 02:26:06.970
the dad bod phenomenon,
'cause it actually,

02:26:06.970 --> 02:26:08.700
prolactin is involved in
laying down a body fat,

02:26:08.700 --> 02:26:10.470
preparing for sleepless nights.

02:26:10.470 --> 02:26:13.630
And presumably that spike
in prolactin is there also

02:26:13.630 --> 02:26:15.100
to suppress sexual activity,

02:26:15.100 --> 02:26:17.480
because there are periods
of time immediately

02:26:17.480 --> 02:26:22.200
near childbirth where sexual
activity is not advantageous.

02:26:22.200 --> 02:26:25.870
- Yeah, you see a prolactin
spike right after breastfeeding.

02:26:25.870 --> 02:26:28.670
So if you think about it,
often when you have an infant,

02:26:30.460 --> 02:26:33.140
you'll breastfeed, put the infant to bed,

02:26:33.140 --> 02:26:35.050
and then immediately go
to bed with your partner,

02:26:35.050 --> 02:26:36.780
which is not particularly conducive.

02:26:36.780 --> 02:26:40.010
It's almost like trying to
have intercourse back to back.

02:26:40.010 --> 02:26:41.380
And it's very difficult.

02:26:41.380 --> 02:26:43.240
- Because of in the prolactin sense?

02:26:43.240 --> 02:26:44.073
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

02:26:44.073 --> 02:26:46.210
- Low dopamine, high prolactin.

02:26:46.210 --> 02:26:48.860
Oxytocin is also increased significantly

02:26:48.860 --> 02:26:51.380
to help with milk let-down as well.

02:26:51.380 --> 02:26:54.390
So yeah, as far as brooding,

02:26:54.390 --> 02:26:58.750
there's definitely a human
equivalent of brooding.

02:26:58.750 --> 02:27:03.290
Some humans call it nesting
instinct, which is both helpful,

02:27:03.290 --> 02:27:07.450
but it's not necessarily a
bad change in a relationship.

02:27:07.450 --> 02:27:09.030
It's just a change.

02:27:09.030 --> 02:27:11.240
And as long as you know that it's coming,

02:27:11.240 --> 02:27:12.210
you're going to do better with it.

02:27:12.210 --> 02:27:14.270
Just like any medication.

02:27:14.270 --> 02:27:16.270
If you are aware of the side effect

02:27:16.270 --> 02:27:17.600
and that it might happen,

02:27:17.600 --> 02:27:20.940
then when it happens, it's not only

02:27:22.210 --> 02:27:25.300
less severe, it also happens less often.

02:27:25.300 --> 02:27:26.563
- Very interesting.
- If you tell the patient.

02:27:26.563 --> 02:27:28.320
- Well as a neuroscientist,

02:27:28.320 --> 02:27:30.360
I come from the framework that

02:27:30.360 --> 02:27:32.720
of course hormones impact
perception and behavior,

02:27:32.720 --> 02:27:35.070
but perception and behavior
also impact hormones.

02:27:35.070 --> 02:27:36.010
I find this fascinating.

02:27:36.010 --> 02:27:37.930
I also really like the example you gave

02:27:37.930 --> 02:27:40.010
of people taking time apart,

02:27:40.010 --> 02:27:43.810
but also these affiliative bonds
that are non-romantic bonds

02:27:43.810 --> 02:27:44.950
can serve as kind of

02:27:44.950 --> 02:27:49.610
a reservoir to replenish dopamine that

02:27:49.610 --> 02:27:51.980
is then released upon
experience going back

02:27:51.980 --> 02:27:54.853
to one's partner or some sort
of regular feature of home.

02:27:56.420 --> 02:27:58.290
Very interesting, and of
course this should exist

02:27:58.290 --> 02:27:59.123
on both sides.

02:27:59.123 --> 02:28:02.560
I'm guessing that from both
the male side and female side,

02:28:02.560 --> 02:28:05.240
there's an interest in kind
of separation and reunion

02:28:05.240 --> 02:28:06.270
as the theme.

02:28:06.270 --> 02:28:07.870
And I guess the frequency will vary for

02:28:07.870 --> 02:28:10.400
different couples and
different situations.

02:28:10.400 --> 02:28:12.990
- Yeah, and I don't want to
make it seem like prolactin

02:28:12.990 --> 02:28:15.120
is all bad, so prolactin does help

02:28:15.120 --> 02:28:16.520
with the nesting instinct.

02:28:16.520 --> 02:28:19.130
It helps with breastfeeding as well.

02:28:19.130 --> 02:28:22.540
A lot of women are diagnosed
with luteal phase defects,

02:28:22.540 --> 02:28:25.110
which is basically the
phase after ovulation,

02:28:25.110 --> 02:28:26.990
but before a period or giving birth.

02:28:26.990 --> 02:28:29.850
A pregnancy's kind of a
prolonged luteal phase.

02:28:29.850 --> 02:28:33.060
And a lot of them will go
on progesterone for this.

02:28:33.060 --> 02:28:36.670
Progesterone can also decrease
prolactin and prolactin

02:28:36.670 --> 02:28:40.320
is also helpful for the
maturity of lungs in infants.

02:28:40.320 --> 02:28:43.380
So it helps the sphingomyelin
to lecithin ratio.

02:28:43.380 --> 02:28:46.710
So if your prolactin's
too low through pregnancy,

02:28:46.710 --> 02:28:49.350
it spikes up very high during pregnancy,

02:28:49.350 --> 02:28:51.380
then it can lead to increased risk

02:28:51.380 --> 02:28:54.250
of respiratory distress of the newborn.

02:28:54.250 --> 02:28:55.240
- Really interesting. Yeah.

02:28:55.240 --> 02:28:56.670
So we certainly don't
want to paint a picture

02:28:56.670 --> 02:28:59.953
where prolactin is the
bad hormone to avoid.

02:29:00.800 --> 02:29:04.700
Without proactive, none of
us would be here of course.

02:29:04.700 --> 02:29:05.950
It's so vital.

02:29:05.950 --> 02:29:08.230
I realized that earlier I raised
the question about whether

02:29:08.230 --> 02:29:11.900
or not cold exposure could
modify hormone output,

02:29:11.900 --> 02:29:14.840
in particular whether or
not ice baths or ice applied

02:29:14.840 --> 02:29:18.050
to specific tissues of the
body, as people are doing,

02:29:18.050 --> 02:29:19.530
one way or the other,

02:29:19.530 --> 02:29:23.860
can change testosterone
levels, estrogen levels.

02:29:23.860 --> 02:29:26.360
In other words, does taking
ice baths and cold showers

02:29:26.360 --> 02:29:28.800
increase testosterone and/or estrogen?

02:29:28.800 --> 02:29:32.580
- Yeah, so taking a ice
bath or a cold shower

02:29:32.580 --> 02:29:34.430
or cold exposure in general,

02:29:34.430 --> 02:29:36.780
it's not going to correct
a vitamin D deficiency

02:29:36.780 --> 02:29:38.450
or a metabolic syndrome.

02:29:38.450 --> 02:29:40.770
So there's a lot of things
that it will not correct

02:29:40.770 --> 02:29:44.720
that are causes of hypogonadism
or low testosterone,

02:29:44.720 --> 02:29:47.110
but it will help acutely,

02:29:47.110 --> 02:29:50.140
specifically the application of cold

02:29:50.140 --> 02:29:52.570
to testes that are too warm.

02:29:52.570 --> 02:29:56.100
So if you have a varicocele
or if you have a little bit

02:29:56.100 --> 02:29:58.710
of a primary hypogonadism,

02:29:58.710 --> 02:30:02.780
which is where testosterone
is not released by the testes,

02:30:02.780 --> 02:30:06.710
but your LH and FSH signals
are sufficiently high,

02:30:06.710 --> 02:30:11.060
then you'll likely respond
to cold exposure better.

02:30:11.060 --> 02:30:13.270
And there's actually undergarments that

02:30:13.270 --> 02:30:15.830
are designed specifically
to help with fertility.

02:30:15.830 --> 02:30:17.030
And there's probably going
to be more and more of that

02:30:17.030 --> 02:30:18.130
in the future.

02:30:18.130 --> 02:30:20.280
You just need to be careful
not to get frost bite,

02:30:20.280 --> 02:30:23.670
because it's a particularly
bad spot to get frost bite.

02:30:23.670 --> 02:30:26.377
- Noted. Could you define varicocele?

02:30:26.377 --> 02:30:28.320
You've mentioned it a few times.

02:30:28.320 --> 02:30:30.430
That's a varicose vein?

02:30:30.430 --> 02:30:33.150
- Yeah, so it's essentially
a varicose vein.

02:30:33.150 --> 02:30:36.940
It brings warm blood and the venous flow

02:30:36.940 --> 02:30:39.440
or the flow back to the
heart is not as good.

02:30:39.440 --> 02:30:42.070
Just like in the legs, it
can happen in the scrotum.

02:30:42.070 --> 02:30:44.380
Usually about 20 to 25% of people

02:30:44.380 --> 02:30:46.470
have one grade of varicocele.

02:30:46.470 --> 02:30:49.170
There's grades one through
four, one through five.

02:30:49.170 --> 02:30:51.450
And most people just have a very mild one,

02:30:51.450 --> 02:30:53.810
usually on the left side
because the blood has

02:30:53.810 --> 02:30:56.660
to go through further to
get back to the heart.

02:30:56.660 --> 02:31:00.140
And it raises the
temperature of the testes.

02:31:00.140 --> 02:31:01.990
Temperature is the enemy of testes.

02:31:01.990 --> 02:31:04.640
So they like to be 5 to 10 degrees cooler

02:31:04.640 --> 02:31:06.000
than the rest of the body.

02:31:06.000 --> 02:31:09.180
- So are saunas particularly
bad for sperm production?

02:31:09.180 --> 02:31:10.790
- They can be, yeah.

02:31:10.790 --> 02:31:11.830
- When you say can be, I mean,

02:31:11.830 --> 02:31:13.930
how long could one safely be in the sauna,

02:31:13.930 --> 02:31:16.540
or would you want to go
back and forth between

02:31:16.540 --> 02:31:18.613
the cold and sauna?

02:31:20.350 --> 02:31:21.990
Are there any data?

02:31:21.990 --> 02:31:24.730
- If someone is having infertility,

02:31:24.730 --> 02:31:28.140
then I tell them to avoid
all saunas empirically.

02:31:28.140 --> 02:31:32.060
If someone has, if they're not infertile,

02:31:32.060 --> 02:31:35.470
but they have a low sperm count,
I also tell them to avoid.

02:31:35.470 --> 02:31:38.920
However, it's mostly warmed water

02:31:38.920 --> 02:31:42.830
that can raise the temperature
of the testes faster

02:31:42.830 --> 02:31:43.663
than the sauna.

02:31:43.663 --> 02:31:45.010
- So hot tubs and things of that sort?

02:31:45.010 --> 02:31:47.040
- Yeah, so hot tub and a jacuzzi.

02:31:47.040 --> 02:31:50.023
Those are enemies number
one and number two of sperm.

02:31:51.070 --> 02:31:54.220
- What about ice baths and
cold showers for women?

02:31:54.220 --> 02:31:57.570
Any evidence that it can
shift hormone output in women?

02:31:57.570 --> 02:31:58.720
- Yeah, it can.

02:31:58.720 --> 02:32:03.720
It increases the activity of
the beta adrenergic receptors,

02:32:05.390 --> 02:32:06.497
even in the central nervous system

02:32:06.497 --> 02:32:08.630
and the astrocytes as well.

02:32:08.630 --> 02:32:10.010
So it can do a few things.

02:32:10.010 --> 02:32:13.940
It can slightly decrease the

02:32:13.940 --> 02:32:15.110
drive for food,

02:32:15.110 --> 02:32:18.170
which astrocytes and beta
adrenergic receptors have,

02:32:18.170 --> 02:32:20.000
some medications that
are weight loss medicines

02:32:20.000 --> 02:32:21.523
also do similar things.

02:32:23.150 --> 02:32:26.900
But it can be beneficial in women too.

02:32:26.900 --> 02:32:29.550
- But no evidence that it
changes estrogen output

02:32:29.550 --> 02:32:30.983
in women, correct?

02:32:32.050 --> 02:32:34.000
- Not that I know of.
- No. Me either.

02:32:35.710 --> 02:32:38.970
Peptides, lot of discussion
these days about peptides.

02:32:38.970 --> 02:32:41.030
Peptides of course just
being strings of amino acids,

02:32:41.030 --> 02:32:43.100
as you mentioned the very small ones like

02:32:43.100 --> 02:32:45.050
two amino acids like L-carnitine

02:32:45.050 --> 02:32:46.660
all the way up to polypeptides,

02:32:46.660 --> 02:32:49.713
which just mean many amino acids.

02:32:50.890 --> 02:32:52.800
There's so many peptides that

02:32:52.800 --> 02:32:54.950
we should probably just do an
entire episode about peptides,

02:32:54.950 --> 02:32:56.880
but I think one of the reasons I'm hearing

02:32:56.880 --> 02:32:58.470
so much about peptides these days

02:32:58.470 --> 02:33:01.260
is that they are not called steroids.

02:33:01.260 --> 02:33:03.540
The name steroids I think

02:33:04.780 --> 02:33:07.580
has come to be associated
with anabolic steroids

02:33:07.580 --> 02:33:10.850
in the context of acne,

02:33:10.850 --> 02:33:12.120
testosterone rage, et cetera.

02:33:12.120 --> 02:33:13.910
But of course testoster, excuse me,

02:33:13.910 --> 02:33:16.420
estrogen is a steroid hormone, right?

02:33:16.420 --> 02:33:19.540
There are other steroid
hormones, as we both know.

02:33:19.540 --> 02:33:23.440
But peptides are gaining
increasing popularity.

02:33:23.440 --> 02:33:25.030
I am willing to go on record saying

02:33:25.030 --> 02:33:26.490
that you can be sure that many

02:33:26.490 --> 02:33:28.640
of the incredible
transformations that you see

02:33:28.640 --> 02:33:32.390
in Hollywood are the
consequence of peptide use.

02:33:32.390 --> 02:33:33.260
And I'd put

02:33:34.488 --> 02:33:37.560
my name behind that because
I'm well aware of people

02:33:37.560 --> 02:33:40.650
that use these to prepare for
roles, but athletes use them.

02:33:40.650 --> 02:33:42.460
And then everyday people
are using them too.

02:33:42.460 --> 02:33:46.780
For instance sermorelin,
tesamorelin, ipamorelin,

02:33:46.780 --> 02:33:50.240
to stimulate the release of growth hormone

02:33:50.240 --> 02:33:51.897
rather than taking growth hormone.

02:33:51.897 --> 02:33:56.470
BPC-157, which is essentially
a synthetic gastric juice

02:33:56.470 --> 02:33:59.160
that normally repairs the gut,

02:33:59.160 --> 02:34:01.110
being used to treat injuries.

02:34:01.110 --> 02:34:03.520
And there are other are ones as well.

02:34:03.520 --> 02:34:05.910
What can we say generally
about peptides? Are they safe?

02:34:05.910 --> 02:34:08.010
Are they not safe? What about sourcing?

02:34:08.010 --> 02:34:09.810
And are there any peptides
that you think could be

02:34:09.810 --> 02:34:12.820
of particular use for people?

02:34:12.820 --> 02:34:14.430
And we should probably
also touch on peptides

02:34:14.430 --> 02:34:17.390
that people shouldn't go anywhere
near with a 10-foot pole.

02:34:17.390 --> 02:34:20.570
- Yeah, definitely, so peptides
are very heterogeneous.

02:34:20.570 --> 02:34:24.140
There's very dangerous
ones and very safe ones.

02:34:24.140 --> 02:34:27.440
My favorite peptide is
the original peptide,

02:34:27.440 --> 02:34:28.800
which is insulin.

02:34:28.800 --> 02:34:32.070
So insulin is a peptide and

02:34:33.390 --> 02:34:34.960
less than 100 years ago,

02:34:34.960 --> 02:34:38.370
there was a scientist studying insulin.

02:34:38.370 --> 02:34:41.990
And at some point, they
saw that an animal had

02:34:41.990 --> 02:34:45.000
its diabetes cured by
insulin inject, cured,

02:34:45.000 --> 02:34:46.440
by insulin injection.

02:34:46.440 --> 02:34:47.680
Less than a year later,

02:34:47.680 --> 02:34:50.930
they were injecting insulin
into every type one diabetic,

02:34:50.930 --> 02:34:52.240
because it was saving their lives.

02:34:52.240 --> 02:34:54.670
- And yet insulin can kill you

02:34:54.670 --> 02:34:57.040
if you take it at the incorrect dose?

02:34:57.040 --> 02:35:00.250
- Yeah, so just like
insulin should be prescribed

02:35:00.250 --> 02:35:02.520
by a doctor, there is
over-the-counter insulin,

02:35:02.520 --> 02:35:04.170
ReliOn or NPH,

02:35:04.170 --> 02:35:08.010
but ideally your insulin is
prescribed by your doctor

02:35:08.010 --> 02:35:11.670
for your diabetes, as it's lifesaving.

02:35:11.670 --> 02:35:14.090
Peptides should be prescribed
by doctors as well.

02:35:14.090 --> 02:35:16.590
And there's several that are FDA approved.

02:35:16.590 --> 02:35:19.220
So you mentioned a lot of different ones.

02:35:19.220 --> 02:35:21.290
Let's start with tesamorelin.

02:35:21.290 --> 02:35:24.300
So tesamorelin was recently FDA approved

02:35:24.300 --> 02:35:26.800
for something called lipodystrophy.

02:35:26.800 --> 02:35:31.170
It happens where body fat is
displaced into abnormal areas,

02:35:31.170 --> 02:35:34.730
often as part of aids or
severe burns, things like that.

02:35:34.730 --> 02:35:37.380
And it helps redistribute
this body fat and give people

02:35:37.380 --> 02:35:39.130
their quality of life back.

02:35:39.130 --> 02:35:41.880
Tesamorelin is a GHRH,

02:35:41.880 --> 02:35:44.600
which I kind of loop into
the category of GHRPs,

02:35:44.600 --> 02:35:47.640
so growth hormone-releasing peptides.

02:35:47.640 --> 02:35:49.660
So it's only a couple
amino acids different

02:35:49.660 --> 02:35:53.810
from endogenously-produced
growth hormone-releasing hormone.

02:35:53.810 --> 02:35:57.480
So growth hormone itself
is also a peptide.

02:35:57.480 --> 02:36:01.150
It's a peptide hormone.
Not a steroid hormone.

02:36:01.150 --> 02:36:01.983
So you have

02:36:04.160 --> 02:36:07.570
different somatotrophs
which are very similar

02:36:07.570 --> 02:36:09.250
to growth hormone.

02:36:09.250 --> 02:36:11.790
Another fun fact is that HPL,

02:36:11.790 --> 02:36:13.870
which is human placental lactogen,

02:36:13.870 --> 02:36:15.450
we love acronyms, right?

02:36:15.450 --> 02:36:18.580
Human placental lactogen
is nearly identical

02:36:18.580 --> 02:36:19.623
to growth hormone.

02:36:21.120 --> 02:36:23.160
The growth hormone in pregnancy

02:36:23.160 --> 02:36:26.610
is not what causes the sugar
spike in gestational diabetes.

02:36:26.610 --> 02:36:29.100
It's the human placental lactogen.

02:36:29.100 --> 02:36:31.230
So if you look at twin pregnancies,

02:36:31.230 --> 02:36:33.380
if they have two placentas

02:36:33.380 --> 02:36:35.580
or more placental tissue making

02:36:35.580 --> 02:36:37.530
more human placental lactogen,

02:36:37.530 --> 02:36:42.320
the risk of gestational diabetes
is exponentially higher.

02:36:42.320 --> 02:36:46.940
So this HPL is only a
couple molecules different

02:36:46.940 --> 02:36:48.540
from growth hormone.

02:36:48.540 --> 02:36:51.837
It is interesting that
these different GHRHs

02:36:51.837 --> 02:36:52.980
and GHRPs actually

02:36:52.980 --> 02:36:55.370
have pretty different
mechanisms of action.

02:36:55.370 --> 02:36:58.420
Ghrelin is also a hormone that's released

02:36:58.420 --> 02:36:59.760
when you're hungry.

02:36:59.760 --> 02:37:01.410
This is probably one of the reasons

02:37:01.410 --> 02:37:04.380
why you have more growth
hormone release overnight.

02:37:04.380 --> 02:37:06.670
And there's a lot of peptides
that are very similar

02:37:06.670 --> 02:37:11.470
to ghrelin, so these peptides
are not bioidentical peptides,

02:37:11.470 --> 02:37:14.470
but they just have a couple
different amino acids changed.

02:37:14.470 --> 02:37:18.110
So they're almost identical
and they're probably going to

02:37:18.110 --> 02:37:20.980
be used in the future for
growth hormone deficiencies,

02:37:20.980 --> 02:37:23.020
including in kids, they've been studied.

02:37:23.020 --> 02:37:24.010
- So if somebody wants

02:37:24.010 --> 02:37:25.600
to increase their growth hormone output,

02:37:25.600 --> 02:37:29.600
in addition to not eating
within two hours of sleep,

02:37:29.600 --> 02:37:31.103
getting good, deep sleep,

02:37:32.170 --> 02:37:34.470
doing all the other
things in the six pillars

02:37:34.470 --> 02:37:35.410
that you mentioned earlier,

02:37:35.410 --> 02:37:37.480
especially resistance exercise

02:37:38.480 --> 02:37:40.183
at some point earlier in the day,

02:37:41.350 --> 02:37:43.870
what are the risks and benefits of taking

02:37:43.870 --> 02:37:46.410
a growth hormone-releasing hormone peptide

02:37:46.410 --> 02:37:50.123
like sermorelin prescribed
by a doctor, of course.

02:37:50.960 --> 02:37:53.410
What should one be concerned about?

02:37:53.410 --> 02:37:54.790
How long could one take these?

02:37:54.790 --> 02:37:57.270
I've even heard that they
can modify gene expression

02:37:57.270 --> 02:38:00.370
so that they really are
changing your hypothalamus

02:38:00.370 --> 02:38:02.810
in very long lasting ways.

02:38:02.810 --> 02:38:05.340
- Yeah, there's definitely a lot of risk,

02:38:05.340 --> 02:38:07.600
tumor growth and cancer.

02:38:07.600 --> 02:38:10.360
So you look at a type one diabetic,

02:38:10.360 --> 02:38:14.530
they have very high incidences
of various types of cancer.

02:38:14.530 --> 02:38:16.070
They have very high growth hormone,

02:38:16.070 --> 02:38:18.950
but low IGF-1 paradoxically.

02:38:18.950 --> 02:38:21.770
So they would likely give
you a similar cancer risk

02:38:21.770 --> 02:38:26.620
to a type one diabetic that
has very high growth hormone.

02:38:26.620 --> 02:38:29.490
However, the benefits of it,

02:38:29.490 --> 02:38:33.260
you think of lipolysis,
decreased body fat,

02:38:33.260 --> 02:38:34.930
increased lean body mass.

02:38:34.930 --> 02:38:36.830
A lot of those,

02:38:36.830 --> 02:38:40.310
you can use other things
to get those benefits.

02:38:40.310 --> 02:38:45.310
So then you don't need growth
hormone for those benefits.

02:38:45.370 --> 02:38:48.270
It just leaves cosmetic benefit

02:38:48.270 --> 02:38:51.180
to which you can usually
use topicals to get.

02:38:51.180 --> 02:38:52.820
Your hair and your skin and your nails,

02:38:52.820 --> 02:38:55.170
there's a lot of other
things that you can do

02:38:55.170 --> 02:38:57.030
other than growth hormone.

02:38:57.030 --> 02:39:01.530
So a lot of people just
don't need these GHRPs

02:39:01.530 --> 02:39:02.860
if they don't have lipodystrophy

02:39:02.860 --> 02:39:05.080
or if they don't have
growth hormone deficiency.

02:39:05.080 --> 02:39:09.030
There is other uses of them,
specifically in injuries.

02:39:09.030 --> 02:39:11.340
So I know that they've been studied,

02:39:11.340 --> 02:39:12.620
I'm not sure if it's in the military.

02:39:12.620 --> 02:39:16.060
We mentioned the woodpecker
or the contrecoup injury.

02:39:16.060 --> 02:39:16.923
So that obviously.
- The head jolting back

02:39:16.923 --> 02:39:19.020
and forth and the brain basically slamming

02:39:19.020 --> 02:39:20.320
up against the front of the skull.

02:39:20.320 --> 02:39:22.370
- So-
- Football, heading the ball

02:39:22.370 --> 02:39:25.410
in soccer, definitely people who use

02:39:25.410 --> 02:39:26.960
the 50 caliber in military,

02:39:26.960 --> 02:39:29.803
although that's a fairly small population.

02:39:31.340 --> 02:39:33.340
And I think anyone that's
hit their head hard

02:39:33.340 --> 02:39:34.250
more than once.

02:39:34.250 --> 02:39:38.350
- Yeah, we can talk
about BPC-157 for a bit,

02:39:38.350 --> 02:39:40.223
GHK-copper peptide for a bit.

02:39:41.420 --> 02:39:44.530
TB-500 or a thymosin beta-4 analog.

02:39:44.530 --> 02:39:48.050
And then we can also
talk about bremelanotide,

02:39:48.050 --> 02:39:49.760
which is melanotan III.

02:39:49.760 --> 02:39:52.150
They have melanotan I and II,

02:39:52.150 --> 02:39:54.040
and then they also have
melanotan III and IV.

02:39:54.040 --> 02:39:57.121
- Yeah, let's talk about
BPC-157 and melanotan,

02:39:57.121 --> 02:39:57.954
'cause I think those are the ones

02:39:57.954 --> 02:40:01.550
that most people are eyeing, so to speak.

02:40:01.550 --> 02:40:06.320
- Yeah, so BPC-157 is body
protective compound 157.

02:40:06.320 --> 02:40:09.850
It's identical or bio-identical

02:40:09.850 --> 02:40:13.080
to gastric protective compound 157

02:40:13.080 --> 02:40:14.870
that's produced in the stomach.

02:40:14.870 --> 02:40:19.870
So as you age, you get
atrophic gastritis very often.

02:40:20.240 --> 02:40:22.620
That's why you have less intrinsic factor,

02:40:22.620 --> 02:40:25.750
which is kind of another peptide
that binds to vitamin B12.

02:40:25.750 --> 02:40:28.990
That's why you can get
age-related B12 deficiencies.

02:40:28.990 --> 02:40:32.410
So that's one reason why
you have more colitis,

02:40:32.410 --> 02:40:34.030
more or diverticulitis as you age.

02:40:34.030 --> 02:40:36.430
You don't have that gastric
protective compound.

02:40:37.460 --> 02:40:41.600
It increases VEGF vascular
endothelial growth factor,

02:40:41.600 --> 02:40:45.360
which basically makes your
blood vessels grow more.

02:40:45.360 --> 02:40:49.520
So that's what causes your
body to form a blood vessel.

02:40:49.520 --> 02:40:53.010
So another medication known as Avastin.

02:40:53.010 --> 02:40:54.760
It's on the WHO's list

02:40:54.760 --> 02:40:57.670
of essential medications for cancer.

02:40:57.670 --> 02:41:01.000
So many different types of
cancer, including colon cancer,

02:41:01.000 --> 02:41:04.250
you treat it with Avastin,
which is a VEGF inhibitor.

02:41:04.250 --> 02:41:06.380
So if you have cancer
or a high cancer risk,

02:41:06.380 --> 02:41:08.680
you probably don't want
to be taking a medication

02:41:08.680 --> 02:41:11.300
that's the exact opposite
mechanism of action

02:41:11.300 --> 02:41:14.200
as your essential anti-cancer med.

02:41:14.200 --> 02:41:15.950
- In other words, if you have cancer,

02:41:15.950 --> 02:41:18.450
you're at risk of cancer, avoid BPC-157?

02:41:18.450 --> 02:41:20.980
- Correct, a lot of people prescribe it

02:41:20.980 --> 02:41:23.070
for six weeks and BPC-157,

02:41:23.070 --> 02:41:25.990
so bremelanotide, that is FDA approved

02:41:25.990 --> 02:41:29.494
for a hypoactive sexual disorder.

02:41:29.494 --> 02:41:32.440
Tesamorelin, that's also
approved for lipodystrophy.

02:41:32.440 --> 02:41:35.620
Interestingly another
one of the melanotans

02:41:35.620 --> 02:41:38.160
is also approved for lipodystrophy.

02:41:38.160 --> 02:41:41.840
And also deficiency in
the melanocortin receptor.

02:41:41.840 --> 02:41:43.780
So the receptor that receives

02:41:44.880 --> 02:41:47.300
the alpha-melanocyte-stimulating hormone,

02:41:47.300 --> 02:41:48.690
it's a very rare condition.

02:41:48.690 --> 02:41:52.560
It's also approved for that,
because if you don't take it,

02:41:52.560 --> 02:41:54.490
then you get obesity.

02:41:54.490 --> 02:41:58.060
But BPC-157 is not FDA approved,

02:41:58.060 --> 02:42:01.780
but it is essentially standard
of care at this point.

02:42:01.780 --> 02:42:03.420
I would say it's,

02:42:03.420 --> 02:42:04.840
if you're not counting insulin

02:42:04.840 --> 02:42:06.870
or growth hormone as peptides,

02:42:06.870 --> 02:42:10.350
it's one of the most commonly
used peptides and anecdotally,

02:42:10.350 --> 02:42:12.360
and in some clinical literature,

02:42:12.360 --> 02:42:15.690
it's fairly well tolerated
for short periods of time.

02:42:15.690 --> 02:42:17.960
I'm not in the camp that
everybody needs to do it two

02:42:17.960 --> 02:42:20.380
to three times a week or even daily

02:42:20.380 --> 02:42:22.760
for six weeks no matter what.

02:42:22.760 --> 02:42:26.900
The major benefit is when you're
going to take it early on,

02:42:26.900 --> 02:42:30.990
because it's going to allow
your body to increase blood flow

02:42:30.990 --> 02:42:34.100
to the injured area, and
the less blood flow it has,

02:42:34.100 --> 02:42:36.790
for example, cartilage, ligaments
have horrible blood flow,

02:42:36.790 --> 02:42:38.470
especially as people age,

02:42:38.470 --> 02:42:40.040
it's going to make a
significant difference.

02:42:40.040 --> 02:42:42.130
So I would wager that that Russian gymnast

02:42:42.130 --> 02:42:44.850
that achilles healed in one
month and completely from

02:42:44.850 --> 02:42:48.120
a full rupture was likely taking BPC-157

02:42:48.120 --> 02:42:49.250
or something very similar.

02:42:49.250 --> 02:42:51.240
- Yeah, I'm willing to
wager on that as well,

02:42:51.240 --> 02:42:52.773
a remarkable recovery.

02:42:53.630 --> 02:42:55.770
And so because it is prescription,

02:42:55.770 --> 02:42:57.180
there are non-prescription forms,

02:42:57.180 --> 02:42:59.120
my understanding of the
non-prescription forms

02:42:59.120 --> 02:43:02.170
and the danger of going
after non-prescription forms

02:43:02.170 --> 02:43:04.780
is that oftentimes they will contain

02:43:04.780 --> 02:43:08.010
what they claim they contain,
BPC-157 in this case,

02:43:08.010 --> 02:43:11.270
but they are not adequately
cleaning out the LPS,

02:43:11.270 --> 02:43:14.050
the lipopolysaccharide which
can cause inflammation.

02:43:14.050 --> 02:43:14.950
In fact, in the laboratory,

02:43:14.950 --> 02:43:18.470
we use LPS to deliberately
induce fever and inflammation

02:43:18.470 --> 02:43:20.670
to study systemic inflammation.

02:43:20.670 --> 02:43:22.280
So this is a warning to people.

02:43:22.280 --> 02:43:23.390
If you're interested in peptides,

02:43:23.390 --> 02:43:25.060
you absolutely need to
work with a physician,

02:43:25.060 --> 02:43:26.340
in my opinion.
- Yeah.

02:43:26.340 --> 02:43:28.740
- Get it from a really
good compounding pharmacy

02:43:29.915 --> 02:43:31.690
that cleans out the LPS.

02:43:31.690 --> 02:43:34.690
Because if you're buying
it through a source that

02:43:34.690 --> 02:43:36.090
a lot of people, I don't
want to name sources,

02:43:36.090 --> 02:43:37.700
but there are these common
sources on the internet

02:43:37.700 --> 02:43:38.540
that everyone knows about.

02:43:38.540 --> 02:43:39.530
They're buying these sources,

02:43:39.530 --> 02:43:41.350
they'll ship it to anyone essentially.

02:43:41.350 --> 02:43:45.690
But then the LPS is really
causing inflammation

02:43:45.690 --> 02:43:48.120
and many people experience
a kind of mild fever

02:43:48.120 --> 02:43:50.530
or tingling from that when they
inject it and they're like,

02:43:50.530 --> 02:43:51.530
oh, I can feel it working.

02:43:51.530 --> 02:43:53.760
That's probably LPS action,

02:43:53.760 --> 02:43:55.960
which is not good for the brain.

02:43:55.960 --> 02:43:58.930
I don't know about on
other peripheral tissues.

02:43:58.930 --> 02:44:01.010
I haven't heard of people
dropping dead from this stuff yet,

02:44:01.010 --> 02:44:03.020
but I certainly wouldn't
want to be ingesting

02:44:03.020 --> 02:44:04.630
any LPs unnecessarily.

02:44:04.630 --> 02:44:07.370
So would you agree that you
should work with a doctor?

02:44:07.370 --> 02:44:08.890
After all you are a doctor.
- Yeah.

02:44:08.890 --> 02:44:10.800
Definitely talk to your doctor about this

02:44:10.800 --> 02:44:12.950
and talk to them about
dosing regimen as well.

02:44:12.950 --> 02:44:15.100
So if they have you
doing it for six weeks,

02:44:15.100 --> 02:44:17.260
ask 'em why am I doing it for six weeks?

02:44:17.260 --> 02:44:19.950
Why not two weeks or why not
as soon as I feel better?

02:44:19.950 --> 02:44:21.360
Can I just stop it?

02:44:21.360 --> 02:44:22.960
Yeah, there's a lot of
good questions like that

02:44:22.960 --> 02:44:24.310
that you should ask your doctor.

02:44:24.310 --> 02:44:26.090
And if somebody's trying to prescribe you

02:44:26.090 --> 02:44:28.980
a bunch of different things, then see,

02:44:28.980 --> 02:44:30.600
is this what they prescribe everybody

02:44:30.600 --> 02:44:32.610
or is this individualized for me?

02:44:32.610 --> 02:44:35.040
There are peptides like GHK-copper peptide

02:44:35.040 --> 02:44:37.180
which is produced
endogenously in the liver more

02:44:37.180 --> 02:44:38.710
at younger ages.

02:44:38.710 --> 02:44:40.430
That's why the liver can regenerate fully,

02:44:40.430 --> 02:44:43.180
is this, the GHK-copper peptide helps.

02:44:43.180 --> 02:44:44.490
And if you're copper deficient,

02:44:44.490 --> 02:44:45.720
which not a whole lot of people are,

02:44:45.720 --> 02:44:47.610
but a lot of people that
have had bariatric surgery

02:44:47.610 --> 02:44:49.250
are copper deficient,

02:44:49.250 --> 02:44:51.750
GHK-copper peptide can help significantly

02:44:51.750 --> 02:44:53.290
with your nervous system.

02:44:53.290 --> 02:44:54.580
And it's also synergistic.

02:44:54.580 --> 02:44:57.860
So any growth agonist
like thymosin beta-4 made

02:44:57.860 --> 02:45:00.130
in kids in the thymus, which shrinks.

02:45:00.130 --> 02:45:03.080
That's another reason why
kids heal really well.

02:45:03.080 --> 02:45:06.590
That and GHK is somewhat
synergistic with BPC,

02:45:06.590 --> 02:45:08.830
but if you don't need all
three, you don't want them.

02:45:08.830 --> 02:45:10.440
And if you don't need
it for more than a week,

02:45:10.440 --> 02:45:13.010
you don't want it for more than a week.

02:45:13.010 --> 02:45:14.450
- I really appreciate you saying that.

02:45:14.450 --> 02:45:16.980
I often say that sometimes
the best dose of something

02:45:16.980 --> 02:45:18.590
to take is zero.

02:45:18.590 --> 02:45:21.610
It's often the case that
the best dosage is zero.

02:45:21.610 --> 02:45:22.650
You mentioned melanotan.

02:45:22.650 --> 02:45:24.460
There are several kinds of melanotan.

02:45:24.460 --> 02:45:26.760
I find it a little bit
of a funny conversation,

02:45:26.760 --> 02:45:29.140
because I first learned about melanotan

02:45:29.140 --> 02:45:31.270
from reading about peptides

02:45:31.270 --> 02:45:33.050
and discovering that people were

02:45:33.050 --> 02:45:35.320
injecting melanotan to get tan,

02:45:35.320 --> 02:45:38.590
because it's in the
melanin synthesis pathway.

02:45:38.590 --> 02:45:41.390
They also discovered,
this isn't an individual.

02:45:41.390 --> 02:45:44.120
This is reading about this
in various manuscripts

02:45:44.120 --> 02:45:46.310
and peer-reviewed papers that

02:45:46.310 --> 02:45:47.910
it could cause things like priapism,

02:45:47.910 --> 02:45:49.620
like sustained erection,

02:45:49.620 --> 02:45:52.350
that might be the last one
that anyone would ever have

02:45:52.350 --> 02:45:55.093
because of damage to the vasculature.

02:45:56.090 --> 02:45:58.140
Also women taking melanotan

02:45:58.140 --> 02:46:00.840
as a way to get tan and lose body fat.

02:46:00.840 --> 02:46:02.550
So this sounds all very recreational.

02:46:02.550 --> 02:46:07.020
Are there any clinical usage of melanotan?

02:46:07.020 --> 02:46:08.470
So separate from the kind

02:46:08.470 --> 02:46:10.550
of extreme biohacking cosmetic world,

02:46:10.550 --> 02:46:13.640
which is really not the main
focus of this podcast ever,

02:46:13.640 --> 02:46:18.070
more in terms of health,
pursuing health optimization.

02:46:18.070 --> 02:46:21.490
- Yeah, there's actually three
FDA approved indications,

02:46:21.490 --> 02:46:22.323
believe it or not.

02:46:22.323 --> 02:46:23.330
Not many people know about this,

02:46:23.330 --> 02:46:26.830
but there's three well
accepted indications.

02:46:26.830 --> 02:46:29.520
One of them is the
hypoactive sexual disorder,

02:46:29.520 --> 02:46:31.950
and more in women,
that's for bremelanotide.

02:46:31.950 --> 02:46:32.873
- So-
- Those are women

02:46:32.873 --> 02:46:33.880
that have essentially

02:46:33.880 --> 02:46:35.460
no libido whatsoever?
- Yeah.

02:46:35.460 --> 02:46:37.690
- But other hormones are in check?

02:46:37.690 --> 02:46:42.360
Yeah, classically it's before menopause.

02:46:42.360 --> 02:46:45.700
So those hormonal issues
are not contributing.

02:46:45.700 --> 02:46:48.430
And when you give them this peptide,

02:46:48.430 --> 02:46:51.860
it's also known as PT-141,
it helps significantly.

02:46:51.860 --> 02:46:53.940
A lot of times you use it in nasal spray.

02:46:53.940 --> 02:46:55.530
It goes straight into the
central nervous system

02:46:55.530 --> 02:46:56.363
and acts centrally.

02:46:56.363 --> 02:46:57.196
You can also inject it,

02:46:57.196 --> 02:46:59.320
and you can also take it via troche.

02:46:59.320 --> 02:47:00.600
- Men and women take it?

02:47:00.600 --> 02:47:03.360
- Correct. It's approved for women.

02:47:03.360 --> 02:47:05.340
But it can also help men.

02:47:05.340 --> 02:47:07.380
And it's relatively safe.

02:47:07.380 --> 02:47:10.020
The only relative contraindication
that I tell people

02:47:10.020 --> 02:47:10.853
and a lot of people say, oh,

02:47:10.853 --> 02:47:12.750
there's no side effects that I know of.

02:47:12.750 --> 02:47:15.570
But if you have a family
history of melanoma

02:47:15.570 --> 02:47:18.380
or potentially have a melanoma
and don't know about it,

02:47:18.380 --> 02:47:20.770
that's why I'm a big advocate
of dermoscopy as well

02:47:20.770 --> 02:47:22.300
on regular skin checks,

02:47:22.300 --> 02:47:23.920
then theoretically it's going to increase

02:47:23.920 --> 02:47:27.140
that alpha-melanocyte-stimulating hormone,

02:47:27.140 --> 02:47:28.430
and it can grow that.

02:47:28.430 --> 02:47:31.340
So that's definitely not a good a thing.

02:47:31.340 --> 02:47:33.680
So be very careful about
longterm administration of it.

02:47:33.680 --> 02:47:35.890
It's also approved for lipodystrophy,

02:47:35.890 --> 02:47:39.310
which is the same exact
thing as tesamorelin,

02:47:39.310 --> 02:47:44.310
which I believe is also
known as Evista or Egrifta.

02:47:44.420 --> 02:47:47.750
And then it's also approved
for the rare genetic condition

02:47:47.750 --> 02:47:51.790
where your receptors or your
melanocytes don't proliferate

02:47:51.790 --> 02:47:53.920
as well, so you usually
have hypopigmentation.

02:47:53.920 --> 02:47:57.750
It's not true albinism,
but it's associated

02:47:57.750 --> 02:48:01.330
with morbid obesity and
very be poor outcomes

02:48:01.330 --> 02:48:04.160
from that in childhood, so
it's used in kids actually.

02:48:04.160 --> 02:48:08.120
- Interesting, well, peptides
are a fascinating landscape,

02:48:08.120 --> 02:48:12.700
but thank you for that deep
dive into several of them.

02:48:12.700 --> 02:48:15.220
We will probably return to you

02:48:15.220 --> 02:48:17.560
to talk about peptides
again in the near future,

02:48:17.560 --> 02:48:19.040
because I know there's a lot more there.

02:48:19.040 --> 02:48:20.140
And a lot of interest.

02:48:21.230 --> 02:48:23.460
I want to talk about the
sixth pillar, all right?

02:48:23.460 --> 02:48:24.620
So just to remind people,

02:48:24.620 --> 02:48:27.820
you said diet, exercise,

02:48:27.820 --> 02:48:30.030
where appropriate, caloric restriction,

02:48:30.030 --> 02:48:33.750
managing stress, sleep
and sunlight are critical

02:48:33.750 --> 02:48:36.370
for everyone at all ages to manage

02:48:36.370 --> 02:48:38.170
and optimize hormone health.

02:48:38.170 --> 02:48:39.360
Then you have the sixth category,

02:48:39.360 --> 02:48:42.610
which is a really intriguing
one, which is spirit.

02:48:42.610 --> 02:48:44.900
Which is kind of unusual
thing to hear coming

02:48:44.900 --> 02:48:46.210
from a medical doctor,

02:48:46.210 --> 02:48:49.770
except that I have many
colleagues and indeed our

02:48:50.860 --> 02:48:53.170
former director of the
National Institutes of Health,

02:48:53.170 --> 02:48:55.770
Francis Collins has talked
about this notion of spirit.

02:48:55.770 --> 02:48:57.330
We've talked about belief effects

02:48:57.330 --> 02:48:59.540
on this podcast before with Alia Crum,

02:48:59.540 --> 02:49:02.600
how one's understanding
of the things that they do

02:49:02.600 --> 02:49:05.800
and their world in general really creates

02:49:05.800 --> 02:49:08.440
an important effect on everything

02:49:08.440 --> 02:49:11.000
at the level of physiology,
not just psychology.

02:49:11.000 --> 02:49:12.530
So as a physician,

02:49:12.530 --> 02:49:15.600
how do you conceptualize
this spiritual aspect?

02:49:15.600 --> 02:49:17.160
And how do you talk to
patients about this,

02:49:17.160 --> 02:49:19.380
given that people walking into your clinic

02:49:19.380 --> 02:49:21.380
presumably have a bunch
of different religious

02:49:21.380 --> 02:49:22.740
and not a religious backgrounds.

02:49:22.740 --> 02:49:23.840
I'm sure some are atheists.

02:49:23.840 --> 02:49:25.970
Some are probably strong believers.

02:49:25.970 --> 02:49:28.090
How do you deal with that?

02:49:28.090 --> 02:49:30.520
And how should people think about this?

02:49:30.520 --> 02:49:34.830
- Yeah, I believe it is
surprisingly well received.

02:49:34.830 --> 02:49:37.660
You wouldn't think at first
glance that a patient really

02:49:37.660 --> 02:49:39.620
wants to talk about their spiritual health

02:49:39.620 --> 02:49:41.050
with their doctor,

02:49:41.050 --> 02:49:43.270
but the way I think about it
and the way that it really is

02:49:43.270 --> 02:49:44.670
is it's like a Venn diagram

02:49:44.670 --> 02:49:47.020
and you have a body and a mind and a soul.

02:49:47.020 --> 02:49:49.430
And you can't have one healthy
without the other healthy,

02:49:49.430 --> 02:49:52.490
even if your mental health is phenomenal,

02:49:52.490 --> 02:49:54.740
and even if your physical
health is phenomenal,

02:49:54.740 --> 02:49:57.250
the mental aspect of spirituality,

02:49:57.250 --> 02:49:59.410
if that piece is not there,

02:49:59.410 --> 02:50:03.930
then that's going to affect your
body physiologically as well.

02:50:03.930 --> 02:50:06.410
And Alia Crum's done some excellent work.

02:50:06.410 --> 02:50:09.690
There's also been a lot of
other studies regarding prayer.

02:50:09.690 --> 02:50:11.540
And I'm a Christian, I believe in God.

02:50:11.540 --> 02:50:15.310
And that gives me a lot of
that resilience and motivation.

02:50:15.310 --> 02:50:18.160
It gives me the cornerstone
or the groundwork,

02:50:18.160 --> 02:50:20.540
how I can interact with life.

02:50:20.540 --> 02:50:22.590
And regardless if someone's an atheist or

02:50:24.128 --> 02:50:27.150
regardless of what someone
believes as far as religion

02:50:27.150 --> 02:50:29.570
or the origin of the species,

02:50:29.570 --> 02:50:33.230
they can know that their
spirituality is going to have

02:50:33.230 --> 02:50:35.450
a profound effect on their mental

02:50:35.450 --> 02:50:37.610
and physical health as well.

02:50:37.610 --> 02:50:39.270
People like to compartmentalize it.

02:50:39.270 --> 02:50:42.250
So they like to talk to
their doctor only about

02:50:42.250 --> 02:50:44.280
the physical health 'cause
it's comfortable to do that.

02:50:44.280 --> 02:50:47.120
They only talk to their pastor or a mom or

02:50:48.110 --> 02:50:50.160
reiki healer for their spiritual health.

02:50:50.160 --> 02:50:52.040
And they just talk to their therapist

02:50:52.040 --> 02:50:55.080
or psychiatrist about their mental health.

02:50:55.080 --> 02:50:58.280
But you need to bring all
three of those things together.

02:50:58.280 --> 02:51:00.780
It's well known that
interdisciplinary clinics lead

02:51:00.780 --> 02:51:02.850
to improved patient outcomes

02:51:02.850 --> 02:51:04.720
and that's just disciplines
within medicine.

02:51:04.720 --> 02:51:07.500
So that's just doctors
that are specializing

02:51:07.500 --> 02:51:08.900
in this or this.

02:51:08.900 --> 02:51:10.610
So this takes a step back

02:51:11.780 --> 02:51:13.320
in the upper part of that tree

02:51:13.320 --> 02:51:16.220
before you've reached those
dichotomies or the split-offs.

02:51:17.138 --> 02:51:18.860
You have your body and
your mind and your soul,

02:51:18.860 --> 02:51:20.680
so your spiritual health
and your mental health

02:51:20.680 --> 02:51:21.930
and your physical health.

02:51:22.790 --> 02:51:26.850
So if you're in line in
all three of those things,

02:51:26.850 --> 02:51:29.180
that builds the cornerstone
for the rest of your health

02:51:29.180 --> 02:51:30.620
and the rest of your life.

02:51:30.620 --> 02:51:33.210
- So if someone comes into
your clinic and they say,

02:51:33.210 --> 02:51:35.150
they're feeling one way in their body,

02:51:35.150 --> 02:51:37.300
they're feeling one way
in their emotional life,

02:51:37.300 --> 02:51:39.650
you run their charts,
you get their blood work,

02:51:40.840 --> 02:51:44.513
and they're an atheist
or they're agnostic,

02:51:45.500 --> 02:51:48.780
what are some of the
sixth pillar practices

02:51:48.780 --> 02:51:51.500
that they can consider that are in keeping

02:51:51.500 --> 02:51:54.820
with their atheism or agnosticism?

02:51:54.820 --> 02:51:58.660
Because I have to assume that
people who are in participate

02:51:58.660 --> 02:52:02.020
or feel that they belong to
a particular religious sex

02:52:02.020 --> 02:52:05.740
will have particular prescriptives
from those religious sex

02:52:05.740 --> 02:52:08.870
that will direct them towards
particular types of prayer.

02:52:08.870 --> 02:52:12.380
But how would somebody who doesn't have

02:52:12.380 --> 02:52:15.133
a prescriptive coming to
them from some other source,

02:52:16.107 --> 02:52:17.700
what could they do or would they do?

02:52:17.700 --> 02:52:19.340
- Yeah, so I certainly don't force prayer

02:52:19.340 --> 02:52:21.300
on anybody or anything like that.

02:52:21.300 --> 02:52:25.780
But it's my belief that being,
especially being an agnostic,

02:52:25.780 --> 02:52:29.560
it's almost the hardest thing,
because if you're an atheist,

02:52:29.560 --> 02:52:30.620
then you have some groundwork

02:52:30.620 --> 02:52:32.460
and you have some spirituality,

02:52:32.460 --> 02:52:36.780
even if it has to do with the
human spirits' interaction

02:52:36.780 --> 02:52:38.000
with the environment,

02:52:38.000 --> 02:52:40.210
things that can't be
physically explained well,

02:52:40.210 --> 02:52:42.650
phenomenon like the work
that Alia Crum does.

02:52:42.650 --> 02:52:45.770
But if you're agnostic, you're
still trying to find that.

02:52:45.770 --> 02:52:49.550
So I hope that everybody does
find what they truly believe

02:52:49.550 --> 02:52:52.750
in as far as their own spirituality.

02:52:52.750 --> 02:52:55.973
But yeah, that's a personal journey.

02:52:56.920 --> 02:52:58.450
From a physician's standpoint,

02:52:58.450 --> 02:52:59.900
and even if I'm friends with them as well

02:52:59.900 --> 02:53:01.030
from a friend's standpoint,

02:53:01.030 --> 02:53:04.710
I don't like to push anybody
in any specific direction.

02:53:04.710 --> 02:53:07.150
So I don't think that
everybody should believe

02:53:07.150 --> 02:53:08.370
what I believe.

02:53:08.370 --> 02:53:11.650
And I don't feel like there
should be any pressure

02:53:11.650 --> 02:53:14.380
for them to believe something different.

02:53:14.380 --> 02:53:15.930
So I think that there can

02:53:15.930 --> 02:53:18.390
be excellent physician-patient rapport,

02:53:18.390 --> 02:53:22.290
regardless of what we believe
and what our backgrounds are.

02:53:22.290 --> 02:53:24.970
- Yeah. That's wonderful to hear.

02:53:24.970 --> 02:53:27.300
I can say without revealing any names

02:53:27.300 --> 02:53:29.670
that I have close colleagues that,

02:53:29.670 --> 02:53:32.020
in every bin of this spectrum,

02:53:32.020 --> 02:53:33.870
like hardcore atheists,

02:53:33.870 --> 02:53:36.510
hardcore religious in different domains,

02:53:36.510 --> 02:53:39.400
different religions, I don't know,

02:53:39.400 --> 02:53:41.490
I don't know if I know many agnostic,

02:53:41.490 --> 02:53:44.360
as to whether or not I know
any agnostics, I should say.

02:53:44.360 --> 02:53:46.310
It's not something that
people commonly discuss,

02:53:46.310 --> 02:53:48.630
but in the context of
science and medicine,

02:53:48.630 --> 02:53:50.790
but it's starting to happen more and more.

02:53:50.790 --> 02:53:52.740
And certainly this issue of spirituality

02:53:52.740 --> 02:53:55.080
is one of the areas in
which neuroscience is asking

02:53:55.080 --> 02:53:55.913
